{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/aeromechanical-systems#top", "content": "Technology Category\nTechnology Development Task\nLab\nBearings\nHigh speed / High precision bearings for Aircraft Mounted Accessory Drive (AMAD) and Aircraft Mounted Accessory Gear Box (AMAGB)\nCVRDE\nHigh speed / High precision bearings for Small Turbo Fan Engine\nCVRDE\nGear Box\nAircraft Mounted Accessory Drive (AMAD) for Combat Aircraft\nCVRDE\nAircraft Mounted Accessory Gear Box (AMAGB) for Combat Aircraft\nCVRDE\nGenerator\nAirborne Electric Power Generator\nCVRDE\nHydraulic and Lube filters\nHydraulic and Lube Filters for Combat Aircrafts\nCVRDE\nLube filters for Aero Engine\nCVRDE\nLanding Gear\nRetractable landing gear system for Unmanned Aerial Vehicle\nCVRDE\nPower Take Off (PTO) shaft\nPower Take Off (PTO) shaft for Combat Aircraft\nCVRDE"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/aeronautics-research-development/about-us#top", "content": "Vision\nMake India technologically strong by establishing world class cutting edge aeronautical science and technology base to provide our Defence, Space and Civil Aviation sectors a decisive edge by equipping them with internationally competitive systems and solutions.\nMission\nTo encourage and fund basic and applied research in pertinent scientific disciplines directly relevant to ouraeronautical systems needed for future by enabling and supporting emerging talents,particularly in academic and research institutions to create and evolve a potential knowledge-base system applicable to future aeronautics needs of the country.\nCharter\nTo formulate research, design and development programmes in aeronautics and allied sciences, keeping in view future needs of the country specifically with respect to aircraft, helicopter, missiles and all other airborne vehicles.\nTo implement such programmes through appropriate institutions and individuals by sponsoring research, design and development projects, creating/ improving infrastructure facilities deemed necessary,while ensuring that they are suitably monitored.\nTo promote in all possible ways such educational and training programmes as may be considered necessary for ensuring that adequate manpower of requisite quality becomes available to various aeronautical organisations in the country.\nTo promote all relevant R&D activities in the country through appropriate scientific meetings, provisions of support for participation of Indian and foreign scientists in such meetings, conduct of relevant competitions as well as other training and visiting programmes within India and abroad as may fall within the scope of the programmes mentioned at sub para (a) above.\nDissemination of appropriate technical information through journals and documents, encouragement of individual and collective efforts and nurturing of young talent by institutionswith suitable awards, scholarships etc. Organisation of necessary centralized services related documentation, software, data-link etc. and in all such other ways that the Board may determine from time to time."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/aeronautics-research-development/board-constitution", "content": "AR&DB Board Members\nDRDO\nSr. No.\nDesignation\n1\nChairman DRDO, Ministry of Defence\nChairman\n2\nSecretary, Defence\nMember\n3\nSecretary, Defence Production\nMember\n4\nChairman, ISRO\nMember\n5\nDG R&D (Aeronautical Systems)\nMember\n6\nDeputy Chief of Air Staff\nMember\n7\nDirector General (Technology Management)\nMember\n8\nAddl. FA (R&D) & JS\nMember\n9\nProgramme Director, ADA\nMember\n10\nDirector, DRDL/RCI/ASL\nMember\n11\nDirector ADE\nMember\n12\nDirector, GTRE\nMember\n13\nDirector, NAL\nMember\n14\nDirector, VSSC\nMember\n15\nPresident, Aeronautical Society of India\nMember\n16\nDirector (D& D) Hindustan Aeronautics Ltd., Bangalore\nMember\n17\nSecretary, AR&DB\nMember Secretary\nSTEERING COMMITTEE OF AR&DB\nThe board is assisted by a Steering Committee in Technology forecasting, monitoring/review of large value/multi-disciplinary projects, and supports planning/setting up of Centers of Excellence.\nThe Steering Committee also assists the Aeronautics R&D Board in the formulation of plans and programmes of relevance to the needs of the country in the areas of Aeronautics & Missiles.\nSTEERING COMMITTEE MEMBERS\nDRDO\nSr. No.\nDesignation\n1\nDr Vikas Kumar, DS & Former Director, DMRL, Hyderabad\nChairman\n2\nDirector General (Aeronautical Systems)\nCo-Chairperson\n3\nDirector General (Technology Management)\nCo-Chairman\n4\nDirector, NAL, Bangalore\nMember\n5\nDirector, GTRE, Bangalore\nMember\n6\nDirector, DRDL, Hyderabad\nMember\n7\nDirector, ADE, Bangalore\nMember\n8\nDirector, Air Staff Requirement, New Delhi\nMember\n9\nGeneral Manager (Design/ARDC), HAL, Bangalore\nMember\n10\nDirector, DMRL, Hyderabad\nMember\n11\nDirector General, Civil Aviation, R&D Centre, New Delhi\nMember\n12\nDirector, Directorate of Special Project, ISRO Hqrs., Deptt. of Space, Antariksh Bhawan, Bangalore\nMember\n13\nSecretary, AR&DB, DRDO HQ Annexe, Old LASTEC Building, 4th Floor, Room No. 411, Metcalfe House, Civil Lines, Delhi-110054\nMember Secretary\nSpecialists Panel of AR&DB\nAR&DB operates through a number of specialist Panels. The Panels meet periodically to review and recommend new proposals and monitor the ongoing projects. In addition, these Panels are also responsible to expand the aeronautics research base in the country by way of motivating and nurturing young scientists and R&D institutions to take up activities in the specialist areas. Presently, there are Seven Specialist Panels to cover the different disciplines, viz.,\nAerodynamics Panel\nAerospace Resources Panel\nMaterials & Manufacturing Panel\nPropulsion Panel\nStructures Panel\nSystems/ Systems Engineering Panel\nUnmanned Aero Systems Panel"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/aeronautics-research-development/contact-us", "content": "Contact Us\nCLUSTER/ DIRECTORATE NAME\nWEB COORDINATOR NAME\nDESIGNATION\nOFFICIAL EMAIL ADDRESS\nCONTACT NUMBER (LANDLINE)\nAeronautics Research & Development Board (AR&DB) DRDO Headquarters Annexe, 4th Floor, Room No. 411, Old LASTEC Building, Metcalfe House, Civil Lines, Delhi-110054\nGp Capt Lalit Kumar Khulbe\nAdditional Director\nlalit[dot]khulbe[at]gov[dot]in\nTele .: 011-23902743\nFax No.: 011-23902794"},
