{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/aeronautics-research-development/forthcoming-events", "content": "AR&DB Meetings / Workshops / Seminars held during the Financial Year 2025-26\n<\nSr. No.\nMeeting\nDate & Venue\n1.\nAerospace Resources Panel\n(i) Aerospace Resources Panel meeting- 1st May 2025 (through video conferencing).\n(ii) Expert Committee meeting under Aerospace Resources Panel on 6th May 2025 at IIT, Delhi\n2.\nMaterials & Manufacturing Panel\n(i) Materials & Manufacturing Panel meeting- 4th April 2025at IIT, Indore.\n3.\nUnmanned Aero System\n(i) Unmanned Aero Systems Panel meeting- 24th April 2025, AR&DB Sectt., DRDO Headquarters  Annexe, Metcalfe House, Delhi (through VC)\nAR&DB Meetings / Workshops / Seminars held during the Financial Year 2024-25\nSr. No.\nMeeting\nDate & Venue\n1.\nSteering Committee of AR&DB\n(i) AR&DB Steering Committee meeting- 30th April 2024 at DRDO Hqrs., DRDO Bhawan, New Delhi\n(ii) AR&DB Steering Committee meeting-26th November 2024 at DRDO Headquarters, DRDO Bhawan, New Delhi\n2.\nAerodynamics Panel\n(i) Aerodynamics Panel meeting - 22nd July 2024 at DRDL Hyderabad\n(ii) Seminar on 'Advances in Aerodynamics Design of Aerospace Vehicles; Co-hosted by Aerodynamics panel and SVNIT on 16th Dec 2024 at SVNIT, Surat and Panel Meeting on 16th-17th Dec 2024 at SVNIT, Surat.\n(iii) Seminar on 'Recent Development in Aerospace Applications' on 24th February 2025 co-hosted by Aerodynamics panel and SRM Institute of S&T, Kattankulathu and Panel meeting on 25th Feb 2025 at SRM Institute of Science and Technology, Kattankulathu.\n3.\nAerospace Resources Panel\n(i) Aerospace Resource Panel  meeting - 14th June 2024, IIT, Bombay\n(ii) Seminar on 'Advances in Aerospace Applications' an outreach programme co-hosted by Aerospace Resources panel and IIT Dharwad - 23rd October 2024 at IIT Dharwad.\n(iii) Aerospace Resoures Panel meeting- 8th January 2025 at IIT, Bombay. Workshop on 'IPR issues in Aeronautics and high technologies' co hosed by IIT Bombay and Aerospace Resources Panel on 9th January 2025 at IIT Bombay.\n(iv) Expert Committee meeting under Aerospace Resources Panel on 28th February 2025 at IIT, Kharagpur.\n4.\nMaterials & Manufacturing Panel\n(i) Materials & Manufacturing Panel meeting- 17th - 18th May 2024 at IIT, Guwahati.\n(ii) Materials & Manufacturing Panel meeting- 5th July 2024 at IIT Indore.\n(iii) Materials & Manufacturing Panel meeting- 12th- 13th September 2024 at IIT Jodhpur.\n(iv) Materials & Manufacturing Panel meeting- 21st October 2024 at IIT, Indore (Through VC).\n(v) Materials & Manufacturing Panel meeting- 17th-19th November 2024 at IIT, Indore.\nvi) Materials & manufacturing Panel meeting - 11th-12th December 2024 at NIT, Calicut.\nGTMAP\n(i) GTMAP PARC (Materials in Small Volumes) meeting- 28\nth\nJune 2024\nat DMRL, Hyderabad.\n(ii) GTMAP PARC (Materials in Bulk) meeting-21st August 2024, IIT, Hyderabad\n(iii)\nGTMAP PARC (Materials in Small Volumes) meeting- 16\nth\nJanuary 2025\n, DMRL, Hyderabad.\n5.\nPropulsion Panel\n(i) Propulsion panel meeting - 12-13th June 2024 at DRDL, Hyderabad\n(ii) Propulsion panel meeting - 3rd September 2024, GTRE, Bangalore\n(iii) Propulsion panel meeting - 28-29th January 2025, DRDL, Hyderabad.\n6.\nStructures  Panel\n(i) Structures Panel meeting - 3rd July 2024, AR&DB Sectt., DRDO HQRs Annexe, Metcalfe House, Delhi\n(ii) Structures Panel  meeting and Academia Outreach Programme on 'Aerospace Structures Technologies'- 12th- 13th September 2024 at NIT Silchar.\niii) Seminar on 'Advances in Aerospace Structures Technology' Co-hosted by IIT, Bhilai and Structures Panel at IIT, Bhiali on 19th Dec 2024 and Panel meeting on 19th-20th December 2024 at IIT, Bhilai.\niv) Structures Panel meeting - 17th -18th March 2025, AR&DB Sectt., DRDO HQRs Annexe, Metcalfe House, Delhi\n7.\nSystems/Systems Engineering Panel\n(i) Systems/Systems Engg. Panel Meeting- 8th - 9th July 2024 at IIT, Kanpur\n(ii) Seminar on’ Systems Engineering for Aerospace Defence Applications’ 23rd September 2024 co-hosted by Systems/ Systems Engg. Panel & IIT, Hyderabad and Systems/Systems Engineering Panel meeting- 23rd -24th September 2024, IIT Hyderabad.\n(iii) Seminar on 'Aerospace Technologies in Defense sector- an overview' on 28th November 2024 & Systems/Systems Engineering Panel meeting -28th-29th November 2024 at BITS, Mesra, Ranchi.\n(iv) System/Systems Engineering Panel meeting - 3rd-4th March 2025, IIT, Kharagpur.\n8.\nSpace Technologies Panel\n(i) Space Technologies Panel meeting on 15th January 2025 at Directorate of  Special Projects, Hyderabad.\n(ii) Space Technologies Panel meeting and Outreach programme co-hosted by IIT Delhi and Space Technologies Panel at IIT Delhi on 21th March 2025.\n9.\nUnmanned Aero System\n(i) Unmanned Aero Systems Panel meeting - 30th May 2024, AR&DB Sectt., DRDO Hqrs Annexe, Metcalfe House, Delhi\n(ii) Unmanned Aero Systems Panel meeting - 30th August 2024, IIT Kanpur\n(iii) Unmanned Aero Systems Panel Meeting - 16th October 2024, AR&DB Sectt, DRDO Hqrs Annexe, Metcalfe House Delhi (through VC).\niv) Seminar on 'Unmanned Aero System Opportunities' on 2nd Dec 2024 co-hosted by IIT Palankkad & Unmanned Aero Systems Panel on 2nd Dec 2024 at IIT Palkkad and UAS Panel meeting -2nd -3rd December 2024 at IIT, Palakkad."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/aeronautics-research-development/list-ongoing-projects", "content": "Aerodynamics Panel\nDRDO\nS.NO.\nTITLE\nPI/Co-PI\nINSTITUTE\n1.\nMeasurement of Forces and Moments on Generic Models in a Hypersonic Shock Tunnel\nDr S Saravanan\nIISc, Bangalore\n2.\nNoise Supression in Supersonic Nozzles\nDr Rajarshi Das\nSchool of Mechanical Engineering, SASTRA Deemed to University, Tirumalaisamudram, Thanjavur\n3.\nEstablishment of Hypervelocity Expansion Tunnel Test Facility and Heat Flux Measurements Over Payload Configurations\nProf Mohammed Ibrahim S\nIIT, Kanpur\n4.\nFluidic Thrust Vectoring of a Supersonic Jet\nDr Arun Kumar P\nIIT, Kanpur\n5.\nCFD Analysis of Ejection Seat System of an Aircraft\nDr Sunil Chandel\nDIAT, Pune\n6.\nSupersonic Jet Control by Tabs with Slanted Perforation\nProf Suresh Chandra Khanda\nRajalakshmi Engineering College, Chennai\n7.\nExperimental Investigation of Base Pressure Field on Ducted Ramjet Intake Configuration\nDr M Viji\nCSIR-NAL, Bangalore\n8.\nCFD Simulation of Ring Laser Gyroscope\nDr Natteri M Sudharasan\nRajalakshmi Engineering College, Chennai\n9.\nInfluence of Mach Number on the Acoustic and Mixing Characteristics of a Strut-Cavity with Different Length to Depth Ratios\nDr NS Vikramaditya\nCSIR-NAL, Bangalore\n10.\nInvestigation and Development of Physics Informed Neural Networks for Analysis of Complex Fluid Dynamics Phenomena\nProf Arya Kumar Bhattacharya\nEcole Centrale School of Engineering, Mahindra University, Hyderabad\n11.\nEstimation of Aerodynamic Heat Flux Over Martian Atmospheric Entry Configurations- A Numerical and Experimental Investigation\nProf Ashok De\nIIT, Kanpur\n12.\nExperimental and Numerical Study on the Interaction of a Shock Tube Generated Blast Wave with Structures for Blast Attenuation and Mitigation\nDr Abhishek Kundu & Prof Satya Prakash\nMNNIT, Allahabad & CMERI, Durgapur\n13.\nPrediction of Aerodynamic Characteristics of Grid Fins at Subsonic, Transonic and Supersonic Flows\nProf P Theerthamalai\nACS College of Engineering, Bengaluru\n14.\nExperimental Studies on Flow Separation and its Control in a Submerged Intake\nDr C Manisankar\nCSIR-NAL, Bangalore\nAerospace Resource Panel\nDRDO\nS.NO.\nTITLE\nPI/Co-PI\nINSTITUTE\n1.\nDRDO Scholarship Scheme for Under Graduate and Post Graduate Level Girls Students Related to Aerospace and Aeronautical Engineering, Space Engg., & Rocketry/Avionics/Aircraft Engg.: 2019 (Batch-1)\nRegistrar( IIT Bombay, IIT Chennai, IIT Kanpur, IIT Kharagpur, DIAT Pune, PEC Chandigarh, IIES&T Kolkata, AVV Coimbatore)\nIIT Kanpur, IIT Bombay, IIT Madras, IIT Kharagpur, PEC Chandigarh, DIAT Pune, SASTRA Univ T.N., IIES Kolkata, BESU Kolkata, AVV, Coimbatore T.N.\n2.\nDRDO Scholarship Scheme for Under Graduate and Post Graduate Level Girls Students Related to Aerospace and Aeronautical Engineering, Space Engg., & Rocketry/Avionics/Aircraft Engg.: 2020 (Batch-2)\nRegistrar(IIT Bombay, IIT Madras, IIT Kanpur, IIT Guwahati, IIT Kharagpur, Birla Institute of Technology, Jharkhand, DIAT Pune, PEC Chandigarh, IIES&T Kolkata)\nIIT Kanpur, IIT Bombay, IIT Madras, IIT Kharagpur, PEC Chandigarh, DIAT Pune, SASTRA Univ T.N., IIES Kolkata, BESU Kolkata, AVV, Coimbatore T.N.\n3.\nDRDO Scholarship Scheme for Under Graduate and Post Graduate Level Girls Students Related to Aerospace and Aeronautical Engineering, Space Engg., & Rocketry/Avionics/Aircraft Engg.: 2021 (Batch-III)\nRegistrar(IIT Bombay, IIT Madras, IIT Kanpur, IIT Hyderabad, Indian Institute of Space Science & Tech., Thiruvananthapuram, Rashtreya Vidyalaya College of Engg., DIAT Pune, PEC Chandigarh, MNNIT, Allahabad, Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, Tamilnadu, Nitte Meenakshi Institute of Technology, Karnataka, Visvesvaraya Technological University, Karnataka)\nRegistrar (IIT Bombay, IIT Madras, IIT Kanpur, IIT Hyderabad, Indian Institute of Space Science & Tech., Thiruvananthapuram, Rashtreya Vidyalaya College of Engg., DIAT Pune, PEC Chandigarh, MNNIT, Allahabad, Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham, Tamilnadu, Nitte Meenakshi Institute of Technology, Visvesvaraya Technological University, Karnataka)\nMaterials & Manufacturing Panel\nDRDO\nS.NO.\nTITLE\nPI/Co-PI\nINSTITUTE\n1.\nExperimental Investigations and Electro-Thermal Modeling of Electrode Wear Compensation in Micro Electric Discharge Machining (uEDM) of Shaped Holes on Super Alloys for Improving the Dimensional Accuracy and Functional Performance of Cooling Holes on Turbine Blades and Vanes\nDr Basil Kuriachen\nNIT, Calicut\n2.\nExperimental Investigations on Nitriding of M50 Nil Steel for Aerospace Bearings Applications\nProf B Venkatesh\nVardhaman College of Engineering, Kacharam, Shamshabad, Rangareddy Dist.\n3.\nMechanical and Tribological Characterization of Al-Si Product Developed by Wire Are Additive Manufacturing\nDr Shivraman\nNIT, Warangal\n4.\nProcess Sequence and Metallurgical Assessment of Electron Beam Weld Joints of Martensitic Stainless Steel for Gear Applications\nDr M Vijayalakshmi\nMahatma Gandhi Institute of Technology (MGIT), Hyderabad\n5.\nPartial Slip Fretting Studies on AL 7075-T6 Alloy at Sub-Zero Temperature\nDr Vadivuchezhian Kaliveeran\nNIT, Mangalore\n6.\nStudies on Creep Behavior of Welded Gas Turbine Grade Su-718 Super Alloy\nDr K Venkateswarlu\nCSIR-NAL, Bangalore\n7.\nDevelopment of Pd Diffused Transition Metal (Mo,Co,W) Based Chalcogenic Heterostructures Support on Carbon Nanostructures/Ni Form for Electrochemical Water Splitting\nDr KK Aruna\nRathinam Technical Campus, Pollachi Road, Eachanari, Coimbatore\n8.\nDevelopment of ZrB2-B4C Functionally Graded Materials for High-Temperature Aerospace Application\nDr Siddhartha Roy\nIIT, Kharagpur\n9.\nDevelopment of Novel B and C Modified Fillers for the Gas Tungsten Arc Welding of Ti Alloys\nDr T Mahesh Kumar\nNIT, Warangal\n10.\nUnderstanding the Role of Hydrogen in Titanium Alloy Weldments\nDr N Kishore Babu\nNIT, Warangal\n11.\nStrain Partitioning and Damage Mechanism during Thermo-Mechanical Fatigue in a Ni-base CM247LC Superalloy\nProf Sumantra Mandal\nIIT, Kharagpur\n12.\nDevelopment of Screw Extruder Based Additive Manufacturing System for Developing Ceramic Core to be used in Turbine Blade Casting\nDr Sudip Kumar Samanta\nCSIR-Central Mechanical Engineering Research Institute, Durgapur\n13.\nNumerical and Experimental Investigations of Additively Manufactured Aircraft Wing Components Using Carbon Fiber Reinforced Polymer Composite Material\nDr DG Thakur\nDIAT, Pune\n14.\nDevelopment of Shape Memory Oxide Thin-Films for Aerospace Applications: Understanding the Phase-Switching Behavior, Related Defect Formation and Shape Recovery Process\nProf Kaustuv Manna\nIIT, Delhi\n15.\nDevelopment of Doped Barium Zirconate Titanate (BZT) Based Piezoelectric Ceramics for Acoustic Emission Sensor Applications\nDr Anoop Kumar Shukla\nAmity Institute of Applied Sciences, Amity University, U.P.\n16.\nDevelopment of Self-Biased Magnetic Materials for Low-Loss Bias-Field-Free Passive Microwave Devices\nProf Arabinda Haldar\nIIT, Hyderabad\n17.\nDevelopment of Perovskite Oxides SrCeO3 and Sr2CeO4 as High-Temperature Thermal Barrier Coating (TBC) Material for Aerospace Application\nProf (Mrs) Shail Upadhyay\nIIT Banaras Hindu University (BHU), Varanasi\n18.\nDevelopment of a Stable Machinability Investigation and Thermal Modelling of Aerospace Material\nProf Chinmaya Prasad Mohanty\nVIT University, Vellore\n19.\nDevelopment of Multiferroic Tapes for Sensing and Energy Harvesting Applications\nDr N Venkata Prasad\nUniversity College of Science, Osmania University, Hyderabad\n20.\nProcess and Hybrid Tool Design for Higher Productivity in FSW Butt-Joints of Thick A1-Alloy 2219 Plates\nProf Jeevan Jaidi\nBITS, Pilani, Hyderabad\n21.\nExtensive Evaluation of Mechanical Properties such as Tensile, HCF and LCF (at Room Temperature & at High Temperature) of Important Superalloys (CMSX-4 or CM-247) and Microstructure-Mechanical Properties Correlation\nProf Sushil Mishra\nIIT, Bombay\n22.\nDesign and Development of a Reconfigurable Electrochemical Machining Centre for Rocket Shells\nProf Janakarajan Ramkumar\nIIT, Kanpur\n23.\nHeteroatoms and Positive Charge Bearing Carbon Skin Comprising Graphene for Energy Storage\nDr K Krishnamoorthy\nCSIR-National Chemical Laboratory (NCL), Pune\n24.\nDevelopment of Long Lasting Polyurethane Nanocomposite Films and Life Time Estimation using Finite Element Analysis with respect to Aerostat Application\nProf Santanu Chattopadhyay\nIIT, Kharagpur\n25.\nMechanical and Microstructural Behavior of Laser Based Directed Energy Deposited and Wire Arc Additive Manufactured Ti-6A1-4V Components\nDr Ajay Kumar\nIIT, Tirupati and Sardar Vallabhabhai National Institute of Technology (SVNIT), Surat\n26.\nCreep and Fatigue of Selective Laser Melted Ti-6242 Alloy\nProf Srikant Gollapudi\nIIT, Bhubaneswar\n27.\nDevelopment of Ultra-Fine-Grained Thin Sheets of Beta Ti Alloys Through Constrained Groove Pressing and Cryo-Rolling Processes\nDr Suresh Neelakantan\nIIT, Delhi\n28.\nFeasibility Study on the Single Crystal Growth of the CMSX-4 Alloy Through the Direct Energy Deposition Process\nProf Abhik Narayan Choudhury\nIISc, Bangalore\n29.\nMEMS Based Tunable Film Based Bulk Acoustic Resonators with Magnetostrictive/ Piezoelectric Bilayer Composite Thin Films\nProf Jitendra Singh\nCSIR- Central Electronics Engineering Research Institute (CEERI), Pilani\n30.\nMicrowave Shielding of Quaternary Composite for Aerospace Industry\nDr Paramjit Kour & Prof Manoranjan Kar\nBIT, Mesra, Ranchi & IIT, Patna\n31.\nRepair of High Value Al-alloys Using Cold Spray Technology\nDr Ayan Bhowmik\nIIT, Delhi\n32.\nFabrication of High Temperature Piezo Pressure Sensor for Aeronautical Application\nDr Rajat Banerjee & Prof Shiv Govind Singh\nCSIR-Central Glass & Ceramic Research Institute, Jadavpur University, Kolkata & IIT, Hyderabad\n33.\nAn Extensive Investigation of Microstructure Evolution during Heat Treatments and Hot Forging of High Strength β-Ti-5553 Alloy\nProf Shanta Chakrabarty\nKIIT Deemed to be University, Bhubaneswar, Odisha\n34.\nDesign and Investigation of Nanostructured TBC Coatings (CoCrA1Y/Ta/Hf as a Bond Coatings and 8% y2O3-ZrO2, Top Ceremic Coatings) on Superni-718 Substrate in Adverse Environment at 800-1000C for Aero Space Engines\nProf Atikur Rahman\nNIT, Srinagar\n35.\nProcess Development for Refining Commercial Magnesium Metal Through Vacuum Distaillation in Semi-Continuous Mode at 5-6kg Scale\nDr Krishna Kumar\nCSIR-National Metallurgical Laboratory, Jamshedpur\n36.\nDevelopment of Incremental Forming Process Incorporating Novel Strategies for Titanium Alloy Based Aerospace Applications\nProf Anupam Agarwal\nIIT, Ropar\n37.\nOptimization of Post-Investment Cast HIPping Treatment of Aerospace Grade Ti-6AI-4V Alloy for Improvement of Fatigue Life\nProf Kumud Kant Mehta\nNIT, Rourkela\n38.\nDevelopment of Aerospace Components Through Electromagnetic Welding\nDr Meraj Ahmed\nCSIR-Advance Materials and Processes Research Institute (AMPRI), Bhopal\n39.\nAlleviation of Black Skin Formation on Anodizing of Additive Manufactured AISi10Mg Alloy Parts and Enhancement of Corrosion Performance\nProf P Chandramohan\nSri Ramakrishna Engineering College, Vattamalaipalayam, Coimbatore\n40.\nEvaluation of Mechanical Properties such as Tensile, Creep, LCF, KIC, FCG, CCG Values if an Important Cast Ni Based Superalloy (BZL-12Y)\nProf Sujoy Kumar Kar & Dr S Sivaprasad\nIIT, Kharagpur & CSIR- NML Jamshedpur\n41.\nOptimization of Friction Stir Welding (FSW) Process Parameters for Dissimilar Aluminum Alloy (2024-T3/7075-T6) Lap Joints\nDr M Suresh Kumar\nCSIR-NAL, Bangalore\nHigh Temperature Materials Initiative with Focus on Gas Turbine Materials (GTMAP) under\nMaterial & Manufactureing Panel\nDRDO\nS.NO.\nTITLE\nPI/Co-PI\nINSTITUTE\n1\nUnderstanding Room Temperature Dwell Fatigue Debit in Titanium Alloys with 3D Microtexture Characterization (GTMAP)\nProf. Satyam Suwas\nIISc, Bangalore\n2.\nLinear Friction Welding of Components for Gas Turbine (GTMAP)\nProf Satish V Kailas\nIISc, Bangalore\n3.\nDesign and Development of Bypass Duct Casing Assembly for Aero Engine Applications using High Temperature Composites (GTMAP)\nDr Ramesh Sundaram\nCSIR-NAL, Bangalore\n4.\nInvestigations into Ternary Interdiffusion in Bond Coat Systems of Я(Ni, Pt) Al and (Ni, Ru) Al (GTMAP)\nProf Kaustubh N Kulkarni\nIIT, Kanpur\n5.\nLaser Shock Peening of Inconel-718 Aero Engine Alloys (GTMAP)\nProf P Prem Kiran\nSchool of Physics, University of Hyderabad, Gachibowli, Hyderabad\n6.\nAccelerated Property Prediction of Titanium and Nickel Based Superalloys and Structural Safety Using Machine Learning (GTMAP)\nProf Abhishek Kumar Singh\nIISc, Bangalore\n7\nPlasma Spraying of Rare-Earth Niobates Powder and Controlling its Stoichiometry and Porosity for the Advanced Thermal Barrier Coating Applications (GTMAP)\nDr Anup Kumar Keshri\nIIT, Patna\n8\nThrough-Process Modeling of DS/SC Superalloy Turbine Blades Processed Using Modified Bridgman Route-Validation with CMSX-4 Alloy (GTMAP)\nProf Abhik Narayan Choudhury & Prof Saswata Bhattacharya & Prof Gandham Phanikumar\nIISc, Bangalore & IIT, Hyderabad & IIT, Madras\nPropulsion Panel\nDRDO\nS.NO.\nTITLE\nPI/Co-PI\nINSTITUTE\n1\nDevelopment of a Can-type GT Combustor Operating in Flameless Combustion Mode\nProf Sudarshan Kumar\nIIT, Bombay & IIT, Kharagpur\n2\nDevelopment of Catalyst System for Stable Combustion of HAN Green Propellants\nDr Shelly Biswas\nBIT, Mesra, Ranchi\n3\nSensitizing Fuel Oxidizer-Diluents Mixtures for Detonation Cycle Engines\nDr Ajay V Singh\nIIT, Kanpur\n4\nInvestigation of T--Vaporizer Atomization Performance- Effect of Internal Geometry\nDr Surya Prakash R\nIIT, Dharwad\n5\nExperimental Studies on Wankel Engine Performance at Enhanced Compression Ratios\nProf AJ Steve Mithran\nCSIR-NAL, Bangalore\n6\nMeasurement of Species Concentration and Temperature Using Coherent Anti-Stokes Ramam Spectroscopy (CARS) in Combust