{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/board-oxygen-generating-system-obogs", "content": "Back to Listing\nOn-Board Oxygen Generating System (OBOGS)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nOn-Board Oxygen Generating System (OBOGS) centric Life Support System to provide enhanced physiology protection to aircrew of high altitude and high speed fighter aircrafts. OBOGS replaces Liquid Oxygen System (LOX) by utilizing bleed air from the aircraft engine and separating its components using molecular sieve (Zeolite) Pressure Swing Adsorption (PSA) technology. The system consists of two molecular sieve beds with oxygen plenum to provide breathing gas to aircrew continuously.\nSalient Features\nLoadTwo bed OBOGS to meet breathing requirements of single and twin crew aircrafts\nBackup Oxygen System (BOS) to provide 40 minutes of breathing oxygen\nEmergency Oxygen System (EOS) to provide 7 minutes of breathing oxygen\nAutomatic backup and emergency oxygen selection\nCurrent status of Development/Production\nAlready developed\nProduction agency involved for the system/product identified\nL&T, Surya Aerotech, Vijay Sabre, United Rubber Industries, Tan Enterprises\nAbility of the production agencies to meet the requirement of Indian Armed Forces/ Security Agencies as well as of export\nYes"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/brahmos-0#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nBrahMos\nBRAHMOS is a universal long range supersonic cruise missile system that can be launched from land, sea and air. BRAHMOS has been jointly developed by DRDO, India, and NPOM, Russia. The system has been designed with two variants for Anti-Ship and Land-Attack roles. BRAHMOS Weapon Systems has been inducted and is operational with the Indian Navy (IN) as well as the Indian Army (IA).\nMore details on BrahMos can be found at\nhttp://brahmos.com"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/brake-parachute#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nBrake Parachute\nLabs\nAerial Delivery Research and Development Establishment (ADRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nBrake Parachutes have been designed to provide adequate deceleration to fighter aircraft of different weight class and to stop them within specified landing speed in both normal and emergency conditions. Well proven and inducted single canopy brake parachute is used to stop the aircraft, having landing weight varying from 9 Ton to 20 Ton for normal and emergency landing speeds. Very stable twin canopies brake parachutes had also been designed and inducted for fighter aircraft landing weight varying from 20 Ton to 40 Ton, for normal and emergency landing speeds. All the fighter aircrafts of the Indian Air Force operating within the country are equipped with the indigenously designed & developed Brake Parachute.\nImages\nBrake Parachute"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/bridge-layer-tank-blt-arjun#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nBridge Layer Tank (BLT) Arjun\nLabs\nCombat Vehicles Research & Development Establishment (CVRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nBLT Arjun is a fast and reliable bridge laying system built on the Main Battle Tank Arjun, it is\n\ncapable of launching a 24 m bridge with in 10 minutes on any wet and dry obstacles, facilitating\n\nspeedy induction\nThe launching mechanism is supported by State-of-the-art hydraulic system for launching and\n\nretrieval operations. It has a separate auxiliary engine provided for contingencies\nSalient Features:\nSlide launch assault bridging system mounted on Arjun chassis\nLoad class of bridge superstructure : MLC-70\nSingle span, tread way type construction\nCrew of two – Commander and driver\nIndependent power unit for bridge launch/retrieval\nBridge Length: 24 m in steel and 26 m in Aluminum alloy\nLaunch/retrieval time: 10 min"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/briefcase-satcom-terminal#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nBriefcase Satcom Terminal\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nDRDO has developed briefcase-type S-Band SATCOM terminals for voice/fax/data services. The terminals operate using the MSS transponder of GSAT-2 satellite and the central hub station. The weight of each terminal is approximately 10 kg and it can be deployed in less than a minute making it highly suitable for providing tactical communication from remote areas."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/bullet-proof-jacket-army-gsqr-1438bis-level5#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nBullet Proof Jacket As Per Army GSQR 1438/BIS Level5\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nModular Bullet Proof Jacket (BPJ) provides 360 degree protection as per the requirement of Indian Army GSQR 1438/BIS 17051 Level 5. BPJ is of 9–11 kg weight for different variants for all three sizes (Small, Medium and Large)."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/c4isr#top", "content": "Technology Category\nTechnology Development Task\nLab\nAI/ML Technology\nAI / ML based Command and Control Application\nDLRL\nAI powered C4I systems\nDRDL\nGIS based Maritime Domain Awarness Application with Data Analytics and ML\nCAIR\nAir to Ground Surveillance\nTechnologies for Air to Ground Surveillance - Mission Suite, Intelligence Exploitation Work Station, secured LOS and SATCOM datalinks\nCABS\nCyber Security\nCommand and Control Systems for missiles capable of handling Cyber attacks and DoS by adversaries\nDRDL\nElectro Optics\nElectro-Optic Payload for Remotely Piloted Strike Aircraft\nIRDE\nMiniaturized Electro Optical Payload for Aerial Launched Unmanned Aerial Vehicle\nIRDE\nMulti-spectral EO-IR Sensor for Intelligent  Surveillance and Reconnaissance (ISR) application\nIRDE\nNext Generation Electro-optical Sensors for surveillance system\nIRDE\nProcessing Unit for  Infra Red Search & Track (IRST) of Twin Engine Deck Based Fighter\nIRDE\nSensor Head Unit for Infra Red Search & Track (IRST) of Twin Engine Deck Based Fighter\nIRDE\nAdvanced Shared Aperture Multi-spectral System (ASAM) for ground Application\nIRDE\nAirborne ultraspectral, hyperspectral, multispectral  & panchromatic high resolution imaging payload for Intelligence, Surveillance & Reconnaissance (ISR)\nIRDE\nCompact Feather Weight Integrated Multi-sensor Surveillance System\nIRDE\nData analysis framework for Hyper-spectral Technologies\nIRDE\nFuturistic Ultra low pitch, High Format Detector for Situational Awareness System\nIRDE\nHand Held Thermal Imager (HHTI) for remote surveillance\nIRDE\nManportable Hyperspectral imaging camera with real-time material/target detection\nIRDE\nWide Area High Resolution Persistence Surveillance System\nIRDE\nFire Control System\nAI based Command & Control for Battlefield Management\nDRDL\nLOS Stabilization\nElectronic polarization compensation for Low  Profile LOS Stabilization Technology\nDEAL\nIntegration & assembly of motors, position sensors, RF components for Low  Profile LOS Stabilization Technology\nDEAL\nLow profile and lightweight direct drive gimbals for Low  Profile LOS Stabilization Technology\nDEAL\nLow profile reflector / patch array antennas for Low  Profile LOS Stabilization Technology\nDEAL\nRF based tracking for Low  Profile LOS Stabilization Technology\nDEAL\nState Space based controllers for Low  Profile LOS Stabilization Technology\nDEAL\nSubmerged Targets\nSubmarine Induced Waves Assessment using Satellite Sensors-Non-acoustic detection of Submerged targets\nNPOL"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/camouflage-technology#top", "content": "Technology Category\nTechnology Development Task\nLab\nAdaptive\nAdaptive Camouflage Technology for Armed Personnel\nDLJ\nAdaptive Camouflage Technology for Combat System\nDLJ\nFabrication of Terrain Specific Camouflage Uniforms in Near-real time by integrating GIS and Automation Technology\nDLJ\nAI/ML Technology\nCamouflaged Object Detection from UAV platform based on AI algorithm\nDLJ\nArtificial Vegetation\nCamouflage of military assets against seasonal variations using Artificial Vegetation\nDLJ\nTraining Simulator\nThermal target training simulator\nDLJ\nVirtual Reality (VR) Based Camouflage Simulation & Training System\nDLJ"},
