{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/catch#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nCATCH\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nIt is an airborne SIGINT system to cater for communication and radar intelligence. It covers UHF to Microwave frequency band and provides high sensitivity employing superhet receiver. Two systems have been inducted on IAF aircrafts."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/cbrn-defence-0#top", "content": "Technology Category\nTechnology Development Task\nLab\nBiomedical Imaging & Sensing\nAdvance tracer development and assessing translational applicability of hybrid radiotracers\nINMAS\nBlast Biodosimetry - To identify biomarkers (proteins/small molecules) for blast induced Traumatic Brain Injury\nINMAS\nBlast dosimeter for recording/measuring the blast overpressure in the field condition\nINMAS\nMedical Diagnosis triage and monitoring RN exposure\nINMAS\nPoint of care device for identified potent candidate marker for Traumatic Brain Injury (TBI) for rapid detection and on field testing\nINMAS\nProduction of medically relevant and medically acceptable radioisotopes- 64 Cu and 44 Sc\nINMAS\nRadiomic Finger Printing of RN exposure & ancillary injuries\nINMAS\nCBRN Countermeasures\nCombinatorial radioprotective and therapeutic countermeasures agents for mix radiation injuries\nINMAS\nDecorporation/ decontaminationg agents\nINMAS\nHardening of Building against CBRN Threats\nR&DE(E)\nUniversal Chemical Biological Warfare (CBW) decontaminant - New formulations of decontaminants which can decontaminate wide spectrum of CBW agents\nDRDE\nCBRN Support\nAdvanced Biodosimetry Techniques\nINMAS\nNext Gen biomarkers for rapid analysis of radiation damage\nINMAS\nMonitoring and Surveillance System\nCBRN Event Assessment System\nDLJ\nRadiation Source and Detection System Simulator\nDLJ\nAdvanced Nuclear Shielding Materials for Surveillance System\nDLJ\nNuclear Explosion Detection & Yield Estimation System\nDLJ\nNuclear Radiation Hardened Electronics\nDLJ\nSatellite payload for detection of Exo-atmospheric nuclear explosion\nDLJ\nVirtual Reality (VR) based CBRN defence Training\nINMAS\nVirtual Reality (VR) based Nuclear Warfare Training Module\nDLJ\nNBC Sensing\nAutomated Chemical Warfare Agent (CWA) sensor kit based on colorimetric sensor array and identification using imaging technique\nDRDE\nBiological Aerosol Detector using Laser Induced Fluorescence (LIF)\nDRDE\nBiological Warfare Agent Detection using Raman spectroscopy\nDRDE\nField identification of selected biological warfare agents using molecular and immunological techniques\nDRDE\nField portable RT-PCR and ICT card reader equipments\nDRDE\nFlame Photometry Detection system for chemical and biological warfare agent\nDRDE\nRemote sensing of chemical and biological agents - Standoff Chemical Detector\nDRDE\nUnambiguous detection of biological and chemical agents\nDRDE\nProtective Clothing & Gears\nChromium Free Carbon for Advanced NBC Canisters & Filters to degrade Chemical Warfare (CW) agents\nDRDE\nNBC Suit based on high adsorbent Activated Carbon Fibre (ACF) technology\nDRDE\nNext generation protective ensemble having in-situ decontamination capability\nDRDE"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/cbrn-facelet-mask#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nCBRN Facelet Mask\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nACF based CBRN Facelet Mask for use in emergency evacuation & rescue operations in case of chemical war alert."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/cbrn-gloves-mk-ii#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nCBRN Gloves Mk-II\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nCBRN Gloves Mk-II which is made with a special formulation of bromo-butyl rubber. Worn with CBRN suit for the protection of the hand."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/cbrn-haversack-mk-ii#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nCBRN Haversack Mk-II\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nACF based CBRN Haversack Mk-II for worn with NBC protective suit and used for keeping necessary accessories during chemical war fare scenario."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/cbrn-mini-ugv#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nCBRN Mini UGV\nLabs\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nCBRN (Chemical, Biological, Radiological & Nuclear) Mini UGV is used for detection, sample collection and marking of CBRN contaminated (Chemical, Biological, Radiological & Nuclear) zones without risk of exposing personnel. UGV being unmanned/ tele-operated vehicles have upper edge over conventional manned NBC recce vehicles, specifically, in terms of personnel safety for the Armed forces.\nExport Potential\nThe UGV platform can be configured for a variety of roles, CBRN being one of them. They are thus expected to have a wide demand worldwide. Export potential to be explored.\nImages\nCBRN Mini UGV"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/cbrn-overboot-mk-ii#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nCBRN overboot Mk-II\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nCBRN overboot Mk-II which is made with a special formulation of bromo-butyl rubber. Worn with CBRN suit for the protection of Leg."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/cbrn-recce-vehicle-mk-ii-tracked#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nCBRN Recce Vehicle Mk-II (Tracked)\nLabs\nVehicles Research and Development Establishment (VRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nThe CBRN Recce vehicle (Tracked) Mk-II is a reconnaissance platform capable of detecting, identifying, monitoring and marking of areas contaminated with CBRN agents and transmit this information to the supported formations. The vehicle is based on BMP-II platform re-engineered to accommodate different systems required for CBRN Recce purpose. The CBRN Reconnaissance Vehicle (Tracked) Mark- II will be used in plains and desert/semi deserts terrains."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/cemilac#top", "content": ""},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/centre_for_military_airworthines/aircraft1#top", "content": "Directorate of Aircraft\nThe directorate of aircraft  facilitates the airworthiness certification and continued airworthiness certification coverage for fixed wing military and transport aircrafts both, manned & unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) and helicopters designed and developed by Public Sector Units, DRDO and private industries. It has seven field units called regional centre for military airworthiness (RCMA) to provide the airworthiness certification locally. Besides coordinating with various user services regarding the certification policy and other related issues, this directorate is also responsible for promulgating the policies/directives/guidelines issued by CEMILAC related to ab-initio aircraft certification, aircraft upgrade programs and life extension activities. The directorate also is an interface between the user services, designers & developers and CEMILAC for matters pertaining to aircraft certification.\nPostal Address\nDirector (Aircraft)\nCentre for Military Airworthiness & Certification (CEMILAC)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence.\nMarathahalli Colony Post.\nBengaluru-560037.\nPhone         : 080 - 25121100\nFax              : 080 - 25234368\nRegional Centre of Military Certification (Aircraft)\nRegional Centre of Military Certification(Aircraft) is located at Bengaluru in the premises of HAL aircraft division. It facilitates airworthiness certification of ab-initio-Projects and continued airworthiness certification activities of military aircrafts of Indian & Western origin. Besides integration clearance / PCs for new development projects & major modification on Indian military aircrafts, it is also involved in approval of SOP & ESOP documents for military helicopters.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness(Aircraft)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nC/o Aircraft Division,\nVimanapura Post.\nBengaluru - 560017\nPhone     : 080 - 2522 6375\nFax          : 080 - 2523 3673\nRegional Certification of Military Airworthiness (Chandigarh)\nRegional Certification of Military Airworthiness (Chandigarh) is located in the IAF, 3-BRD Chandigarh complex. It facilitates airworthiness approval of indigenous airborne spares and modifications for helicopters of Russian origin. The centre also provides airworthiness approval of general spares & systems and Electro-Optical systems being indigenously designed & developed.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Chandigarh)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nC/o 3 BRD, Air Force\nChandigarh - 160003\nPhone : 0172 - 2637225\nFax : 0172 - 2637017\nRegional Certification of Military Airworthiness (Goa)\nRegional Centre of Military Airworthiness(Goa) is located in Goa in the premises of Naval Base, INS Hansa. It facilitates continued airworthiness certification activities of military aircrafts of Indian Navy. It is also involved in integration clearance / clearance for new development projects and modification on Indian Naval Military Aircrafts. It also maintains day-to-day contact with naval units at Goa on technical issues arising due to operational use and take necessary action to ensure maintenance of airworthiness.\nAddress\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Goa) DRDO,\nMinistry of Defence C/o INAS 552 NFTS, INS Hansa Dabolim,\nGoa - 403801\nPostal Address\nPlease Contact RCMA (Nasik)\nRegional Certification of Military Airworthiness (Helicopters)\nRegional Centre of Military Airworthiness (Helicopters) is located at Bengaluru in the premises of HAL(Helicopter Division). It facilitates airworthiness certification for ab-initio – projects / developmental projects of military helicopters and their modifications. It also undertakes integration clearance for newly developed / modified LRUs besides approval of SOP and ESOP documents for military helicopters of Indian & Western origin.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Helicopters) DRDO,\nMinistry of Defence\nC/o HAL Helicopter Division.\nBengaluru - 560017\nPhone : 080 - 2523 1533\nFax : 080 - 2523 2139\nRegional Centre of Military Airworthiness (Kanpur)\nRegional Centre of Military Airworthiness (Kanpur) is located at Kanpur in HAL premises. It facilitates airworthiness of western aircrafts, its modifications, life extension programs and also airworthiness coverage for airborne parachute systems. Besides integration clearance for newly developed / modified LRUs, this centre is involved in approval of SOP and ESOP documents for western aircrafts.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Kanpur)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nC/o. HAL Aerodrome PO.\nKanpur - 208008\nPhone     : 0512 - 2453693\nFax          : 0512 - 2457101\nRegional Centre of Military Airworthiness (Missile)\nRegional Centre of Military Airworthiness (Missiles) is located in Hyderabad in the premises of DRDL, Kanchanbagh. It is involved in airborne store development programme by facilitating airworthiness support to Air-Air Missile programme for fixed wing aircraft and Anti Tank Guided Missile programme for rotary wing. Besides other projects, it is also involved in life extension for Air Launched Missile and conversion of Short Range Missile.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Missile) DRDO,\nMinistry of Defence\nDRDL Campus\nKanchanbagh\nPO Hyderabad – 500058\nPhone : 040 - 29804057\nFax : 040 - 24341142\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Nasik)\nRegional Centre of Military Airworthiness (Nasik) is located in the premises of HAL, Ojhar. It facilitates airworthiness certification of Russian origin aircraft operated through design evaluation of indigenous development of materials, spares, rotables and systems. It is providing certification cover towards life extension, modifications and integration of various stores/systems besides providing continued airworthiness coverage.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Nasik)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nC/o HAL Nasik\nOjhar Township, Nasik - 422207\nPhone    : 02550 - 275159\nFax         : 02550 - 275912"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/centre_for_military_airworthines/aps1#top", "content": "Directorate of Public Interface\nThe Directorate of Public Interface is the single point of contact of CEMILAC for the defence eco-system. Besides liasoning with DRDO HQs & Ministry of Defence, this directorate is the nodal agency of CEMILAC to drive the industry outreach & interactions through synergy meets/seminars/workshops/one-to-one meetings. Most importantly, this directorate is responsible to issue directions for certification. Also the directorate is responsible for processing type approvals and design organisation approvals. Further   the public interface directorate compiles & generates reports & returns on behalf of CEMILAC and publishes guidelines/booklets/compendium/journals towards certification & airworthiness.\nPostal Address\nDirector (Public Interface)\nCentre for Military Airworthiness & Certification (CEMILAC)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nMarathahalli Colony Post\nBengaluru - 560037\nPhone        : 080 - 25121400\nFax             : 080 - 25234765\nEmail         : dte-mat[dot]pi[at]gov[dot]in"},
