{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/controlled-aerial-delivery-system-cads", "content": "Back to Listing\nControlled Aerial Delivery System (CADS)\nLabs\nAerial Delivery Research and Development Establishment (ADRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nCADS delivers the attached payload within a CEP of 100 m utilizing gliding & manoeuvring capability of a high performance RAM Air Parachute. The system operates under complete autonomous mode with manual override capability during its entire flight regime. The system could be dropped from an altitude of 7600 m (max) (AMSL) and can travel up to 30 km. CADS technology for 500 kg payload has already developed and demonstrated successfully for induction. The lab is under advanced stage of development of technology for 1Ton payload delivery capability and intends to extend it up to 7 Ton."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/copyright-policy#top", "content": "Material featured on this Portal may be reproduced free of charge after taking proper permission by sending a mail to us. However, the material has to be reproduced accurately and not to be used in a derogatory manner or in a misleading context. Wherever the material is being published or issued to others, the source must be prominently acknowledged. However, the permission to reproduce this material shall not extend to any material which is identified as being copyright of a third party. Authorisation to reproduce such material must be obtained from the departments/copyright holders concerned."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/counter-swarm-technology#top", "content": "Technology Category\nTechnology Development Task\nLab\nAI/ML Technology\nSwarm of Vertical Take Off and Landing (VTOL) UAVs as anti-swarm\nDYSL-AT"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/crevasse-crossing-bridge-ccb", "content": "Back to Listing\nCrevasse Crossing Bridge (CCB)\nLabs\nResearch & Development Establishment (Engrs.)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nThe crevasse crossing bridge is fabricated using light weight high strength weldable and selfageing aluminium alloy for crossing crevasses in snow bound areas. It enhances the mobility of troops, arms ammunition and supplies in these regions.\nDetachable railing is provided for safety. The bridge is designed for a load up to 550 kg i.e. snow scooter + pay load, besides limited uncleared fresh snow. The bridge is launched across the crevasse manually, with the help of a nose launching assembly.\nImages\nCrevasse Crossing Bridge (CCB)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/cu-ti-non-sparking-tools#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nCu‐Ti Non Sparking Tools\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nDMRL has developed a Cu‐4.5Ti alloy for manufacturing non‐sparking tools as a substitute to toxic and expensive Cu‐Be alloys. The alloy possesses good conductivity and strength.\nAdvantages\nNon‐toxic and the problem of health hazards does not arise\nLower cost as Ti ores are in abundance\nApplication Areas\nNon‐sparking tools are widely used in mining, petroleum and explosive handling industries in defence as well as civil sectors."},
