{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/defence-science-forum/aims-objectives", "content": "To create scientific temperament and environment among scientists of DRDO through close interactions among themselves.\nTo promote intellectual activities of science and technology by the way of conducting seminars, debates, lectures, conferences, symposia etc by inviting eminent experts of both national and international repute from various disciplines.\nTo create awareness among the scientists regarding latest developments in various fields of science and technology.\nTo promote reading habits and library culture among scientists by disseminating scientific and technical information relevant to their work.\nTo exchange scientific ideas among fellow scientists.\nBesides celebrating National Science Day on 28th February and National Technology Day on 11th May every year, Defence Science Forum regularly organises seminars and symposia where eminent Scientists of DRDO as well as outside DRDO give talks on various subjects."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/defence-science-forum/dsf-recent-results", "content": "DSF winners\n450 KB\nPoster score\n278 KB\nQuiz score\n189 KB\nEssay score\n441 KB"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/defence-science-forum/forthcoming-events", "content": "Defence Science Forum (DSF) has planned to celebration National Science Day 2023 on 28th Feb 2023 at Kothari Auditorium, DRDO Bhawan, DRDO HQr. Secretary DD R&D and Chairman DRDO will preside over the function."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/defence-science-forum/home#top", "content": "Defence Science Forum (DSF) has planned to celebration Technology Day 2023 on 17th May 2023 at Kothari Auditorium, DRDO Bhawan, DRDO HQr. Secretary DD R&D and Chairman DRDO will preside over the function.\nIntroduction\nDefence Research & Development Organisation is engaged in developing indigenous knowledge and technology to look after the needs of defence forces. It is well known that almost all the areas of technology development are interdisciplinary in nature for which specialists belong to different specialties like Engineering, Physics, Chemistry, Biology and their sub-specialties need to interact in a constructive and cohesive manner. Only then the lofty goal of upliftment of machine and man-behind-the machine can be achieved.\nIn order to develop a common platform where scientists of various disciplines could interact for mutual development the Defence Science Forum has been created in the year 1994 keeping in mind the objectives of interaction of scientists of various disciplines, to foster fellowship, exchange of ideas with luminaries of different disciplines and feasibility & planning of all interdisciplinary projects where expert opinion is required.\nTo meet these objectives periodical invited lectures, colloquium and seminars are organised by this forum. Besides these Defence Science Forum also organise special functions on National Science Day and on Technology Day."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/defence-science-forum/national-science-day", "content": "National Science day is celebrated every year on 28th Feb. - the day when Raman's effect was invented by Prof C.V. Raman at the Indian Association for the Cultivation of Science, Kolkata. After the formation of the forum on 4-10-94, following speakers have addressed on Science day in the forum till date.\nDATE\nTOPIC\nSPEAKER\n04-03-2021\nNational Science Day 2021 Lecture\n05-03-2018\nBridging Academic R&D with Product Innovation - a few case studies and a way forward\n130 KB\nProf. V. Ramgopal Rao Director IIT Delhi New Delhi\n28-02-2017\nWellness : A New Concept\n133 KB\nDr. B M Hegde, Padma Bhushan Awardee\nPresident World Academy of Authentic Healing Sciences, Mangalore\n04-03-2016\nRenewable Energy p Roadmap - R&D issues\n482 KB\nShri Upendra Tripathy, IAS\nSecretary, Ministry of New and Renewable Energy\n27-02-2015\nNational Science Day Address\nDr. Sudershan Kumar, DS & CC R& D (PC & SI)\n27-02-2015\nThe P (Not Equal To) NP Hypothesis\n367 KB\nProf. Manindra Agrawal (IIT Kanpur)\n27-02-2015\nMachines (Non-human) And Thinking: Can They Co-exist\nDr Pinaki Roychowdhury, Sc F, DTRL (Delhi)\n27-02-2015\nBroadband Electromagnetically Coupled Circularly Polarized Antenna Design\nShri Prashant Kumar Mishra, Sc E, RCI Hyderabad\n27-02-2015\nReduction of Hydrogen Gas Evolution on Aluminum Anode of Al-AgO Battery by Heat Treatment\nShri M Srinivas, Sc C, NSTL\n28-02-2014\nFuturistic Science & Technology for National Security\n1.2 MB\nProf. Sanjay Govind Dhande, Member UGC, National Security Advisory Board and Former Director IIT Kanpur\n28-02-2014\nNational Science Day Address\nShri Avinash Chander, Secretary Department of Defence R&D, DG R&D and SA to RM\n28-02-2013\nFrontiers in Non-Destructive Evaluation: Science & Technology\nPadma Shri Dr Baldev Raj\n28-02-2013\nNational Science Day Address\nShri Avinash Chander, Distinguished Scientist & CC R&D (MSS)\n28-02-2012\nNuclea