{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/dr-smt-chandrika-kaushik#top", "content": "Dr. (Smt) Chandrika Kaushik\nOutstanding Scientist & Director General - Production Coordination & Services Interaction (PC & SI)\nDr. (Smt) Chandrika Kaushik, Scientist 'H' & Outstanding Scientist, took over as Director General(Production Coordination & Services Interaction (PC & SI) w.e.f. 1 June 2022."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/dr-upendra-kumar-singh#top", "content": "Dr Upendra Kumar Singh\nDistinguished Scientist & Director General - Soldier Support System (SSS)\nDr. Upendra Kumar Singh has been appointed as Director General - Soldier Support System (SSS)."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/drdo-biotoilet-floating-conditions-0", "content": "Back to Listing\nDRDO Biotoilet for Floating conditions\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nDue to human excrements, river and lakes are getting contaminated and eutrophication is happening. Many a lake (as per example Dal lake, Srinagar) can be saved from incorporation of human excreta through DRDO based Biotoilet technology. This variants DRDO Biotoilet for Floating condition can address the issue.\nMain Features:\nDesigned for treatment under floating conditions in lakes and rivers with easy serviceability and toeing (if required).\nHouseboat sanitation (eg. Dal Lake, Kashmir) can appropriately be addressed.\nProvision for working in freezing condition.\nEffluent water quality as per environmental norms."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/drdo-biotoilet-floating-conditions", "content": "Back to Listing\nDRDO Biotoilet for Floating conditions\nLabs\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nDue to human excrements, river and lakes are getting contaminated and eutrophication is happening. Many a lake (as per example Dal lake, Srinagar) can be saved from incorporation of human excreta through DRDO based Biotoilet technology. This variants DRDO Biotoilet for Floating condition can address the issue.\nMain Features:\nDesigned for treatment under floating conditions in lakes and rivers with easy serviceability and toeing (if required).\nHouseboat sanitation (eg. Dal Lake, Kashmir) can appropriately be addressed.\nProvision for working in freezing condition.\nEffluent water quality as per environmental norms."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/drdo-biotoilet-high-altitude-areas-0", "content": "Back to Listing\nDRDO Biotoilet for High altitude areas\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nMaintaining appropriate Sanitation condition is a serious problem at high altitude region because of the low temperature and terrain conditions. To address the issue, DRL has developed appropriate sanitation system for HA region. Many such systems are installed at army units situated in extreme locations of Himalayan region.\nMain Features:\nSpecially designed (patented) system, that can withstand extreme cold conditions especially during winter months.\nAppropriately insulated system that can be used for small posts for armed forces to larger units (volume of the treatment system is as per users).\nThermostatically controlled heating can be provisioned as per requirements.\nThe system can be used for small to large number of users.\nMinimum human intervention\nUseful for Armed Forces personnel stationed at extreme location\nSafe to discharge water to the environment or can be reused after proper treatment"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/drdo-biotoilet-high-altitude-areas", "content": "Back to Listing\nDRDO Biotoilet for High altitude areas\nLabs\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nMaintaining appropriate Sanitation condition is a serious problem at high altitude region because of the low temperature and terrain conditions. To address the issue, DRL has developed appropriate sanitation system for HA region. Many such systems are installed at army units situated in extreme locations of Himalayan region.\nMain Features:\nSpecially designed (patented) system, that can withstand extreme cold conditions especially during winter months.\nAppropriately insulated system that can be used for small posts for armed forces to larger units (vo-lume of the treatment system is as per users).\nThermostatically controlled heating can be provisioned as per requirements.\nThe system can be used for small to large number of users.\nMinimum human intervention\nUseful for Armed Forces personnel stationed at extreme location\nSafe to discharge water to the environment or can be reused after proper treatment"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/drdo-biotoilet-indian-railway-0", "content": "Back to Listing\nDRDO Biotoilet for Indian Railway\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nDRDO has developed biotoilet for Indian Railway, where the biotoilets are fitted in the coaches for on board treatment of fecal matter and urine. At least 2.5 lakh Bio-digesters have already been fitted with train coaches. With IR-RDSO, this uniquely designed patented technology is keeping railway tracks defecation free.\nMain Features:\nSpecially designed to cater the requirements of trains.\nNo foul discharge from coaches into the tracks\nHygienic disposal of effluent"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/drdo-biotoilet-indian-railway", "content": "Back to Listing\nDRDO Biotoilet for Indian Railway\nLabs\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nDRDO has developed biotoilet for Indian Railway, where the biotoilets are fitted in the coaches for on board treatment of fecal matter and urine. At least 2.5 lakh Bio-digesters have already been fitted with train coaches. With IR-RDSO, this uniquely designed patented technology is keeping railway tracks defecation free.\nMain Features:\nSpecially designed to cater the requirements of trains.\nNo foul discharge from coaches into the tracks\nHygienic disposal of effluent"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/drdo-biotoilet-plain-areas", "content": "Back to Listing\nDRDO Biotoilet for plain Areas\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nBiotoilet is a uniquely designed patented anerobic containment and on-site treatment system that degrades human excreta (feces& urine) into gases and water with the help of group of potential microorganisms. The system is getting popular for onsite sewage treatment and can be installed from house hold (individual) to community level including railway stations, bus stands including schools, colleges and apartments.\nMain Features:\nOn-site construction-based system for household to community level.\nAdjustable to user’s requirements for application under different conditions.\nSecondary treatment (includes Reed bed system) of effluent water.\nNegligible human intervention.\nRecycling of effluent water for reuses.\nGeneration of odourless and inflammable biogas that may be harvested and used in specific case."},
