{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/event/national-science-day-celebration-drl-2019", "content": "National Science Day Celebration at DRL, 2019\nDate\n11/05/2019\nStatus\nCompleted\nType\nCelebration\nVenue\nTezpur\nNational Science Day was celebrated at DRL, Tezpur with the illuminating presence of “Master Innovator Dr. Uddhab Kumar Bharali, Padmashree Awardee” from North Lakhimpur district of Assam as the Chief Guest for the occasion. National Science Day oration titled “Aeration: A Nature’s approach for water treatment” was delivered by, Dr. Rama Dubey, Sc ’E’. On this occasion, “HYPOTHESIA: overcoming challenges of modern India with science”, - a competition among students of local schools was also conducted, which was aimed at students’. This was followed by the awe-inspiring presentation by the Chief Guest of the day, which showed his different simple yet highly impactful innovations in various fields including agriculture engineering, food science and apparatus for the divyangs. Finally the illustrious event came to an end with the scientists of DRL interacting with the Master Innovator.National Science Day was also celebrated at DRL Dett, Salari (Arunachal Pradesh) under the supervision of Dr. Duyi Samyor, Research Associate with the participation of teachers of local school and government officials."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/event/new-time-invitation-attend-drdo-oration-prof-balram-bhargava-secretary-department-health", "content": "New Time: Invitation to attend DRDO Oration by Prof. Balram Bhargava, Secretary, Department of Health Research and Director General, ICMR on  \"Value Conscious Innovations\" at 1415 hrs on 31 Dec 2019, Venue - Bhagwantham Auditorium\nDate\n18/12/2019\nTo\n01/01/2020\nStatus\nCompleted\nType\nInvited Talks\nVenue\nBhagwantham Auditorium\nInvitation to attend DRDO Oration by Prof. Balram Bhargava, Secretary, Department of Health Research and Director General, ICMR on \"Value Conscious Innovations\" at 1415 hrs on 31 Dec 2019, Venue - Bhagwantham Auditorium\nDocument(s)\nDr. Balram\n(255.27 KB)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/event/successful-firing-brahmos-air-launched-missile-su-30-mki-aircraft", "content": "Successful Firing of BrahMos Air Launched Missile from Su-30 MKI Aircraft\nDate\n23/05/2019\nTo\n23/12/2019\nStatus\nCompleted\nSuccessful Firing of BrahMos Air Launched Missile from Su-30 MKI Aircraft\nLink\nSuccessful Firing of BrahMos Air Launched Missile from Su-30 MKI Aircraft"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/event/successful-flight-nirbhay-ngl-06", "content": "Successful Flight of Nirbhay NGL 06\nDate\n15/04/2019\nStatus\nCompleted\nType\nAchievement\nIndia successfully tested its indigenously built Nirbhay cruise missile off the coast of Odisha on 15 April 2019. This was the sixth test of the Nirbhay, which is a subsonic cruise missile, distinct from the supersonic Brahmos. The Nirbhay was first tested in 2013. The Nirbhay missile had a problematic development, with some of the early tests experiencing failure. Jane's Defence Weekly reported in February that problems related to the missile's flight control software and hardware had been rectified.\nAccording to the Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO), the Nirbhay cruise missile uses a turbofan engine and uses inertial navigation and GPS guidance to reach its target. The Nirbhay has a range of around 1,000km. The Nirbhay is similar in concept to the US Navy's Tomahawk cruise missile. The Nirbhay can navigate to its target by flying past preset 'waypoints' on its route, often flying at very low levels."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/ew-system-sujav#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nEW  system  SUJAV\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nIt is a vehicle based compact communication Electronic Warfare system, developed as a spinoff of a major programme with jamming facilities in VHF and UHF frequencies for Low Intensity Conflict applications. More than seven numbers of systems have been deployed by Indian Army."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/export-products?title=&sort_by=title&page=3#top", "content": "Search for Product\nSort by\nAsc\nDesc\nNBC Suit Permeable Mk IV\nRead More\nNISHANT\nRead More\nOn-Board Oxygen Generating System (OBOGS)\nRead More\nP7 Heavy Drop System\nRead More\nParamilitary Variant of WhAP 8x8\nRead More\nPilotless Target Aircraft – LAKSHYA\nRead More\nPINAKA Ammunition Support Vehicles\nRead More\nRobotic Kit for Automated Driving (RKAD)\nRead More\nShort Span Bridge 10m\nRead More\nSnake Repellent\nRead More\nSubmarine Escape Set\nRead More\nTorpedo Advanced Light (TAL)\nRead More\nWatermelon in Ladakh\nRead More\nWeapon Locating Radar (WLR)\nRead More\nWheeled Armoured Platform (WhAP) 8x8\nRead More\nWheeled CBRN Vehicle\nRead More\nPagination\nFirst page\n« First\nPrevious page\n‹‹\nPage\n1\nPage\n2\nPage\n3\nCurrent page\n4"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/export-support#top", "content": "DRDO support industries in evolving the specifications of the export variant of the products (based on DRDO technology) to enable industries to respond to the RFPs. DRDO also carries out customization in the product to meet the requirement of customer countries based on the requirement of the Industries. The \"DRDO SOP for Export of Military Equipment\" facilitate Indian industries and DRDO labs to provide necessary technical support to industries for responding to RFI before necessary approval from MoD is obtained by the industry."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/faqs#top", "content": "Search your Query\nWhat is the full form of DRDO?\nDRDO stands for Defence Research & Development Organisation\nWhen was DRDO formed?\nDRDO was formed in 1958.\nHow can I join DRDO?\nDRDO has Recruitment and Assessment Centre (RAC) for Scientists (Group 'A' Class I Gazetted Post) recruitment and CEPTAM for recruitment of DRTC, Admin & Allied Cadre (Group ‘B’ and Group ‘C’) recruitment\nWhat are the pay scales of scientists/ technical cadre staff at various levels?\nFor complete information visit website\nhttps://rac.gov.in\nHow I can apply for JRF/SRF/RA/Apprentice Schemes in DRDO?\nEach individual lab publishes the requirements of manpower in what’s new section of DRDO website and in its lab page what’s new section as and when required.\nWhat are various modes of induction of scientists into DRDO system?\nLateral Recruitment for Scientist 'C' and above\nTalent Search Scheme (NRIs) for Scientist 'C' and above\nDeputation & Absorption\nI have some experience in Research & Development in the areas of interest to DRDO. Can I join DRDO at a higher post?\nApart from inducting Scientists 'B' (Entry Level), DRDO has following schemes for inducting Scientists 'C' and above (upto Scientist 'G') based on number of years of experience:\nLateral Recruitment for Scientist 'C' and above as per requirement of the Labs.(Through Advertisement)\nTalent Search Scheme (NRIs) for Scientist 'C' and above subject to suitability in DRDO Labs.\nHow can I contact DRDO for my recruitment related queries?\nGoto the page\nwww.rac.gov.in/feedback_form\nfor any recruitment related queries\nWhere are the labs of DRDO situated?\nDRDO labs are spread across India\nWhat is the procedure for doing summer Training in DRDO?\nYou can apply for summer training to Director of a suitable lab as per your discipline. You may visit DRDO website\nhttps://drdo.gov.in\nfor this purpose.\nI am NRI. What is the upper age limit to join DRDO?\nGrade\nUpper Age Limit\nC\n34\nD\n44\nE\n44\nF\n49\nG\n49\nAny experience required to be a scientist in DRDO?\nNo experience required for the post of Scientist B (entry level). And for other Scientist post, there is experience needed respectively as per guidelines. Goto website\nhttps://rac.gov.in\nI am a journalist, how can I get the information about latest news in DRDO?\nLatest news related to DRDO is updated in Press release section of DRDO website.\nI am a vendor how can I sell my products and services in DRDO?\nNew vendor can register online in DRDO website under Procurement section to provide products and services.\nI am research scholar, how can I know project sponsorships/scholarship/project grants opportunities?\nGo to the webpage\nwww.drdo.gov.in\nI am a research scholar, I want to publish my research paper in DRDO journals? What is the process?\nDRDO has separate web portal for publications. Visit\nhttps://publications.drdo.gov.in\nfor more information.\nIs DRDO Provide any amount for summer training?\nNo.\nDoes DRDO Lab outsource man power on contract basis for their project?\nYes. But, if there is requirement in project. Tender is published in website\nhttps://eprocure.gov.in/\nDid not find the information you were looking for?\nWhat code is in the image?\nEnter the characters shown in the image.\nGet new captcha!\nVertical Tabs\nRevision information\nRevision log message\nBriefly describe the changes you have made."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/feedback#top", "content": "Complete the below form to send us your complaint and suggestion. Your complaint and suggestions will be very much appreciated. If you provide us with your contact information, we will be able to answer your questions.\nFields marked with\n*\nare required.\nName\nContact Number\nEmail ID\nType\nSelect Type\nComplain\nSuggestion\nOthers\nOther Type\nSubject\nSelect Subject\nCareer\nProduct\nTechnology\nOthers\nOther Subject\nMessage\nEnter the Characters\nGet new captcha!\nVertical Tabs\nReset"},
