{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/flexi-life-saver-water-purifier", "content": "Back to Listing\nFlexi Life Saver Water Purifier\nLabs\nDefence Laboratory Jodhpur (DLJ)\nFlexi Life Saver Water Purifier is a simple and compact, cost-effective membrane based unit, in bottle-form which is field-usable, handy and user-friendly water purifier for purifying surface waters into potable water by just sipping and needs no electricity. Licensing Agreement for Transfer of Technology (ToT) of FLSWP has been signed with M/s Kent RO Systems LTD, Noida (UP)."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/flight-simulators", "content": "Back to Listing\nFlight Simulators\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nAvionics Part Task Trainer (APTT) for upgraded MIG-27\nThe APTT is a Real-Time Part Task Trainer used for providing training to the pilots of upgraded aircraft. The main emphasis in the APTT is to provide functional simulation of all the avionics subsystems of the upgraded aircraft, EW systems and weapon release systems. It provides training under normal flying (take off, landing and en route navigation) and under failure conditions.\nComputerized Pilot Selection System (CPSS)\nThe system is used to evaluate the candidates’ psychomotor skills along with cognitive information processing skills. A state-of-the-art embedded micro controller based CPSS with built-in security features has been designed and developed. The tests comprehensively evaluate the qualities required for military pilots such as psychomotor skills, Information processing skills (speed and accuracy), coordination, visualization, time-sharing, etc. by subjecting the candidates to perform concurrent multiple tasks.\nPilot mental workload assessment Simulator\nThis state-of-the-art simulation facility consisting of a flight simulator based on Real Time Simulator (RTS) and three channel visual projection display system along with cylindrical screen integrated with other psycho physiological measurement systems are especially established to assess the mental workload of fighter pilots. This facility is used to get a real time data capture for mental workload studies. The data collection is mission & task based and as such would help in building statistical models to arrive at the pilot’s work load for a given task and estimate the spare capacity of the pilot for better utilization."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/food-test-kits#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nFood Test kits\nLabs\nTest Kits\nMeat Test kit\nMilk adulteration kit\nFrozen/Chilled Chicken/Meat Quality Evaluation Field kit\nTest kit for E. coli detection\nPesticide detection kit\nPresumptive test kit for coliform detection\nAcidity testing paper strips\nTest kits for food borne pathogens / toxin"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/friction-stir-processed-aluminum-silicon-alloy-electronic-packaging-application", "content": "Back to Listing\nFriction Stir Processed Aluminum-Silicon Alloy for Electronic Packaging Application\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nBulk ultrafine grained hypereutectic Al-35% Si and Al-50% Si alloy has been developed by Friction Stir Processing (FSP) technology. The Al -35% Si and Al-50% Si alloy produced by FSP technology possesses ultrafine microstructure and excellent combination of strength, toughness & ease of machining."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/full-body-protector-female-soldiers#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nFULL BODY PROTECTOR FOR FEMALE SOLDIERS\nLabs\nDefence Institute of Physiology & Allied Sciences (DIPAS)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nThe Full Body Protector (FBP) has been ergonomically designed and developed based on the anthropometric data of female Indian troops. Well suited FBP for  the female troops working in riot control, as requested by RAF & CRPF.\nSalient Features\nExclusively for females as per their anatomy\nThe FBP consist of different parts which provide protection to most vulnerable part of the body in riot situations.\nProposed in 3 sizes: Medium, Large and Extra Large\nAnti-stab,\nAnti-puncture,\nAnti impact,\nAcid resistant\nFire resistant\nToT Holders:\n1)\nM/s Ajit Technoplast Pvt.Ltd.,\n104/430,P Road, Kanpur-208012, Uttar Pradesh, India, Contact No. : 9335036523/991839697\n2)\nM/s Netplast Pvt.Ltd\n. 2& 4 Uptron Estate, Panki, Kanpur-208022, Contact No.: 9336836886\n3)\nM/s Applied Systems\n128, Shanti Industrial Estate, SN Road, Mulund, Mumbai-400080, Contact No.: 09869075111\n4)\nM/s Bhagwan Associates\nGala No.117 Udyog Kshetra, Mulund Goregaon Link Road Mumbai-400080, Contact No.: 9820043612\n5)\nM/s Frontier Protective Wear\n, 2/2A Ho Chin Minh Sarani, Kolkata-700071, Contact No.: 9811149515\n6)\nM/s Novex Industries\n1724/125 Shanti Nagar, Tri Nagar, Delhi-110035. Contact No.: 09910008725\nImages\nFEMALE SOLDIER WEARING FULL BODY PROTECTOR\nSOLDIER OF RAF WEARING EXISTING FULL BODY PROTECTOR"},
