{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/headquarter-clusters/technology-management#top", "content": "Corporate Directorates\nDirectorate of Extramural Research & Intellectual Property Rights (DER&IPR)\nDirectorate of Futuristic Technology Management (DFTM)\nDirectorate of Technology Development Fund (DTDF)\nResearch Boards\nAeronautics Research & Development Board\nArmaments Research Board\nNaval Research Board\nLife Sciences Research Board"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/headquarter-cluster/about-us/human-resources", "content": "HR cluster is responsible for HR planning, organization in recruitment, selection, compensations, performance assessment, training and development of DRDO’s human capital. The HR corporate addresses various aspects of acquisition, nurturing and retention of best available talent. The formulation of establishment policies and ensure compliance to the GOI guidelines is also taken care by HR."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/headquarter-cluster/about-us/planning-coordination-system-integration", "content": "The Cluster of Production Coordination & Services Interaction (PC&SI) formulates policies for facilitating faster induction of DRDO developed systems by Armed Forces; advocating DRDO technologies to Indian Industries for production of systems and has augment industry technical competence; extending technical support and hand holding of Indian industries involved in development and production of systems for use of Armed Forces; boosting self reliance in defence by safeguarding the interests of DRDO and industries engaged in indigenous development of systems; facilitating cooperation among DRDO labs, foreign government agencies and academia for futuristic S&T and development of advanced systems and in supporting MHA and CAPFs by providing technical solutions based on indigenous technologies."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/headquarter-cluster/about-us/resource-management", "content": "R & M is the nodal cluster for the resource management of DRDO and deals in the planning and execution of projects and programmes taken up by the organization. It is responsible for financial management, material management, infrastructure requirements of DRDO and other corporate function like vigilance, security, Rajbhasha, O&M, coordination with parliament, C&AG, etc."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/headquarter-cluster/about-us/technology-management", "content": "The cluster has a mandate to create a research ecosystem in the academia, research institutions and industry for meeting the science and technology needs of defence and security of the nation. TM cluster identifies research gaps and provides financial grant to academic, R&D institutions and industry to undertake basic, applied and technology development research projects/programmes relevant to defence applications. It enables the cross fertilisation of ideas and experiences between defence and non-defence experts in scientific and technical fields relevant to defence applications; TM cluster is responsible for synergising the national needs and priorities of armed forces, to develop core competence in key areas; and lead technological innovations useful for short and long term combat technologies."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/headquarter-cluster/contact-us/human-resources", "content": "Director General\nHuman Resources (HR)\nDRDO Bhawan, DRDO HQrs\nRajaji Marg, New Delhi-110 011\nPhone :\n011-23016132,23016163\nFax :\n011-23016127\nEmail\n: dghr[dot]hqr[at]gov[dot]in"},
