{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/centre_for_military_airworthines/standards", "content": "S.NO\nNAME\nSUBJECT\n1\nARINC429 TUTORIAL\nAvionics Interface Technologies\n2\nDO 178B\nSoftware Consideration in Airborne system & Equipments Certification\n3\nDO-160D\nEnvironmental Conditions & Test Procedures for Airborne Equipments\n4\nDO-181Ddraft\nMode Select(ATCRBS/MODE S) Airborne Equipment\n5\nDSSD\nDRDO Standards for Software Development\n6\nMIL-HDBK-217-Rev1\nReliability Prediction of Electronic Equipment\n7\nMIL-HDBK-217-Rev2\nReliability Prediction of Electronic Equipment\n8\nMIL-HDBK-704-8\nTest Procedures for Demonstration of Utilization Equipment\n9\nMIL-PRF-29595A - Li-Ion Batteries\nLi- ion Batteries\n10\nMIL-STD-461E\nRequirement for the control of Electromagnetic interference\n11\nMIL-STD-704E\nAircraft Electric Power Characteristic\n12\nMIL-STD-882E System Safety Assessment\nSystem Safety\n13\nMIL-STD-883-3000-4000-Full\nDrive source,Dynamic\n14\nMIL-STD-883-5000-Full\nParameter Mean Value Control\n15\nMIL-STD-1275B\nElectrical System in Millitary vechicle\n16\nmil-std-1399\nInterface Standard for shipboard System\n17\nMIL-STD-1553Tutorial\nElectrical & Protocol Characteristic of Data bus\n18\nMIL-STD-1629FMECA\nEffects & Criticality Analysis"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/centre_for_military_airworthines/swec1", "content": "Directorate of Systems\nThe Directorate of Systems facilitates certification of electrical and electronic systems involves design evaluation of multiple LRUs with each LRU consisting of multiple software and CEH components embedded. Systems RCMAs ensure that certified systems are compliant to operational, performance and environmental specifications as per applicable international standards and/or user requirements.\nBesides coordinating the functioning of five regional centres, this directorate is also responsible to manage the four specialised centres viz., SCC, e-CS, C-CAT, SRM Centre.\nPostal Address\nDirector (Systems)\nCentre for Military Airworthiness & Certification (CEMILAC)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nMarathahalli Colony Post\nBengaluru - 560037\nPhone          : 080 - 25121451\nFax               : 080 - 25230856\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (APS)\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (APS) located at CEMILAC premise is responsible for certification of all avionics, mission payloads & sensors electrical systems including respective Complex Electronic Hardware and Test Rigs.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (APS)\nC/o Centre for Military Airworthiness & Certification (CEMILAC)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nMarathahalli Colony Post\nBengaluru - 560037\nPhone       : 080 - 25121500\nFax            : 080 - 25230856\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness(Hyderabad)\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Hyderabad) located at Balanagar, Hyderabad inside HAL premises handles certification of avionics such as communication, navigation, radar, control systems, EW systems, antennas, batteries etc. It also supports production of Su-30 avionics and LCA avionics at HAL (Avionics Division).\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Hyderabad)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nC/o HAL Hyderabad Division.\nHAL PO, Balanagar,\nHyderabad – 500042\nPhone        : 040 - 23779301, 23779302\nFax             : 040 - 23779350\nEmail          : rdrcma[dot]hyd[dot]cemilac[at]gov[dot]in\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Korwa)\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Korwa) located at premise of HAL (Korwa), handles certification of avionics such as flight data recorders, EO payloads, IRST, data link systems, mission management systems, HUD, MAWS, various sensors etc. It also supports production of INGPS and Su 30 avionics at HAL(Korwa).\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Korwa)\nPO HAL(Korwa),\nAmethi – 227412\nPhone          : 05368 - 255156, 255741\nFax               : 05368 - 255068\nEmail            : rdrcma[dot]kor[dot]cemilac[at]gov[dot]in\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Lucknow)\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Lucknow) located at Lucknow in HAL premise is responsible for certification of major and minor accessories of aircraft, helicopters, UAVs. It has certified thousands of accessories such as starter generators, wheels & brakes, hydraulic & fuel pumps, various valves, actuators, heat exchangers etc.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Lucknow)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nC/o HAL Lucknow Division\nLucknow – 226016\nPhone           : 0522 - 2351206, 23501927\nFax                : 0522 - 2350022\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Software)\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Software) located at CEMILAC premise is specialised centre for certification of safety and mission critical real time embedded airborne software, air launched weapon software, ATE & test rig software, and other ground software that have impact on operation of airborne systems.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Software)\nC/o Centre for Military Airworthiness & Certification (CEMILAC)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nMarathahalli Colony Post\nBengaluru - 560037\nPhone            : 080 - 25121451\nFax                 : 080 - 25230856\nSpecialised Centres\nCentre for Certification of Advanced Technologies (C-CAT)\nThis centre facilitates evaluation of niche and futuristic technologies, like complex electronic hardware, software defined radios, system on chips AI/ML. The centre has state-of-art V&V facilities for CEH certification.\nPostal address\nTechnology Director, C-CAT\nCentre for Military Airworthiness & Certification (CEMILAC)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nMarathahalli Colony Post\nBengaluru - 560037\nPhone          : 080 - 25121004\nFax               : 080 - 25230856\nE-Certification System (e-CS)\nThis centre manages day-to-day operations, updation and maintenance of the e-certification portal.\nPostal Address\ne-Certification Operations Management Centre\nC/o Centre for Military Airworthiness & Certification (CEMILAC)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nMarathahalli Colony Post\nBengaluru - 560037\ne-CS Helplines\n080 - 2512 1081\n080 - 2512 1005\nSoftware Certification Centre (SCC)\nThis centre facilitates static/dynamic testing of C/C++ code and requirements traceability for software certification standard compliances. The centre has various tools like LDRA, Rational DOORS, MATLAB with Simulink, Polyspace and Understand for C, C++, to accomplish this.\nPostal Address\nHead, SCC\nCEMILAC, DRDO\nMinistry of Defence\nMarathahalli Colony Post\nBengaluru - 560037\nPhone       : 080 - 2512 1452\nFax            : 080 - 25230856\nSafety Reliability and Maintainability (SRM) Centre\nThis is one of the centres of excellence setup by CEMILAC to handhold the DRDO Labs, PSUs and various MSMEs/SMEs in complying to the key requirements in Safety, Reliability and Maintainability by carrying out SSA, FHA, FTA, FMECA etc.\nPostal address\nHead, SRM Centre\nCEMILAC (DRDO)\nMinistry of Defence\nMarathahalli Colony Post\nBengaluru - 560037\nPhone          : 080 - 25121085/25121083\nFax               : 080 - 25230856\nEmail           : srm-centre[at]gov[dot]in"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/centre_for_military_airworthines/templates", "content": "SOFTWARE DOCUMENTATION\nS.NO\nNAME\nDOWNLOAD\n1\nPlan for Software Aspects of Certification\nDownload Doc file\n2\nSoftware Accomplishment Summary\nDownload Doc file\n3\nSoftware Configuration Index\nDownload Doc file\n4\nSoftware Configuration Management Plan\nDownload Doc file\n5\nSoftware Design Description\nDownload Doc file\n6\nSoftware Development Plan\nDownload Doc file\n7\nSoftware Quality Assurance Plan\nDownload Doc file\n8\nSoftware Requirements Description\nDownload Doc file\n9\nSoftware Verification Cases & Procedures\nDownload Doc file\n10\nSoftware Verification Plan\nDownload Doc file\nHARDWARE DOCUMENTATION\nS.NO\nNAME\nDOWNLOAD\n1\nBill of Material\nDownload Doc file\n2\nCompliance Matrix\nDownload Doc file\n3\nFunctional Test Plan\nDownload Doc file\n4\nMaster Drawing Index\nDownload Doc file\n5\nQualification Test Plan (SOFT or LQT or QTP)\nDownload Doc file\n6\nStandard of Equipment (SOE)\nDownload Doc file\n7\nStandard of Preparation (SOP)\nDownload Doc file\n8\nTechnical Specification\nDownload Doc file\n9\nTechnicalS pecification Test Jig\nDownload Doc file\nFORMS/FORMATS\nS.NO\nNAME\nDOWNLOAD\n1\nApplication for Type Approval\nDownload Doc file\n2\nCOMPONENT CHANGE PROPOSAL\nDownload Doc file\n3\nDRAWING CHANGE PROPOSAL\nDownload Doc file\n4\nProfoma for Design Criteria\nDownload Doc file\n5\nTypical Contents of a Test Schedule\nDownload Doc file"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/centre_for_military_airworthines/uav1", "content": "Directorate of Propulsion\nThe Directorate of Propulsion provides airworthiness coverage for ab-initio design & development for engine projects, licence manufacturing/overhaul /repair of aero engines, indigenisation of airborne stores, bought-out engines. This directorate also provides coverage to ab-initio aircraft of fuel system & power plant system, secondary power system (SPS) of aircraft through its three regional centres of military airworthiness(RCMA). In addition, this directorate is also involved in the release of various airworthiness procedures/ regulations and evolving guidelines for aero engines.\nPostal Address\nDirector (Propulsion)\nCentre for Military Airworthiness & Certification (CEMILAC)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence.\nMarathahalli Colony Post.\nBengaluru - 560037.\nPhone        :  080-25121300\nFax             : 080-25234781\nEmail         : gdpropulsion[dot]cemilac[at]gov[dot]in\nRegional Centre Military Airworthiness (Engines)\nRegional Centre Military Airworthiness (Engines) provides airworthiness certification coverage of all type of aero engines of western origin viz. turbojet, turbofan, turboprop, turboshaft, piston & rotary engines and starters. RCMA (Engines) also provides certification coverage for bought-out and joint development aero-engines programs. In addition, it provides coverage for indigenisation of various systems, airborne stores etc. In addition, RCMA (Engines) also provides support for secondary power system, general system and propulsion systems of various projects of ADA.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Engines)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence.\nC/o HAL Engines Division\nC V Raman Nagar Post\nBengaluru - 560093.\nPhone      : 080 - 25242341\nFax           : 080 - 25240075\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (GTRE)\nRegional Centre of Military Airworthiness(GTRE) is located in the premises of GTRE, Bengaluru. It provides airworthiness certification for advanced aero gas-turbine engines indigenously designed & developed and Advanced Turbo Gas Generator. RCMA (GTRE) also caters the certification requirements for indigenous development of LRUs/components besides coordinating & guiding system safety analysis for various projects. In addition, this office also works on the airworthiness aspects of propulsion system, secondary power system  and aircraft fuel system of fixed wings and other projects.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (GTRE)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence\nGTRE Campus\nCV Raman Nagar\nBengaluru - 560093\nPhone     : 080 - 25194062/25342168\nFax          : 080 - 25245572\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Koraput)\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Koraput) is located in premises of HAL (Koraput), Sunabeda. It is responsible for airworthiness of Russian origin aero-engines manufactured and overhauled by HAL(Koraput). The RCMA is also mandated with the responsibility to ensure airworthiness of aero-engines, its associated systems, sub-systems and LRUs.\nPostal Address\nRegional Centre for Military Airworthiness (Koraput)\nDRDO, Ministry of Defence.\nC/o HAL Koraput Division\nPost Box No.15\nSunabeda- 763002\nPhone      : 06853 221677\nFax           : 06853 220382\nEmail       : rdrcma[dot]kpt[dot]cemilac[at]gov[dot]in"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/centre_for_military_airworthines/what-we-do", "content": "CEMILAC is a Military Airworthiness Regulatory body under the umbrella of DRDO, located at Bangalore with 18 regional centres spread across the length & breadth of the country. The primary role is to certify the Airworthiness of Military Air systems (Aircraft, Helicopter, Engines, UAV etc.) along with other airborne stores used by Indian Armed Forces & Coast Guard.\nCEMILAC ensures that all the Air Systems & associated systems/stores meet the stringent safety & performance standards before being inducted in to the services. Further the organisation provides continued airworthiness coverage by certifying all modification / upgradation / life extension etc., right till end of service life of the aircraft.\nCEMILAC plays a crucial role in ensuring safety & reliability of the military aviation assets of Indian armed forces thereby contributing to operational efficiency."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/centre_for_military_airworthines/who-can-approach-us", "content": "Any organization/PSU/company/firm which is into design and development of Products for Indian defense airborne applications can approach CEMILAC for airworthiness certification irrespective of the fact that they have an order from the services/DRDO Lab/PSUs or not.\nApplication Format to seek CEMILAC Certification for Airborne Products\nIMTAR Forms 10A Airborne System\nIMTAR Forms 10B Airborne Store"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/citizen-charter", "content": "CITIZEN’S CHARTER\nDepartment of Defence Research and Development\nGovernment of India\nVision\nEmpowering the nation with state-of-the-art indigenous Defence and security technologies and systems.\nMission\nDesign & develop state-of-the-art sensors, weapon systems, platforms & allied equipment in defence & Security domains of land, air, sea, space & cyber.\nFacilitate production and induction of Systems & Technologies developed through Department’s R&D ecosystem.\nProvide technological solutions to the Services to enhance combat effectiveness.\nNurture & Strengthen Defence R&D capability in Indian industry, Science & Technology(S&T) institutions & academia through collaboration.\nDevelopment of infra-structure and test & evaluation facilities; design certification; skill development and strengthen human resources.\nSphere of Activities/Business\nApprising, assessing and advising Raksha Mantri on the influence on National Security of emerging developments in Science and Technology.\nRendering advice to Raksha Mantri and to the three services and inter services organisations on all scientific aspects of weapons; weapon-platforms; military operations; surveillance; support and logistics in all likely theatres of conflict.\nTo function, with the concurrence of the Ministry of External Affairs, as the nodal coordinating agency of the Ministry of Defence on all matters relating to Instruments of Accord with foreign Governments relating to the acquisition of technologies whose export to India is the subject of national security related controls of foreign Governments.\nFormulation and execution of programmes of scientific research and design, development, test and evaluation, in fields of relevance to national security.\nDirection and administration of agencies, laboratories, establishments, ranges, facilities, programmes and projects of the Department.\nAll matters relating to certification of the design air worthiness of military aircraft, their equipment and stores.\nAll matters relating to the protection and transfer of technology generated by the activities of the Department. 8. Scientific analysis support and participation in the acquisition and evaluation proceedings of all weapon systems and related technologies proposed to be acquired by the Ministry of Defence.\nTo render advice on the technological and intellectual property aspects of the import of technology by production units and enterprises manufacturing, or proposing to manufacture, equipment and stores for the Armed Services. 10. To deal with reference made under section 35 of the Patents Act, 1970 (39 of 1970).\nFinancial and other material assistance to individuals, institutions, universities and bodies corporate, for study and for the training of manpower on aspects of Science and Technology that bear on national security.\nIn consultation with the Ministry of External Affairs, international relations in matters connected with the role of Science and Technology in national security including:\n(a) Matters relating to relations with Research Organisations of other countries and with Inter-governmental agencies, particularly those which concern themselves, interalia, with the scientific and technological aspects of national security.\n(b) Arrangements with Universities, educational and research-oriented institutions or bodies corporate abroad to provide for foreign scholarships and the training of Indian scientists and technologists under the administrative control of the Department.\nExecution of works and purchase of lands debitable to the budget of the Department.\nAll matters relating to personnel under the control of the Department.\nAcquisition of all types of stores, equipment and services debitable to the budget of the Department.\nFinancial sanctions relating to the Department.\nAny other activity assigned to, and accepted by, the Department through understanding or arrangements with any other Ministry, Department, Agency of the Government of India whose activities have a bearing on the scientific and technological aspects of national security.\nAutonomous Bodies: Aeronautical Development Agency.\nStakeholders/Clients\nPrimarily, following agencies have been identified as stakeholders /clients of the Department of Defence Research and Development in varying degrees:\nMinistry of Defence\nMinistry of External Affairs\nMinistry of Home Affairs/ Other Ministries\nArmed Forces\nR&D centres of other Government Departments, Public and Private Sectors\nCoast Guard\nAcademic Institutions\nDefence Publics Sector Undertakings and Industrial Partners/Defence Industry\nCitizens of the Country.\nStatement of Services provided to Stakeholders/Clients\nServices provided to stakeholders/clients are elaborated in the topic ‘Sphere of Activities /Business’, given above. A summary is given below:-\nDesign & Development of weapons systems and platforms.\nScientific / technological help to the stakeholders.\nPromoting R&D in Indian industries.\nTechnology transfer of various DRDO developed products.\nWork on up-gradation of products.\nFacilitate exchange of engineers & scientists among DRDO, Industry & Academia.\nPromote green field research by Academia in areas related to defence applications.\nPhysical, Psychological, Physiological protection/well being of soldiers\nMake spin off technologies available for public utility.\nRedressal of Stakeholders Grievances/Concerns\nThe Department’s core business is to design, develop and facilitate production of state-of-the-art weapon systems, sensors and enabling technologies for the Armed Forces. The Department offers opportunity to the stakeholders to participate through different forums in the activities of the Department, and, on need basis ensures participation of such stakeholders who directly and actively influence the working of the Department. Peer Review Committee, Monitoring Committees, Apex Boards, Joint Project Monitoring Teams(JPMTs),Steering Committees ,Synergy Meetings and Quarterly Interaction Meetings (QIMs) are some of the examples.\nStakeholders continuously participate in the monitoring of the projects /programmes of their interest. All the concerns of the stakeholders are addressed objectively and timely in an institutionalized manner.\nFor general interactions with the Services, the Department’s Headquarter has a Directorate of Interaction with Services for Business (DISB). For all other agencies, Department’s Directorate of Planning and Coordination is the first contact point. Director Planning and Coordination is ex-officio Nodal Officer for the Citizen’s Charter.\nDRDO is placed in the Second Schedule of RTI Act, 2005 and is exempt from disclosure of information under Section 24(1) except information pertaining to allegations of corruption & human rights violations.\nExpectations from the Stakeholders/Clients\nA. Ministry of Defence\nInvolve the Department in making of capability development plans.\nShare threat perception with the Department.\nEvolve national policy enabling indigenisation of defence systems to ensure Aatma Nirbharta\nB. Armed Forces\nShare threat perception & operational requirement with the Department.\nInvolve the Department in formulation of Qualitative Requirements (QRs).\nInvolve the Department from conceptualization to deployment of the products intended to be indigenously developed and those imported.\nShare philosophy and methodology of the trials and acceptance tests with the Department.\nShare results of User trials and acceptance test spontaneously and transparently.\nEvolve integrated plans in consultation with the Department.\nBecome financial stakeholders in the development projects / programmes.\nDepute officers and personnel with appropriate background for the project/programme teams.\nC. Production Partners\nDevelop a long term strategic perspective of the technologies developed by the Department.\nFinancial stake in the developmental projects of interest.\nAllocate resources for concurrent technology transfer, absorption and production of items developed by the Department.\nWork on upgradation of products.\nFacilitate exchange of engineers/scientists between DRDO and industry.\nD. R&D Centres in Other Sectors\n1. Act as incubation centres for the technologies by the Department.\nUndertake incremental R&D work on technologies established by the Department.\nE. Academia\nTake up sponsored research, in the areas of interest of the Department.\nCreation of Centres of Excellence to pursue R&D in the emerging technology areas.\nWebsite of the Department :\nwww.drdo.gov.in\nKey Personnel of the Department\nSecretary Department of Defence (R&D) and Chairman DRDO,\nDRDO Bhawan, New Delhi-110011\nPhone : 011-23011519\nFax : 011-23018216\nDirector General (R&M)\n,\nDRDO Bhawan, New Delhi-110011\nPhone : 011-23011860\nFax : 011-23015395\nNodal Officer for the Citizen’s Charter\nDirector, Planning and Coordination\nDRDO Bhawan, New Delhi-110011\nPhone : 011-23016278\nFax : 011-23016174"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/contact-us", "content": "DRDO Headquarter\nDefence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO)\nOffice Address:\nDRDO Bhawan, Rajaji Marg, New Delhi-110011\nSubject Specific Query\nDirectorate of Industry Interface & Technology Management (DIITM)\n(For Transfer of Technology (ToT), Limited Series Production (LSP), Test facilities and Industry Support related queries)\nDirector\nDirectorate of Industry Interface & Technology Management (DIITM)\nRoom No 447, DRDO Bhawan, DRDO HQrs,\nRajaji Marg, New Delhi -110011\nPhone :\n011-23013209/ 23015291\nFax :\n011-23793008\nEmail :\ndiitm[dot]hqr[at]gov[dot]in\nDirectorate of Futuristic Technology Management (DFTM)\n(for Advanced Technology Centres related queries)\nDirector\nDirectorate of Futuristic Technology Management (DFTM)\nRoom No 325, DRDO Bhawan\nRajaji Marg, New Delhi- 110011\nPhone:\n23007794\nFax:\n23013462\nExtramural Research & Intellectual Property Rights (ER&IPR)\n(for academia related queries only)\nDirectorate of Extramural Research & Intellectual Property Rights (ER&IPR)\nDefence Research & Development Organisation (DRDO)\nRoom No. 348, DRDO Bhawan\nRajaji Marg, New Delhi-110011\nPhone :\n011 - 23017661\nFax :\n011 - 23017582\nEmail :\nerip_er[dot]hqr[at]gov[dot]in\nTechnology Development Fund (TDF)\nDirector\nDirectorate of Technology Development Fund (DTDF)\nRoom No 325, DRDO Bhawan\nRajaji Marg, New Delhi- 110011\nPhone:\n011-23007325/26, 23007794\nFax:\n23013462\nRTI Cell\n(RTI related queries only)\nRTI Cell\nDRDO HQ, New Delhi\nTel\n: 011-2301 5433, 2300 7724\nFax\n: 011-2301 5437\nEmail\n: cpio[dot]hqr[dot]hqr[at]gov[dot]in\nDirectorate of Civil Works & Estates (DCW&E)\n(Only for Enlistment of Contractors)\nDirector\nDirector (Civil Works & Estates)\nDRDO Bhawan, Rajaji Marg New Delhi - 110011\nTel:\n011 23011644, 011 23007003\nFax:\n+91 1123007596\nEmail:\ndcwe-works4[at]gov[dot]in\nDefence Scientific Information & Documentation Centre (DESIDOC)\n(for DRDO website related queries only)\nDirector\nDefence Scientific Information & Documentation Centre (DESIDOC)\nMetcalfe House, Delhi-110054\nFax\n: 011-23819151, 011-23813465\nE-mail\n: director[dot]desidoc[at]gov[dot]in\nRecruitment & Assessment Centre (RAC)\nContact\nRecruitment Applicants (CEPTAM)\nDirector\nCentre for Personnel Talent Management (CEPTAM)\nMetcalfe House\nDelhi-110054\nHelpdesk Number:\n011 - 23882323 (04 Lines), 23819217\nFax\n: 011-23810287\nEmail:\ndirector[dot]ceptam[at]gov[dot]in\nDirectorate of Public Interface (DPI)\n(for social media accounts and media related queries only)\nOfficial Accounts\nTwitter:\nDRDO_India\nFacebook:\nDPIDRDO\nInstagram :\ndpi.drdo\nDirectorate of Public Interface (DPI)\nRoom No. 117, 'A' Wing\n1st Floor, DRDO Bhawan\nDRDO HQs, New Delhi - 110 011\nPhone :\n011-23011073 (Off)\nFax :\n011-23007636\nEmail ID :\ndpidrdo[dot]hqr[at]gov[dot]in"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/copyright-policy", "content": "Material featured on this Portal may be reproduced free of charge after taking proper permission by sending a mail to us. However, the material has to be reproduced accurately and not to be used in a derogatory manner or in a misleading context. Wherever the material is being published or issued to others, the source must be prominently acknowledged. However, the permission to reproduce this material shall not extend to any material which is identified as being copyright of a third party. Authorisation to reproduce such material must be obtained from the departments/copyright holders concerned."},
