{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments?title=&page=3#top", "content": "Search for Laboratory & Establishments\nNo active record(s) available currently for this section.\nPagination\nFirst page\n« First\nPrevious page\n‹‹\nPage\n1\nPage\n2\nCurrent page\n3"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/advanced-systems-laboratory-asl#top", "content": "Vision\nThrust on design & development and flight evaluation of various types of missile systems\nMission\nTo develop state of the art core technologies required for design & development of missile systems."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/aerial-delivery-research-and-development-establishment-adrde#top", "content": "Vision\nTo be globally competitive in Technologies and Systems Development related to Parachute, Decelerators and Lighter-than-Air systems\nMission\nDevelop the entire range of Parachutes and Lighter-than-Air Systems to meet the needs of Services. Enhance expertise and infrastructre for undertaking Integrated Systems Development Task.\nProducts\nAerostat Health Monitoring System\nAircraft Arrester Barrier System\nAircrew Parachutes\nAkashdeep Medium class Aerostat\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/aeronautical-development-establishment-ade#top", "content": "Vision\nTo be a Centre of excellence for development of state-of-the-art Unmanned Air Vehicles and Aeronautical Systems for the Services\nMission\nTo develop and lead to production of Unmanned Air Vehicles and Aeronautical Systems to meet the needs of the Services and progressively enhance the Technological Infrastructure and Capabilities\nProducts\nABHYAS\nAvionics Part Task Trainer (APTT) for upgraded MIG-27\nCombat Aircraft Systems- Systems & Subsystems for LCA\nComputerized Pilot Selection System (CPSS)\nView All\nPhotos\nVisit of Dignitaries to LCA Full Mission Simulator at ADE\nSuccessful Test Firing of Quick Reaction Surface-to-Air Missiles (QRSAM)\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/armament-research-development-establishment-arde#top", "content": "Vision\nTo design and develop Competitive conventional armament systems and related technologies Leading to total self-reliance of the nation.\nMission\nTo equip the armed forces with world class, affordable weapon systems through innovation, research, integration, test and evaluation and transfer of technology to build a strong technology base for future developments through synergy amongst national research labs, academia and public / private industry participation.\nProducts\n500kg Prefragmented Bomb\n120 mm Armaments for ARJUN MBT\n120 mm Penetration Cum Blast (PCB) AND Thermobaric (TB) Ammunition For MBT Arjun\n125mm FSAPDSMk-II Ammunition\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/centre-air-borne-system-cabs#top", "content": "Vision\nThe VISION of the lab is to “Meet Technological Challenges of Airborne Surveillance Systems”.\nMission\nThe MISSION is to “Develop Key Technologies and Infrastructure for building efficient and cost-effective Airborne Surveillance Systems”.\nProducts\nAirborne Early Warning and Control (AEW&C)\nGround Exploitation System (GES)\nIdentification Friend or Foe (IFF) MK XII (S) with Mode 4 Capability\nPhotos\nInauguration of Security Complex by Shri M S Easwaran, DS, PGD(AEW and C) and Director, CABS on 9th May 2017\nInauguration of the hanger for FTB and AWACS (I) by Dr. S Christopher, Chairman and Secretary DD (R and D) on 9th May 2017\nInauguration of the Administrative Block by Dr. C.P. Ramanarayanan, DS, DG(Aero) on 9th May 2017\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/centre-artificial-intelligence-robotics-cair#top", "content": "Vision\n“Adding value to information\nEnabling battle space dominance”\nMission\n“To add value to information by delivering dependable information systems to the Defence services for battle space dominance, by developing domain & technologies that ensure relevance, security, safety, resiliency, survivability and trustworthiness enabling the use of these systems in mission critical applications with required guaranties of assured performance”\nProducts\nAir Defence Control and Reporting System (ADC & RS)\nAutomatic Electronic Switch (AES)\nAutonomous Navigation System\nAutonomous Search Robot\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/centre-fire-explosive-and-environment-safety-cfees#top", "content": "Vision\nTo evolve into a Centre of Excellence in the field of Fire Science & Engineering, Explosive and Environment Safety & to provide integrated safety advice and services to MoD establishments.\nMission\nR&D in Fire Science & Engineering, Explosive and Environment Safety; Regulatory Authority for Fire, Explosive and Environment Safety in MoD establishments; and Nodal agency for implementation of Safety Healthy Environment (SHE) & Disaster Management for DRDO.\nPhotos\nCentre for Fire, Explosive and Environment Safety (CFEES)\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/combat-vehicles-research-development-estt-cvrde#top", "content": "Vision\nBe a Centre for Design & Development of State-of-the-art Armored Fighting Vehicles (AFVs) for the Army & Spin-offs for Other services (Air force, Navy & CAPF).\nMission\nDesign, develop and lead to production of Tracked Armoured Vehicles, Specialist Vehicles and Combat Aircraft systems to meet the needs of the services. Build technological capabilities in critical areas including test & evaluation of Combat systems.\nProducts\n130mm SP Gun - CATAPULT\n5 kW Brushless DC Generating System for LCA Tejas\n5 kW brushless DC Generating system for LCA Tejas\nAircraft Mounted Accessory Gear Box\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-bio-engineering-electro-medical-laboratory-debel#top", "content": "Vision\nTo become a world class laboratory in the development of protective and life support equipment and biomedical devices and systems specific to service combatants\nMission\nTo carry out design, development and evaluation of state-of-the-art life support and biomedical systems and devices.\nCoordinate user evaluation and induction into Services.\nTransfer technology for productionization.\nExplore utilization of spin-off technologies for civilian application.\nProducts\nCBRN Defence\nCombat Free Fall System (CFF)\nHAPO chamber"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-electronics-application-laboratory-deal#top", "content": "Vision\nBe a center of excellence in the field of Military Communications & Surveillance Technologies.\nMission\nDevelopment of Software Based Radios, Anti‐Jam Data Links, Secure Satcom Systems, Millimeter Wave Communication & Surveillance Systems.\nProducts\nCombat Net Radio (CNR)\nCommunication support in disaster relief :\nConnecting Continents-Mission Antarctica:\nData-Link System – Nishant UAV\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-electronics-research-laboratory-dlrl#top", "content": "Vision\nBe a Centre of excellence in the field of Electronic Warfare.\nMission\nDesign and develop state-of-the art integrated Electronic Warfare systems for the Services and achieve self-reliance in critical technologies and components.\nProducts\nAEW&C (CSM) and Indigenous ESM & RWR Systems for AEW&C\nAJANTA\nCATCH\nCOIN-A\nView All\nPhotos\nDLRL Annual Day Celebrations 18th Nov 2018\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-geoinformatics-research-establishment-dgre#top", "content": "Vision\nTo be a leader in the development of critical technologies for enhancing combat effectiveness with a focus on terrain & snow based challenges.\nMission\nTo create a geospatial information system for operational planning & military intelligence\nTo provide cutting edge engineering solutions for ensuring safe movement of troops in all kind of terrain with a focus on avalanches & landslide5\nTo build AI enabled intelligent solutions for deployment"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-institute-high-altitude-research-dihar#top", "content": "Vision\nTo transform Defence Institute of High Altitude Research into a world class leader in cold arid agro-animal technologies.\nMission\nDIHAR will evolve novel inputs, with focused R&D in cold arid agro-animal technologies, which will enhance the agro-animal productivity to enhance the availability of fresh foods for troops in Ladakh, the most difficult terrain of the world.\nProducts\nCattle Development\nDouble Humped Camel for carrying load\nHigh  altitude adapted cattle\nHigh  altitude adapted chicken\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-institute-physiology-allied-sciences-dipas#top", "content": "Vision\nBe a center of excellence in the field of environmental physiology and human factor research.\nMission\nOptimization of human performance in different occupational environment conditions using physiological, biochemical, nutritional and ergonomic approach.\nProducts\nActive Ear Defender\nAlocal Cream for Prevention of Cold Injuries\nErgo Back Pack\nERGONOMICALLY DESIGNED LIGHT WEIGHT BOOTS\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-institute-psychological-research-dipr#top", "content": "Vision\nDIPR will emerge as a centre of excellence in Military Psychology.\nMission\nTo provide psychological support to the armed forces in selection, training, effective man-machine interface and motivation to enhance mental health and operational efficiency of the armed forces.\nProducts\nComputerized Pilot Selection System (CPSS)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-laboratory-dlj#top", "content": "Vision\nTo become a centre of excellence in Camouflage, Desert Sciences & Nuclear Radiation Management Technologies.\nMission\nTo achieve excellence and self reliance in the areas of Multispectral Camouflage and Low Observable Technologies, provide solutions to Desert related problems, and develop Nuclear Radiation Sensor Technologies and Applications of Radioisotopes.\nProducts\nBeta light\nContamination Monitoring Systems\nElectrochromic Panel\nFast Setting and High Strength Polymer Concrete Composites (PolyCC) For Rapid Repair of Runways\nView All\nPhotos\nDLJ Photo Gallery\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-research-development-establishment-drde", "content": "Vision\nBe a centre of excellence for chem-bio defence.\nMission\nDesign and develop state-of-the-art technologies and products for chem-bio defence and establish state-of-the-art repository and test & evaluation facilities for developed products.\nProducts\nAnthrax Detection Kit\nAutoject Injectors MK-II\nBiodigester\nBiodigester for Indian Railways\nView All\nPhotos\nDRDO SCIENTIST OF THE YEAR AWARD-2017\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-research-development-laboratory-drdl", "content": "Vision\nEmpower the nation with state-of-the-art indigenous systems and technologies for missile based weapon systems deployable from underwater, sea, land and air based platforms.\nMission\nDesign, development and leading-to-production of systems and technologies for missile based weapon systems deployable from underwater,sea, land and air based platforms.\nEnsure product support, product upgrade and end-of-life replacement.\nEstablish critical infrastructure and facilities for design, testing and evaluation.\nProducts\nAkash\nASTRA\nHelina\nMan-Portable Anti Tank Guided Missile\nView All\nPhotos\nInauguration of new buildings/facilities\nDRDL Annual Day Celebrations\nVisit of dignitaries at DRDL\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-research-laboratory-drl", "content": "Vision\nTo be a centre of excellence in technology development for troops for jungle warfare and border areas of North East (NE) India.\nMission\nTo provide world class technologies/ products/ knowledge/ services to Armed Forces to enhance their performance in jungle warfare and border areas of NE India.\nProducts\nChilli Grenade (CapsigrenadeTM)\nChilli Spray (CapsisprayTM)\nDearsenification Unit (DAU)\nDRDO Biotoilet for Floating conditions\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/defence-scientific-information-documentation-centre-desidoc#top", "content": "Vision\nTo provide essential science and technical research, development information rapidly, accurately and reliably to support DRDO’s Scientists’ needs.\nMission\nTo establish an integrated resource centre and state-of-the-art information management system encompassing knowledge centre, publishing, e-services, printing and multi-media\nTo collaborate with national and international institutions/academia/ organizations for cooperative partnerships to improve upon quality and bring visibility to DRDO's R&D Publications\nTo introduce new innovative Defence Research Journals for the benefit of R&D community\nTo improve the role of DESIDOC's Defence Science Library by reinventing library functions and services with focus on the perception and expectation of the users\nEmbracing advanced technologies to provide library and information services on emerging digital platforms\nIntroducing digital imprint of DRDO to connect with the scientific and civil society through online community\nBuilding a \"single window\" facilitation by improving the quality of print-media, multi-media and network services\nProducts\nDefence Life Science Journal (DLSJ)\nDefence Science Journal (DSJ)\nDESIDOC Journal of Library & Information Technology (DJLIT)\nDRDO E-Library\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/drdo-young-scientist-laboratory-artificial-intelligence-dysl-ai", "content": "Vision\nNo active record(s) available currently for this section.\nMission\nNo active record(s) available currently for this section."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/drdo-young-scientist-laboratory-dysl-at", "content": "Vision\nTo make India self-reliant in developing asymmetric warfare technologies which are subtle, unconventional and cost effective to combat new age threats by tactically engaging with its disruptive capabilities.\nMission\nTo design and develop unconventional technologies by promoting collaborative research within the country through academia and industry to enhance the capabilities of the armed forces in asymmetric warfare scenario."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/drdo-young-scientist-laboratory-dysl-ct", "content": "Vision\nEmphasis on incorporating cognitive technologies into existing System like classical radar, radio, surveillance systems to make them more agile to the environment.\nMission\nTo develop state of art advanced Cognitive technologies."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/drdo-young-scientist-laboratory-dysl-qt#top", "content": "Vision\nTo become a center of excellence by achieving technical capabilities and self-reliance on Quantum Technologies.\nMission\nTo explore Quantum Technologies and improve the TRL from 1 to 5 and subsequently to 9 in Quantum Computing, Communications and Sensing technologies."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/drdo-young-scientist-laboratory-smart-materials-dysl-sm#top", "content": "Vision\nTo be a pioneer in the field of smart materials and provide technology solutions for defence.\nMission\nAccelerated discovery and insertion of smart materials\nTo provide smart materials solutions for defence sector"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/electronics-radar-development-establishment-lrde#top", "content": "Vision\nTo create a Centre of Excellence in the field of Radar Systems and Technologies fulfilling Nation’s Defence / Security needs.\nQuality Policy\nLRDE is committed to the indigenous development of modern RADAR systems through an effective Quality Management System.\nQuality Objectives\nDevelop modern RADAR systems to meet User requirements.\nEnhance capabilities in Technologies and Systems Engineering.\nImplement Quality Management System and enhance Quality through continual Improvement.\nISO 9001:2015 Certification\nMission\nTo Design and Develop state-of-the-art Radar Systems meeting the current and futuristic requirements of the Tri-Services, Para-Military forces, Intelligence and Strategic Missions.\nTo establish indigenous production capability through Industry partnership to achieve total self-reliance in the field Radars.\nTo promote in-house Research, engage Academia& Industry to build competence towards creating a Centre of Excellence in the field of Radar Technologies.\nTo provide operationalization and life cycle support to the Users.\nProducts\n2D Low Level Light Weight Radar (LLLR): BHARANI MK I\n3 D Medium Range Surveillance Radar for Airforce- Rohini\n3D Low Level Light Weight Radar Aslesha Mk I\n3D Surveillance Radar for Indian Navy -Revathi\nView All\nPhotos\nProducts Gallery\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/gas-turbine-research-establishment-gtre#top", "content": "Vision\nTo be a centre of excellence for aero gas turbine design and development of related technologies.\nMission\nTo design, develop and integrate advance technologies, state of art aero gas turbine engines and their derivatives for defence forces.\nProducts\nAdvanced Full Authority Digital Electronic Controller\nEngine Fuel Control System\nKaveri\nKaveri Core Engine – Kabini\nView All\nPhotos\nPhoto Gallery\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/high-energy-materials-research-laboratory-hemrl#top", "content": "Vision\nBe a centre of excellence in the field of High Energy Materials and associate technologies.\nMission\nDevelop expertise and technologies relating to High Explosives, Propellants and Pyrotechnics and transfer the technologies to industry, enhance the infrastructure and scientific understanding to meet the future challenges.\nProducts\n500 kg GP Bomb\n81 mm Anti-thermal Anti-laser (AT-AL) Smoke Grenade\n84 mm High Temperature Suffocating Smoke (HTSS) Ammunition\nAdvanced Air Defence (AAD) Warhead\nView All\nPhotos\nBIMSTEC MILEX-2018\nWorld Quality Day\nInternational Women’s Day 2019\nHEMRL Raising Day 2019\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/institute-nuclear-medicine-allied-sciences-inmas", "content": "Vision\nThe Vision of INMAS has been identified as to be a center of excellence in biomedical and clinical research with special reference to ionizing radiation.\nMission\nThe Mission of INMAS is clinical research in nuclear medicine and non-invasive imaging methods with a focus on biological radio-protectors and thyroid disorders\nProducts\nINMAS Products"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/institute-technology-management-itm#top", "content": "Vision\nTo be a center of excellence in Technology Management training and research.\nMission\nTo provide world class training in the field of Technology Management.\nTo strive for continuous improvement of faculty, infrastructure and management systems.\nTo carry out research in the areas of Technology Management for enhancing Techno-Managerial skill of human resources.\nPhotos\nVISITORS TO ITM\nMid Career Training Augmentation (MITRA) (18 Apr-13 May 2022)\nInauguration of Advance Work Study Course (AWS-28) on  07 Mar 2022\nOnline Course on R and D Management for Newly Promoted TO ‘C’ during  31 Jan -04 Feb 2022\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/instruments-research-development-establishment-irde", "content": "Vision\nTo achieve excellence in the fields of Optics & Electro-optical Instrumentation with a commitment to provide high quality Instruments.\nMission\nTo design and develop state-of-the-art Night Vision Devices & Thermal Imagers.\nTo design and develop compact Laser Based Instruments.\nTo design and develop Integrated Electro-optical Surveillance and Fire Control Systems.\nTo carry out research in the area of Photonics.\nProducts\nCommander’s TI (MK-II) for T-72 Tanks & BMP II\nCommander’s TI for T-90 Tank\nElectro-Optical Fire Control System for armoured vehicles and naval ships\nGap Measuring Device Mk III\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/integrated-test-range-itr#top", "content": "Vision\nTo be a trusted Integrated Test Facility, delivering reliable and quality services to all customers.\nMission\nTo achieve excellence in service quality and reliability\nTo attain global best practices and become a world class test range\nTo be a technology driven and efficient organization\nTo encourage ideas, talents and value systems\nTo work with Vigour, Dedication and Innovation with Total Customer Satisfaction as the ultimate goal\nTo promote work culture that fosters Individual Growth, Team Spirit and Creativity to overcome challenges and attain goals\nTo contribute towards community development and Nation Building"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/naval-science-technological-laboratory-nstl", "content": "Vision\nTorpedoes, underwater targets and decoys, ship fire control systems and underwater mines with competitive and cutting edge technologies.\nHydrodynamics with expertise for supporting indigenous design of marine vehicles and provide comprehensive facilities.\nStealth technology for naval platforms.\nMission\nDesign, development and evaluation leading to production of Torpedoes, Mines, Targets, Decoys, Fire Control Systems and induction into services and establish test facilities for the same.\nEstablish world-class hydrodynamic test Facilities for evolving Design Criteria through model tests for surface and sub-surface vehicles and torpedoes.\nDevelop Structural Design Capabilities and Materials for mitigation of radar, infrared, magnetic, acoustic and electric signatures leading to stealthier platforms.\nProducts\nAnti Torpedo Decoy System (ATDS)\nAutonomous Underwater Vehicle (AUV)\nHelicoptor Fire Control System\nIntegrated Anti Submarine Warefare Complex\nView All\nPhotos\nYoga Day-2022\nWomens Day-2022\nNational Technology Day-2022\nNational Science Day-2022\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/proof-experimental-establishment-pxe", "content": "Vision\nTransform the range into a world-class dynamic Test & Evaluation centre for armament stores.\nMission\nTest, evaluation and proof of various types of armament stores."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/research-centre-imarat-rci#top", "content": "Vision\nTo be the leader in the development of guided missile systems for our Armed Forces by developing the frontier technologies, multidisciplinary competence and avant-garde infrastructure leading to self-reliance.\nMission\nBe a premiere institute for developing Frontier Technologies in collaboration with Academic institutions & industry.\nFoster Human Resources for professional Excellence.\nOrganize for the induction and production of the guided missile systems on to the Armed forces.\nProducts\nControl Systems Technologies & Products\nFlight Instrumentation Technologies & Products\nImaging Infra-Red (IIR) Seeker systems\nNavigation Technologies & Systems\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/research-development-establishment-rdee#top", "content": "Vision\nTransform R&DE(E) into a world-class Engineering Systems Laboratory through research, innovation and development of state-of-the-art technology and also through collaborative-engineering and continual improvement.\nMission\nDesign and Develop high performance engineering systems, equipment, products and technologies related to:\nMobility and Counter-Mobility Systems\nField Defence and CBRNe Collective Protection Systems\nLaunch Systems for Weapons and Unmanned Aerial Vehicles\nAdvanced Products using Composite Materials\nRobotics and Unmanned Systems\nMicro Electro-Mechanical Systems\nSpecialized Power Systems and Solutions\nSpecialized Engineering Equipment and Solutions.\nProducts\n5m Short-span Bridging System (SSBS)\nAir-storage and delivery system for ‘Aditya'\nAircraft-arrester barrier system\nBar Mine Layer (BML) Mk-II\nView All\nPhotos\nSports Activities\nGreen Initiatives\nSwachh Bharat\nRepublic Day Celebration at RDE School\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/scientific-analysis-group-sag", "content": "Vision\nTo make Scientific Analysis Group the finest Cryptology and Information Security Laboratory in the World.\nMission\nTo develop tools and techniques based on contemporary Mathematics, Computer Science and Electronics & Communication for Analysis of Security and IT products.\nTo build generalized as well as domain/system specific analytical algorithms and tools.\nTo establish state-of-art facilities for electronic probing, communication signal & protocol analysis.\nPhotos\nSAG received Titanium Trophy 2014\nMs. Navneet Gaba received Scientist of the year award 2016\nMr. Sanchit Gupta received Young Scientist of the year award 2016\nMr. Aditya Raj received Best Performance Award 2016\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/solid-state-physics-laboratory-sspl#top", "content": "Vision\nBe the centre of excellence in Research and Development of Semiconductor Materials, Microelectronics Devices and Nanotechnology\nMission\nDevelop semiconductor materials and electronic devices/components for Optoelectronics/ microwave/ sensor applications and establish production centres thereof.\nEstablish scientific knowledge base and build world class scientific research teams/leaders for futuristic cutting edge technologies.\nStrengthen scientific interaction with academia, industry and international centres of excellence.\nProducts\nAdvanced Semiconductor Products & Technology\nAlGaN/GaN HEMT\nAlGaN/GaN HEMT Processed Wafer\nAlGaN/GaN Multifinger HEMT\nView All\nPhotos\nRajbhasha Activities\nSports Events\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/terminal-ballistics-research-laboratory-tbrl#top", "content": "Vision\nTBRL envisage self-reliance in the development of technologies related to warheads and provide state-of–the-art diagnostics facilities for assessment of terminal effects of armaments systems.\nMission\nDevelop technologies and products related to warheads.\nProvides state-of-the-art diagnostics facilities for test and evaluation of armaments systems.\nBuild strong technology base in the country in the field of armaments by providing requisite infrastructures and committed quality manpower\nProducts\nBaffle Range"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/labs-and-establishments/vehicles-research-and-development-establishment-vrde", "content": "Vision\nTo get transformed into a centre of excellence in the field of Light Tracked combat Vehicle, Specialist Wheeled vehicle and Unmanned Vehicles to provide indigenous solutions to Armed Forces for the mobility of their weapons and equipment’s and also to LIC (Low Intensity Conflict) operations.\nTo provide total solution to Defence and Automotive Industry for all their homologation and developmental testing needs through continuous evolution of the NCAT (National Centre for Automotive Testing) into a world class test facility.\nMission\nResearch, Development, Trial and Evaluation of :\nCombat and Combat Support Vehicles – Wheeled.\nCombat and Combat Support Vehicles - Light Tracked (Up to 25t GVW).\nSpecialist Vehicles including Strategic Missile Program.\nUnmanned Ground Vehicles.\nEngines for UAVs (Rotary and Reciprocating).\nContinuous upgradation & Augmentation of Test Facilities at NCAT.\nProducts\n180 Hp Diesel Engine for UAV\n70 T Tank Transporter for MBT Arjun\nCBRN Recce Vehicle Mk-II (Tracked)\nInfantry Protected Mobility Vehicle (IPMV)\nView All"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/life-sciences-research-board/about-us#top", "content": "Format for submission of ‘Concept Note’ to LSRB\nFormat of New project proposal submission\nVision\nTo expand and deepen the knowledge base in the area of life sciences in order to harness and nurture the research talent in the academic institutions of the country to meet the national needs of Defence Services.\nMission\nTo catalyse the needed cross-fertilization of ideas and experiences between scientific community in technical fields to provide the required support to soldier in operations and the knowledge for integrating “human factors” to optimize his combat effectiveness.\nCharter\nThe Life Sciences Research Board (LSRB) of Defence Research & Development Organisation (DRDO) was set up to support and strengthen research base in the area of life sciences through projects under Grant-in-Aid Scheme to meet the national needs of Defence Services. The scheme is coordinated through five specialist panels:-\nLife Support & Biomedical Devices (LSBD)\nSoldier Health & Drug Development (SH&DD)\nPhysiology of Extreme Environment & Behavioural Sciences (PEE&BS)\nBiotechnology and Bioremediation (BTB)\nFood, Agriculture & Bioprospecting (FAB)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/life-sciences-research-board/concept#top", "content": "DRDO\nSr. No.\nAppointment\nAppointee Institute/Organisation\n1\nChairman\nProf Ashutosh Sharma, President, INSA,  Institute Chair Professor, IIT Kanpur, and\nFormer Secretary to the Government of India, DST\n2\nCo-Chairman\nDirector General (Technology Management)\nO/o DG (TM),  DRDO, HQ\nDRDO Bhawan, New Delhi\n3\nCo-Chairman\nDirector General (Life Sciences)\nO/o DG (LS),  DRDO HQ\nDRDO Bhawan, New Delhi\n4\nMember\nSecretary, ICMR/Representative\nIndian Council of Medical Research (ICMR), PB No.4911, Ansari Nagar, New Delhi\n5\n-do-\nSecretary, ICAR/Representative\nIndian Council of Agricultural Sciences (ICAR), Krishi Bhawan, New Delhi\n6\n-do-\nAddl. Financial Advisor (SM) & JS, DRDO Bhawan, New Delhi\n7\n-do-\nDG, AFMS/Representative\nO/o DGAFMS, M-Block, New Delhi\n8\n-do-\nAddl. DGAFMS (MR, H & Trg) O/o DGAFMS, M-Block, New Delhi\n9\n-do-\nIFA (R&D),\nDRDO Bhawan,\nNew Delhi\n10\n-do-\nDirector, NII/Representative,\nNational Institute of Immunology (NII),\nNew Delhi\n11\n-do-\nDirector, CFTRI/Representative\nCentral Food Technological Research Institute (CFTRI), Mysore\n12\n-do-\nHead, Radiation Biology & Health Sciences Division,\nBhabha Atomic Research Centre (BARC),  Bombay\n13\n-do-\nExternal Expert from Academia (02 Nos.)\n14\n-do-\nChairman, Spl Panel on “Physiology of Extreme Environment & Behavioral Sciences (PEE&BS)”\n15\n-do-\nChairman,  Spl Panel on “Biotechnology and Bioremediation (BTB) ”\n16\n-do-\nChairman, Spl Panel on “Soldier Health & Drug Development  (SH&DD) ”\n17\n-do-\nChairman, Spl Panel on “Life Support & Biomedical Devices (LSBD) ”\n18\n-do-\nChairman, Spl Panel on “Food Science, Hill Agriculture, Bio-fuels & Bioresources  (FSH&ABB) ”\n19\nOne Director from any Life Sciences lab\n20\nMember Secretary\nMember Secretary, LSRB\nDRDO HQ, DRDO Bhawan, New Delhi\n21\n-do-\nChairman, Spl Panel on “Soldier Health & Drug Development  (SH&DD) ”\n22\n-do-\nChairman, Spl Panel on “Life Support & Biomedical Devices (LSBD)”\n23\n-do-\nChairman, Spl Panel on “Food Science, Hill Agriculture, Bio-fuels & Bioresources (FSH&ABB)”\nOne Director from any Life Sciences lab\n24\nMember Secretary\nMember Secretary, LSRB\nDRDO HQ, DRDO Bhawan, New Delhi"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/life-sciences-research-board/contact-us#top", "content": "Dr. Gaurav Mittal,\nMember Secretary,\nLIFE SCIENCES RESEARCH BOARD (LSRB)\nDefence Research & Development Organization\nMinistry of Defence\nRoom No. 409, 4rd Floor, DRDO HQrs Annexe,\nOld LASTEC Building, METCALFE HOUSE COMPLEX,\nDelhi-110054\nEmail ID\n: lsrb[dot]hqr[at]gov[dot]in"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/life-sciences-research-board/eligibility#top", "content": "Who may Submit\nGrants are offered to IITs, universities, colleges, departments, laboratories approved research Institutes, eminent scientists working in reputed R&D Organizations / Institutes with well established R&D facilities, Government and non-Government sector etc.\nWhere / Whom to Submit\nMember Secretary\n,\nLIFE SCIENCES RESEARCH BOARD (LSRB)\nDefence Research & Development Organization\nMinistry of Defence\nRoom No. 409, 4th Floor, DRDO HQrs Annexe,\nOld LASTEC Building, METCALFE HOUSE COMPLEX,\nDelhi-110054\nEmail ID\n: lsrb[dot]hqr[at]gov[dot]in"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/life-sciences-research-board/formats#top", "content": "List of Ongoing Projects\nDRDO\nS No\nProject Title\nPI & Institution Name\nLSRB Panel\n1\nHybrid Ocnis for food technology\nDr. K. Rajagopal, CFTRI, Mysore, Karnataka\nFAB\n2\nDevelopment and Characterization of second generation chimeric antigen receptor T-Cell tagged with riboflavin photo- Activation to specifically target adherent cancers, using patient derived HSCs Maintained under microgravity\nDr. Madhulika Dixit, IIT Madras, Chennai\nSH&DD\n3\nPhytotherapeutics mechanism against aflatoxin induced neurodegenerative disorders\nDr. Sadhna Srivastava, Jiwaji University, Gwalior, M.P.\nBTB\n4\nInvestigating role of serum magnesium in patho-physiology of heat illness and susceptibility among Indian population\nDr. Kalpana Kumari Barhwal, Bhubaneswar, Odisha\nPEE&BS\n5\nDevelopment of a scalable route for the manufacture of Prussian blue insoluble of pharmaceutical grade an FDA approved decorporation drug\nDr. Y V Madhavi, NIPER, Balanagar, Hyderabad\nSH&DD\n6\nDevelopment of new & novel radiation dosimetric OSL materials by ion implantation technique and chemical methods for improved dosimetry\nDr. Pratik Kumar, AIIMS, New Delhi\nSH&DD\n7\nEvaluation of locally available phytogenics as feed additives\nDr. Mohd. Tufail Banday, SKUAST-Kashmir, Srinagar, J&K\nFAB\n8\nDesign and development of natural hepato protective churnam for army personnel working in extreme conditions\nDr. Y Swarnalatha, Sathyabama University, Chennai\nFAB\n9\nStress related health problem management of college students by yoga with nutraceutical interventions\nDr. Dilip Kumar Nandi, Raja Narendra Lal Khan Womens College, West Bengal\nPEE&BS\n10\nCorrelation between psychological and physiological parameters of stress among staff and students an empirical study\nDr.Neeraj Kaushik,NIT, Kurukshetra, Haryana\nPEE&BS\n11\nHigh altitude-hypoxia mediates thrombosis in soldiers: inhibition of autophagy as a strategy to combat high altitude-low oxygen induced thrombosis\nDr. Rajdeep Chowdhury, Birla Institute of Technology and Science, Rajasthan\nPEE&BS\n12\nDevelopment of wearable kinesiological system using sensorized glove and existing motion capture system for uper limb kinematics and kinetics analysis during lifting tasks\nDr. Rajdeep Ojha, Christian Medical College, Vellore, Tamil Nadu\nLS&BD\n13\nDevelopment of thermally conductive elastomeric composites for liquid cooled garments to mitigate thermal stress\nDr. T Niranjan Prabhu, M.S. Ramaiah University of Applied Sciences, , Karnataka\nLS&BD\n14\nMesoporous antibacterial bioactive glass microsphere impregnatednon woven surgical cotton gauze based haemostatic dressing for profusely bleeding military wounds\nDr. Jui Chakraborty, CSIR- Cenrat Glass and Ceramic Research Institute,Kolkata,West Bengal\nSH&DD\n15\nA multilayered regenerative scaffold engineered to heal deep wound by mimicking anatomical architecture of natural tissue\nDr. Debrupa Lahiri, IIT, Roorkee, Uttarakhand\nSH&DD\n16\nScreening for drugs against the endoplasmic reticulum stress-responsive Rta proteins of Candida albicans for antifungal therapy: implications in wound infections\nDr. Sneh Lata Panwar, Jawaharlal Nehru University, New Delhi\nSH&DD\n17\nTargeting Redox-Regulated Signaling system for Radioprotection using Grape proanthocyanidins: Amolecular Approach for product development\nDr Krishna Das Saha, CSIR-Indian Institute of Chemical Biology , West Bengal\nSH&DD\n18\nDesign and development of affinity based sensors for the deectionof radiological compounds in point of CBRN emergencies using ZnO NPs functionalized by amidoxine and mugenic acid\nDr. Raj Mohan Balakrishnan, NIT-Surathal, Mangalore, Karnataka\nSH&DD\n20\n\"Non-Contact electrocardiogram system for continuous monitoring of cardiac system and to evaluate the armed forces personnel performance\"\"\"\nDr. N.R. Raajan, SASTRA Deemed to be University, Thanjavur, T.N.\nLS&BD\n21\n\"Development of a standard method for identification of dope dyed and exhaust dyed polyster fibers/fabrices\"\" \"\nDr. Prasanta Kumar Panda, The Bombay Textile Research Association, Ghatkopar (W), Mumbai\nLS&BD\n22\nDevelopment of Silver and Gold Nanoprobes for the optical and electrochemical monitoring of H2S, Cysteine and glutathione in human blood\nDr. Kaushal Kumar Upadhyay, Banaras Hindu University, Varanasi, U.P.\nPEE&BS\n23\n\"Development of rapid point-of-care diagnostic kit for infections associated with combat war wound and sepsis in armed forces\"\"\"\nDr. Ruchi Jain Dey, BITS Pilani, Talangana\nBTB\n24\nExploring Novel Biomarkers in Indian Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension Patients Through Transcriptomics Approach\nDr. Rashmi Rana, Sri Ganga Ram Hospital, New Delhi\nPEE&BS\n25\nDevelopment of AI Based predictive algorithms for bionic hand action recognitions\nDr. Govind R. Kadambi, M.S. Ramaiah University of Applied Sciences, Bengaluru, Karnataka\nLS&BD\n26\nNano fabric conditioner to impart antimicrobial property to nomex or high performance fabrics\nDr. G.S. Hikku, Chettinad Hospital & Research Institution, Tamil Nadu\nLS&BD\n27\nDesign Synthesis and evaluation of sugar conjugated pyridine oximes as reactivators of oganophosphorous nerve agent inhibited acetylcholinesterase\nDr Sabita Nayak, Ravenshaw University, Cuttack, Orrisa\nBTB\n28\nDevelopment of optoelectronic biochemical sensor based on calyx systems for the rapid detection of warfare agents\nDr V.K. Jain, Gujarat University, Ahmedabad\nBTB\n29\nHaemostatic Microcapsules\nDr. SomenathGanguly, IIT, Kharagpur\nSH&DD\n30\nProbiotics mediated host bioenergetic health modulation as a novel approach to the management of microbial infections\nDr. Vikram Saini, AIIMS, New Delhi\nSH&DD\n31\nAutomated Cognitive metrics classification framework to improve himan machine collaboration\nDr. Partha Pratim Roy, IIT Roorkee, Uttarakhand\nSH&DD\n32\nHuman performance enhancement via tDCS in VR and performance forecasting via machine learning methods\nDr. Varun Dutt, IIT Mandi, Himachal Pradesh\nSH&DD\n33\nDetection and Management of Pain: Pain to Pleasure by neuromodulation\nProf. SanjitDey, University of Calcutta, Kolkata\nSH&DD\n34\nDevelopment Alginate-Silver Nano-composite embedded with Adipose-Derived Stem Cells for the Healing of Deep Burn Wounds\nDr. Everette Jacob Remingtin Nelson, Vellor Institute of Technology, Tamil Nadu\nSH&DD\n35\nIntelligent Video Based Human Activity Analysis\nDr. Sunita Virant Dhavale, DIAT, Pune\nDIPAS\n36\nDesign and Development of an advanced 3D woven honeycomb composite structure shell with high energy absorbent liner for air crew helmet\nDr. Bijoya Kumar Behera, IIT, Delhi\nLS&BD\n37\nProductization and clinical evaluation of Bio-potential signal analysis system for mobility assistance\nDr M. Sasikala, Anna University, Chennai\nLS&BD\n38\nAssessment of speech, communication, oral motor function and its clinical determinants among the patients with Post Burn facial and neck contractures\nMrs. Sindhusha Chandran, JIPMER, Pondicherry\nSH&DD\n39\nIISc-DRDO-INMAS Collaboration to explore biomedical applications of shockwaves\nProf. Dipshikha Chakravortty, Indian Institute of Science, Bangalore, Karnataka\nSH&DD\n40\nMolecular Investigation in Renin Angiotensin Aldosterone System (RAAS) in Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) and Hypertension\nDr. Bhuvnesh Kumar, Sharda University, Greater Noida, U.P.\nPEE&BS\n41\nDesign and Development of smart nanomaterial-based biosensors for pesticide detection in food\nDr. PratibhaKumari, Deshbandhu College, University of Delhi, New Delhi\nFAB\n42\nTesting On-Spot Food Quality for the Defense Personnel and Combating the Counterfeiters using Simple Fluorophores\nDr. Manab Chakravarty, BITS Pilani, Hyderabad\nFAB\n43\nHand Held Electrochemical Platform for biomedical applications with particular emphasis on stress marker detection\nDr. A. Subbiah, CSIR- Central Electrochemical Research Institute (CECRI), Tamil Nadu\nLS&BD\n44\nUnderstanding the Molecular Events Involved in Cellular Responses to Heat Stress\nDr. Ashu Bhan Tiku, Jawaharlal Nehru Unviersity, New Delhi\nPEE&BS\n45\nDevelopment of RASAR - based Expert Systems for Ligand-Based Virtual Screening of Drug Like Substances against Various Toxicity Endpoints in a Non-animal Alternative Approach\nProf. Kunal Roy, Jadavpur University, Kolkata\nSH&DD\n46\nSynthesis and Biological Evaluation of New Clickable Ethynylestradiol-Folic acid based Dual Targeting 68GA radiolabeled PET Probes for Breast Cancer Imaging\nDr. Jasleen Kaur, Amity University, Uttar Pradesh\nSH&DD\n47\nDevelopment of reusable macrocyclic probes for detedction and separation of radioactive metal ions\nDr. Satish Kumar, St. Stephen's College (University of Delhi), New Delhi\nSH&DD\n48\nIdentification of key regulators and their controlling mechanism in a combinatorial Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis Network: An Integrated Bioinformatics Analysis\nDr. Shazia Haider, Jaypee Institute of information Technology, Noida Uttar Pradesh\nSH&DD"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/life-sciences-research-board/institutions-interacted#top", "content": "Indian Institutes of Technology, Delhi.\nIndian Institutes of Technology, Guwahati.\nIndian Institutes of Technology, Kharagpur.\nIndian Institute of Technology, Banaras Hindu University, Varanasi.\nUniversity of Delhi, Delhi\nUniversity of Hyderabad, Hyderabad\nUniversity of Allahabad, U.P.\nTezpur University, Assam\nJiwaji University, Gwalior, M.P.\nGuru Jambheshwar Univ. Of Sci. & Tech. Hisar, Haryana\nAnna University, Chennai\nJSS College of Arts, Commerce and Science, Mysuru, Karnataka\nICAR-Indian Institute of Agricultural Research, New Delhi\nICAR-Central Institute of Post Harvest Engineering & Technology, Ludhiana\nCSIR- Institute of Genomics & Integrative Biology, New Delhi\nCSIR-Central Glass and Ceramic Reserach Institute, Kolkata\nCSIR-Indian Institute of Chemical Biology, Kolkata\nNational Institute of Mental Health and Neurosciences (NIMHANS), Bangalore\nIndian Institute of Science (IISc), Bangalore\nAll India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS), New Delhi\nAll India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS), Bhubaneswar\nRavishankar Shukla Univ., Chhattisgarh\nIndian Institute of Crop Processing Technology, Tamil Nadu\nCentre of Biomedical Research, Lucknow"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/life-sciences-research-board/norms-tot#top", "content": "Biotechnology & Bioremediation (BTB) Panel\nPanel Chairman :\nDr. Manmohan Parida, Director, DRDE, Gwalior\nPanel Members :\nDr. J. K. Batra, NII, New Delhi\nDr. R.P. Singh, IIT Roorkee\nDr. G.B.K.S. Prasad, Jiwaji Univ., Gwalior\nDr. Anil Kumar Gaur, GBPUAT, Uttarakhand\nDirector / Rep. from INMAS\nDirector / Rep. from DIPAS\nSpl Panel Member Secretary (Scientist),  DRDE, Gwalior\nPhysiology of Extreme Environment & Behavioral Sciences (PEE&BS) Panel\nPanel Chairman :\nDr. Rajeev Varshney, Director, DIPAS, Delhi\nPanel Members :\nDr. Rana Pratap Singh, Professor of Cancer Biology, School of Life Sciences, Jawaharlal Nehru University, New Delhi\nDr. Anita Kamra Verma, Professor, Nanobiotechnology Lab, Department of Zoology, Kirori Mal College, University of Delhi, Delhi\nDr. Latika Mohan,Professor of Physiology, AIIMS, Rishikesh, Uttarakhand\nDr. Meenakshi Chaswal, Professor, ABVIMS & RML Hospital, Delhi\nDirector / Rep. from INMAS\nDirector / Rep. from DIPR\nMember Secretary, LSRB/Rep\nSpl Panel Member Secretary (Scientist), DIPAS, Delhi\nLife Support & Biomedical Devices (LSBD) Panel\nPanel Chairman :\nDr. R Indu Shekhar, Director, DEBEL, Bangalore\nPanel Members :\nProf. N.R. Jagannathan, AIIMS, New Delhi\nDr. G. Ravindran, Anna Univ., Chennai\nDr. Rama Subba Reddy, IIT Madras\nProf. D. Sukumar, Sri Jayachamrajendra College of Engineering, Mysore\nDirector / Rep. from DRDE\nA senior scientist at the level of Joint Director\nSpl Panel Member Secretary (Scientist), DEBEL, Bangalore\nSoldier Health & Drug Development (SH&DD) Panel\nPanel Chairman :\nDr. Sudhir Chandna , Director, INMAS, Delhi\nPanel Members :\nProf. R. K. Seth (Retd), Department of Zoology, Delhi University\nProf. Pawan K. Dhar, School of Biotechnology, JNU\nProf. Surender Singh, Dept. of Pharmacology, AIIMS, New Delhi\nDr. Rakesh Kumar Parashar, Dept. of Chemistry, Delhi University\nDr. Ritu Kulshreshtha, Professor, Vallabhbhai Patel Chest Institute, Delhi\nDirector / Rep. from DIPAS\nDirector / Rep. from DRDE\nMember Secretary, LSRB / Rep\nSpl Panel Member Secretary (Scientist), INMAS, Delhi\nFood, Agriculture & Bio-prospecting (FAB) Panel\nPanel Chairman :\nDr. D.V. Kamboj, Director, DRL, Tezpur\nPanel Members :\nDr. Debendra C. Baruah, Professor, Tezpur University, Assam\nDr. S.C. Deka, Professor , Tezpur University, Assam\nDr. B.N. Hazarika, Dean and Professor, College of Horticulture & Forestry, Central Agricultural University, Pasighat Arunachal Pradesh\nDr. R.K. Goyal, Director Research, Maharana Pratap Horticultural University, Karnal, Haryana\nDr. V.S. Chauhan, Chief Scientist, CFTRI, Mysore, Karnataka\nDirector / Rep. from DIHAR\nDirector / Rep. from DFRL\nDirector / Rep. from DIBER\nMember Secretary, LSRB / Rep\nSpl Panel Member Secretary (Scientist), DRL, Tezpur, Assam"},
