{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/index.php/transfer-technologies", "content": "Transfer of Technology (ToT)\nDRDO Policy for Transfer of Technology 2025\nDownload PDF 4.6 MB\nCounter Covid 19 Technologies\nCategory A Technologies (Military Technologies)\nThese are the technologies for which Indian Armed Forces/ MHA/ other Govt. agencies (both central & state) are the only end users. Category ‘A’ technologies are military technologies and are referred to as “MILTECH”. Export of Cat ‘A’ technologies is subjected to approval process of DRDO and MoD, Govt of India. ToT to the industry is done directly by DRDO for all Category ‘A’ technologies.\nCategory A Technologies ready for ToT\nCategory-A Technologies ready for ToT to Indian Industies\n(*) Additional / Balance Licenses\nDRDO\nTechnology\nLAB\nNo of License Available\nDate of Publishing\nAir Retainable type Inflatable Aircraft Decoy technology (InfADec)\n86 KB\nDLJ\n03\n22/05/2025\nREMOCON\n177 KB\nINMAS\n04\n22/05/2025\nCartridge Electric Operating Fire Extinguisher (EOFE)\n250 KB\nARDE\n03\n09/05/2025\nManufacturing of shaped miniature Detonating Cord\n184 KB\nHEMRL\n03\n06/05/2025\nImprovised Explosive Device (IED) Containment Vessel\n169 KB\nR&DE (E)\n03*\n17/04/2025\nMounting and Support Equipment for Multi Spectral Camouflage Net (MSCN)\n3.5 MB\nDMSRDE\n06*\n08/04/2025\nG-Band Coupled Cavity Traveling-Wave Tube (G-Band CCTWT)\n210 KB\nMTRDC\n02\n26/03/2025\nCBRN Resuscitator (Manual)\n115 KB\nDEBEL\n06\n25/03/2025\nModular Bridging System\n82 KB\nR&DE(E)\n01\n25/03/2025\nPinaka Mark-I Rocket System\n75 KB\nARDE\n01\n20/03/2025\nPinaka Mark-II Rocket System\n75 KB\nARDE\n01\n20/03/2025\nFuel Cell based Hybrid Power Supply (FC-HPSS)\n156 KB\nR&DE (E)\n06\n12/03/2025\nClosed Vessel Test System\n86 KB\nHEMRL\n10\n12/03/2025\nPinaka Multi Barrel Launcher and Battery Command Post (BCP)\n74 KB\nARDE\n02\n21/02/2025\nManufacturing of 500kg Pre-fragmented (PF) Bomb\n95 KB\nARDE\n03\n21/02/2025\nMilitary Combat Par