{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/infantry-protected-mobility-vehicle-ipmv", "content": "Back to Listing\nInfantry Protected Mobility Vehicle (IPMV)\nLabs\nVehicles Research and Development Establishment (VRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nWheeled 8x8 Configuration, 600 hp engine, fully automatic transmission, 7.62 mm RCWS, Ballistic protection with composite add-on Armour & blast protection for the crew. Order directly placed by Indian Army for Infantry Protected Mobility Vehicle (IPMV) after successful trials of WhAP at Leh-Ladhak region."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/inflatable-structure-radome", "content": "Back to Listing\nInflatable Structure (Radome)\nLabs\nAerial Delivery Research and Development Establishment (ADRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nInflatable structure has been designed and developed indigenously by ADRDE with an objective to serve as a shelter to provide controlled environment for effective and continuous functioning of expensive electronic and strategic systems. The inflatable structure consists of hemispherical envelope of 80 feet base diameter, airlock tunnel, air blowers, air conditioners, electrical control system and emergency power backup system. The hemispherical envelope is fabricated with electro-magnetic transparent coated fabrics specially designed to sustain harsh and highly degrading environmental conditions for desired operational life. The electrical control system monitors the wind conditions and maintains pressure and temperature inside the structure within desired limits using heavy duty air blowers and air conditioners respectively. The system is operational 24X7 meeting all the requirements of the customer."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/integrated-anti-submarine-warefare-complex", "content": "Back to Listing\nIntegrated Anti Submarine Warefare Complex\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nSalient Features\nInterfaces to present Weapon and Sensor fit of SNF class of ships\nGenerates Fire Control Solution for Launching Rockets (RB 600) & Torpedoes by performing Target Tracking using state-of-the-art CMA Algorithms\nCompleted FATS & Ground Trials at ASW School Kochi. Installed on INS RANJIT for sea trials\nIndigenous System costs Rs 4 Cr as against Rs 30 Cr for an Imported System"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/integrated-coastal-surveillance-system-icss#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nIntegrated Coastal Surveillance System (ICSS)\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nThe Integrated Coastal Surveillance System (ICSS) is a system developed for guarding India's coastal territory for quick detection, location and monitoring of movements of suspect dhows, motorized and traditional vessels in a given controlled area, round the clock without any physical presence."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/integrated-multi-function-site-imfs-hhti-lrf#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nIntegrated Multi-Function Site (IMFS) (HHTI with LRF)\nLabs\nInstruments Research & Development Establishment (IRDE)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/ipr#top", "content": "Objective\nTo provide boost to Indian industries and Defence industries, through free access to Indian patents by DRDO.\nLicense Fee and Royalty\nThe license for the use of patent shall be granted on zero license fees as well as zero royalty payment.\nProcedure for use of DRDO Patents by Indian Industry\n2867 KB\nDRDO Policy for Use of Patents by Indian Industry\n212 KB\nDRDO IPR Policy 2016\n610 KB\nList of Patents\n798 KB"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/ir-guided-missile-tester#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nIR Guided Missile Tester\nLabs\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nIR Guided Missile Tester (IRGMT) is a system for performing in situ functionality tests of R 73 IR Guided Missile onboard the LCA. It is a calibrated IR source that generates the signatures of an aircraft as seen by the IR Guided Missiles. It is a universal test system and can be used for testing other IR guided missiles as well."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/ir-signature-suppression#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nIR Signature Suppression\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nInfrared Signature Suppression (IRSS) devices are fitted in the exhaust system of ship propulsion and power generation equipment that keeps exhaust metal ducts at considerable low temperature and cools the exhaust. The device has been inducted into the services."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/iron-removal-unit-3000-lhr-mk-iii", "content": "Back to Listing\nIron Removal Unit (3000 L/hr, MK III)\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nWater quality of most parts of NE region of India is ferruginous in nature. To provide iron free drinking water, DRL had developed Iron Removal Unit (IRU) which needs no electricity to run. The product is available in two variants: 300 L/Hr and 3000 L/Hr. It can reduce iron from 40 ppm to <0.3 ppm in water\nMain Features of IRU, Capacity: 3000 L/hr\nConsists of one aeration system, an aeration cover and six filtration chambers\nMade of mild steel\nRemoves iron from 54 to<0.3 ppm (WHO/BIS limit)\nIt brings down the TDS, pH, Turbidity, Conductivity of filtered water to the desirable limit\nFlow rate of output water: 3000 L/hr\nNon-electrical system"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/iron-removal-unit-iru", "content": "Back to Listing\nIron Removal Unit (IRU)\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nWater quality of most parts of NE region of India is ferruginous in nature. To provide iron free drinking water, DRL had developed Iron Removal Unit (IRU) which needs no electricity to run. The product is available in two variants: 300 L/Hr and 3000 L/Hr. It can reduce iron from 40 ppm to <0.3 ppm in water\nMain Features of IRU, Capacity:300L/hr\nRemoves excess iron from contaminated/ferruginous water\n\nStructure: Cylindrical; Made of FRP\n\nRemoves iron from 40 ppm to <0.3 ppm (Desirable WHO/BIS)\n\nReduce turbidity to desirable limits\n\nFiltration rate: 300 L/hr (approx.)\n\nNon-electrical system"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/join-drdo#top", "content": "Your browser does not support the video tag.\nRegister Here"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/kaveri-core-engine-kabini", "content": "Back to Listing\nKaveri Core Engine – Kabini\nLabs\nGas Turbine Research Establishment (GTRE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nKabini engine comprising of high pressure compressor, combustor and high pressure turbine is used for demonstrating hot end parts technology and study the aero-mechanical behaviour of High Pressure spool of the kaveri engine."},
