{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/director/defence-institute-high-altitude-research-dihar", "content": "Dr Om Prakash Chaurasia\nScientist ‘G’, Director\nDr Om Prakash Chaurasia, Scientist ‘G’, has taken over as Director, Defence Institute of High Altitude Research (DIHAR), Leh-Ladakh from 15th Feb 2017."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/director/defence-institute-physiology-allied-sciences-dipas", "content": "Shri Devakanta Pahad Singh\nDirector, Defence Institute of Physiology & Allied Sciences (DIPAS)\nShri Devakanta Pahad Singh, Scientist G has been appointed as Director DIPAS w.e.f. 01 Feb 2025."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/director/defence-institute-psychological-research-dipr", "content": "Dr. Arunima Gupta\nScientist 'G' and Director, DIPR\nDr Arunima Gupta\n, Scientist ‘G’ assumed the charge as Director, Defence Institute of Psychological Research (DIPR), DRDO w.e.f. 02 May 2023.\nDr Gupta is acclaimed for her significant contributions in the areas of personality assessment and military psychology during her distinguished career spanning over three and half decades. In the year 1988, she joined DIPR, DRDO and started her professional journey as a young psychologist after undergoing initial training at DIPR and Air Force Selection Board, Dehradun.\nShe played a pioneering role in the development of selection system for women entry in the armed forces and introduction of two stage selection system. Her leadership in guiding research endeavours, continuous training of assessors and standardisation of selection system was instrumental for evolving ingenious solutions & strengthening psychological support to the Indian Armed Forces. The spin-offs of her research work has benefitted Tri-services, Central Armed Police Forces, security agencies and other civilian organisations of national repute.\nShe coordinated several research projects and training programmes, initiated collaborations with Academia & also significantly contributed in international joint collaborations. As an expert member in various selection committees of Indian Armed Forces and advisory member of study groups, she was vital in formulation of progressive policies & envisioning futuristic research areas.\nShe is a post graduate in Psychology from HNB Garhwal University, Uttarakhand and received her PhD in psychology from Bharathiar University. She is a Life Member of various academic and professional societies such as Indian Science Congress Association, Indian Academy of Applied Psychology and Indian Academy of Social Sciences. She co-edited books, authored publications in reputed journals, national and international conferences, authored technical reports/manuals/guides & contributed chapters in many Books.\nIn recognition of her sustained R&D contributions, she has been conferred with DRDO National Science Day Oration award and Technology Group Award."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/director/defence-laboratory-dlj", "content": "Sh. V Sachithananda Shenoi\nDirector, Defence Laboratory Jodhpur (DLJ)\nSh. V Sachithananda Shenoi\nOutstanding Scientist has been appointed as Director DLJ on 11 November 2024."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/director/defence-materials-and-stores-research-and-development-establishment-dmsrde", "content": "Dr. Mayank Dwivedi\nOutstanding Scientist and Director, Defence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/director/defence-metallurgical-research-laboratory-dmrl#top", "content": "Dr. R Balamuralikrishnan\nOutstanding Scientist & Director, Defence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nDr. R. Balamuralikrishnan\n, Outstanding Scientist / Scientist ‘H’, has taken over as Director, Defence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL), Hyderabad on 31 Jan 2023.\nDr. Balamuralikrishnan obtained his B. Tech. in Metallurgical Engineering from IIT-Madras in 1991, and his M.S. (1992) and Ph.D. (1998) in Materials Science and Engineering from Carnegie Mellon University, Pittsburgh, USA.  Following a three-year post-doctoral stint, also at CMU, he joined DMRL as Scientist D in 2001.\nHis research interests include the physical metallurgy of high-performance steels and nickel base superalloys, with a strong emphasis on advanced microstructural characterization and establishing/understanding the processing-structure-property correlations in these important engineering materials. He is also interested in applying modelling and simulation tools to study materials and processes. He has first-hand experience of 25+ years in working with speciality steels, across the entire spectrum from concept-to-product.  His work has been influential in establishing the entire ecosystem, starting from lab scale scientific studies to industrial scale production and certification for final use,for the manufacture of speciality steels for naval construction.He has a strong interest in fostering/enabling interactions between academia, R&D institutions and the industry sector towards transitioning concepts to (successful) products.He has delivered nearly 100 keynote/invited talks at various R&D institutions, academia, industries, Government bodies and conferences.\nDr. Balamuralikrishnan has received the DRDO Agni Award (Team member) for Excellence in Self-Reliance in 2005, Hubert I. Aaronson Fellowship from the Indian Institute of Science in 2010, DRDO National Science Day Oration Silicon Medal in 2011, Metallurgist of the Year Award by the Ministry of Steel in 2017, and Outstanding Researcher (Steel) in an Academic Institute and R&D Labs Award by Indian Steel Association in 2019."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/director/defence-research-development-establishment-drde", "content": "Dr. Manmohan Parida, Outstanding Scientist\nDirector, Defence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)"},
