{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/interaction-with-other-labs/electronics-radar-development-establishment-lrde", "content": "Inter-Cluster\nLRDE is one of the major labs of ECS Cluster. LRDE has developed Radar Systems as part of Projects/Programmes of Labs of other Clusters viz. Aero, MSS, NS&M, A&CE .\nThe areas of joint development include development of Radar Systems for Airborne Platforms, SAM Systems, Coastal Surveillance and Ballistic Missile Defence.\nIntra-Cluster\nLRDE has interaction with ECS Cluster Labs for its various projects . Areas of joint development include Electro Optic Tracking System, Passive Emitter Trackers etc.,\nIndustry\nLRDE has also made a mark in the area of private partnership and expanded its vendor base, wherein various vendors for realization of the Radar subsystems have been successfully established. LRDE has been enabling the Govt Policy of ‘Make in India’ since a long time through Vendor development for Radar Subsystem realization. The Lab practices concurrent system engineering, R&D – Industry Partnership with Professional approach to Technology and Project Management.\nAcademia\nLRDE has continuous interaction with academia for addressing futuristic technologies through collaborative design & development to cut down development time and realise ‘design to cost’ production ready systems.\nLRDE has been using Knowledge base from the academic institutes in India for providing Research Services in the form of CARS –“Contract for Acquisition of Research Services”. Currently, LRDE is currently pursuing eight CARS projects from different Universities & Institutes.\nSr. No.\nCollege/Institution Involved\n1\nNational Engineering College Kovilpatti Tamil Nadu - 628503\n2\nIndian Institute of Science\nBangalore - 560012\n3\nCORI, PES University Bangalore\n4\nDepartment of ECE National Institute of Tech, Surathkal Mangalore-575025\n5\nIDST Bangalore- 560093\n6\nElectrical Engineering Department IIT, Mumbai"},
