ig\nCOAS's Commendation Card\n1994\nDECRUZ AJ\nGunner\nCOAS's Commendation Card\n1996\nDAYAL YADAV RP\nComdr\nCOAS's Commendation Card\n1996\nIETE-BV Baliga Memorial Award\nIETE-BV Baliga Memorial Award\nName\nRank\nAward Name\nYear\nSUNDARESH S\nSc G\nIETE-BV BALIGA MEMORIAL AWARD\n2002\nIETE-NV Gadadhar Memorial Award\nIETE-NV Gadadhar Memorial Award\nName\nRank\nAward Name\nYear\nSATHYAMURTHY S\nSc G\nIETE- NV GADADHAR MEMORIAL AWARD\n2003\nINAE Award\nINAE Award\nName\nRank\nAward Name\nYear\nJAYASHREE VARADHAN\nSC G\nSUMAN SHARMA AWARD\n2010\nINAE Fellow\nINAE Fellow\nName\nRank\nAward Name\nYear\nSIVAKUMAR P Dr.\nDS\nINAE FELLOW AWARD\n2014\nNational Design Award by Institution of Engineers\nNational Design Award by Institution of Engineers\nName\nRank\nAward Name\nYear\nNATARAJAN M\nDIRECTOR\nNATIONAL DESIGN AWARD\n1996\nSIVAKUMAR P\nSc F\nMECH ENGG DESIGN AWARD\n2002\nSIVAKUMAR P\nDIRECTOR\nNATIONAL DESIGN AWARD\n2012\nNational Award for Physically Handicapped\nNational Award for Physically Handicapped\nName\nRank\nAward Name\nYear\nPARASURAMAN C\nLDC\nNATIONAL AWARD\n1992\nShram Sri Award by Govt of India\nShram Sri Award by Govt of India\nName\nRank\nAward Name\nYear\nAYYAVU S\nTA B\nSHRAM SHRI\n1998\nBALASUBRAMANIAN S\nTA B\nSHRAM SHRI\n1998\nMURUGAN M\nTA B\nSHRAM SHRI\n1998\nKRISHNAMURTHY K\nSTA\nSHRAM SHRI\n1998\nGUNASEKARAN PK\nTA A\nSHRAM SHRI\n1998\nRAMALINGAM T\nTech B\nSHRAM SHRI\n2000\nSASIDHARAN NAIR P\nTech A\nSHRAM SHRI\n2000\nSELVAKUMAR K\nSTA C\nSHRAM SHRI\n2000\nVISWANATHAN K\nSTA C\nSHRAM SHRI\n2000\nSUBRAMANIAN C\nTech A\nSHRAM SHRI\n2000\nShram Vir Award by Govt of India\nShram Vir Award by Govt of India\nName\nRank\nAward Name\nYear\nMADHU D\nTCN C\nSHRAM VIR\n1994\nDHANDAPANI V\nTech B\nSHRAM VIR\n1995\nMUNNUSWAMY PK\nTCN C\nSHRAM VIR\n1995\nCHANDRU R\nTCN C\nSHRAM VIR\n1995\nSEKHAR DM\nSTA\nSHRAM VIR\n1996\nSARAVANAN V\nSTA\nSHRAM VIR\n1996\nSustainable Industry - Institute Partnership Award by Society for Educational and Entrepreneurship Development\nSustainable Industry - Institute Partnership Award by Society for Educational and Entrepreneurship Development\nName\nRank\nAward Name\nYear\nCVRDE\nSUSTAINABLE INDUSTRY - INSTITUTE PARTNERSHIP\n2014\nIndustrial Safety Award by Govt of Tamilnadu\nIndustrial Safety Award by Govt of Tamilnadu\nName\nRank\nAward Name\nYear\nCVRDE\nSAFETY AWARD\n2003\nCVRDE\nSAFETY AWARD\n2004\nRecognition\nOperationalization of Arjun MBT Mk-I tanks\nCVRDE was assigned the task of operationalization of Arjun MBT Mk-I tanks by Honourable Raksha Mantri which are with various army regiments. As desired, CVRDE has successfully completed the task by making 107 Arjun MBT Mk I operational in time.\nTo appreciate the efforts of CVRDE towards operationalization, DGMF has arranged for a meeting of DRDO team on 19th November 2018 with Chief of Army Staff (CoAS) as part of good will gesture. The meeting was attended by Dr. G. Satheesh Reddy, Secretary DD(R&D) and Chairman DRDO, Shri S. Guruprasad, DG (PC&SI) and Shri V. Balamurugan, OS & Director, CVRDE. The CoAS has appreciated the efforts of CVRDE in operationalizing 107 Arjun MBT Mk I tanks. During the occasion, DRDO presented one scaled model of Arjun MBT Mk IA to CoAS.\nDr. G. Satheesh Reddy, Secretary DD (R&D) & Chairman DRDO, Shri.S.Guruprasad, DG (PC&SI) and Shri. V. Balamurugan, OS & Director, CVRDE presenting a scaled model of Arjun MBT Mk IA to General BipinRawat, PVSM, UYSM, AVSM,YSW, SM, VSM, ADC, Chief of Army Staff\nGeneral Bipin Rawat, PVSM, UYSM, AVSM,YSW, SM, VSM, ADC,Chief of Army Staff, discussing with Dr. G. Satheesh Reddy, Secretary DD (R&D) and Chairman, DRDO, Shri.S.Guruprasad, DG (PC&SI) and Shri. V. Balamurugan, OS & Director, CVRDE\nDiscussions between General Bipin Rawat, PVSM, UYSM, AVSM,YSW, SM, VSM, ADC, Chief of Army Staff, Shri. V. Balamurugan, OS & Director, CVRDE & Dr. G. Satheesh Reddy, Secretary DD (R&D) and Chairman DRDO\nInternational Patents\nS.No.\nTitle\nYear\nPatent Application No.\nPatent No.\nCountry\n1\nA Vehicle and Method for Detecting and Neutralizing an Incendiary Object\nDr. N. Babu,\nShri R. Alexander,\nSmt. Swarna Ramesh,\nSmt. Lakshmi Prathibha\n2022\nUS15/561479\nUS11221196B2\nUnited States\n2\nA Vehicle and Method for Detecting and Neutralizing an Incendiary Object\nDr. N. Babu,\nShri R. Alexander,\nSmt. Swarna Ramesh,\nSmt. Lakshmi Prathibha\n2021\nEP1677149A-2016\nEP3278051A4\nEuropean Patent Office\nNational Patents\nSr. No.\nTitle\nYear of Filing\nPatent Application No.\nPatent No.\nCountry\n1\nFlow straightener throttle for fan testing rig\nInventors:\nShri A. Vinayagam\nShri P. L. Sathyanarayan\nDr. N. V. Mahalakshmi\n2005\n3376/DEL/2005\n259631\nIndia\n2\nSliding and tracking hybrid locomotion to Robot for uneven terrain\nInventors:\nShri N. Babu\nShri G. Kannan\n2008\n2588/DEL/2008\n279176\nIndia\n3\nMuzzle bore sight with extension bar\nInventors:\nShri S. Senthuranathan\nShri C. Mohanarengam\n2007\n721/DEL/2007\n285901\nIndia\n4\nA vehicle for detecting and removing buried objects and method thereof\nInventors:\nShri N. Babu\nShri G. Kannan\nDr. N. Seetharaman\n2009\n2081/DEL/2009\n307274\nIndia\n5\nFlexible Coupling Inventors:\nDr. S. Ganesan,\nDr. V. Balamurugan,\nDr. S. Nagesh, S. Jothi\n2014\n794/DEL/ 2014\n356370\nIndia\n6\nHeight Adjustment System for a Seat Inventors:\nM. Munusamy,\nD. Thanikaivel,\nP. Saravanan,\nS. Maniyam,\nJ. Rajesh Kumar,\nDr. V. Balaguru,\nDr. P. Sivakumar\n2014\n2380/DE L/ 2014\n376220\nIndia\n7\nNano-coolant(s) and method for preparation thereof Inventors:\nDr. S. Dhanalakshmi,\nDr. Srinivas Vadapalli (GITAM University)\nNithiya Priya Karthikeyan\nM. H. Khader Basha\nA. Kumarasamy\nDr. P. Sivakumar\n2017\n20171103 8702\n349611\nIndia\n8\nA method for Obtaining Tin Selenide Thin Films. Inventors:\nDr. S. Dhanalakshmi,\nDr. Geetha Priyadarshini (PSG IAS) ,\nDr. K. Sasikumar,\nV. Priya,\nV. Shalini (PSG IAS),\nK. Sekar\nV. Balamurugan\n2022\n20191104 0407\n390745\nIndia\n9\nSeat Height Adjustment Inventors:\nV. Dhanasekaran,\nK. Viswanathan,\nM. Gnanaseharan,\nM. Sunil,\nG. Srinivasan,\nDr. V. Balaguru,\nDr. P. Sivakumar\n2022\n2381/DEL /2014\n400847\nIndia\n10\nA rotary positive displacement machine Inventors:\nN. S. Prasad,\nDr. P. Sivakumar\n2022\n1122/DEL /2014\n402851\nIndia\n11\nA hinge assembly for hatch of a vehicle and a method thereof Inventors:\nDr. J. Roopchand,\nDr. P. Sivakumar\n2022\n093/DEL/ 2015\n403369\nIndia\n12\nAmmunition Storage Assembly Inventors:\nM. Gnanaseharan,\nK. Viswanathan,\nG. Umapathy,\nM. Sunil,\nG. Srinivasan,\nJ. Rajesh Kumar,\nDr. M. A. Muthumanickam,\nDr. V. Balaguru,\nDr. P. Sivakumar\n2022\n3283/DEL /2014\n412147\nIndia\n13\nSimulation based Integrated Test Facility Inventors:\nS. Ramesh,\nB. Rohini,\nS. Jothi\n2022\n1216/DEL /2012\n414922\nIndia\nCopyright\nTitle\nGranted on\nAuthors\nReg. no.\nFax flow automation software\n07-18-2013\nS. Madivanan Sc G\nJeyapradha Ganesh, Sc F\nAD Kannagi ,TO B\nSW 6648/2013"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-awards/defence-bio-engineering-electro-medical-laboratory-debel", "content": "Lab Awards\nAgni Award for Excellence in Self Reliance\nAgni Award for Excellence in Self Reliance for the year 2001 was Awarded to Shri CGS Sarma, Director, DEBEL and his team comprising of Dr VC Padaki, Sc `F', Dr ASK Prasad, Sc `E', Dr PP Krishnapur, Sc `E', Shri TM Kotresh, Sc `D' and Smt DT Shakunthala, Sc `D'\nAgni Award for Excellence in Self Reliance 2007\nDr. VC Padaki, Director, Scientists and team members of project Combat Free Fall Parachute System was conferred with the Agni Award for Self Excellence 2007 for the successful completion and induction of Life support Systems for Combat Paratroopers, on 12 May 2008 on National Technology Day.\nAgni Award for Excellence in Self Reliance 2008\nDr. VC Padaki, Director, Scientists and team members of Under Water Technology Group were conferred with Agni award for Self Reliance 2008 for the successful development of Submarine Escape Set. Hon. Defence minister Sri AK Antony conferred the award to Director during the directors conference at Vigyan Bhawan, New Delhi on 23 Feb 2010.\nISAMPE Award 2008\nShri R Indushekar, Scientist 'E' was awarded ISAMPE (Indian Society for Advancement of Materials and Process Engineering) outstanding Design and /or Process Development Award - 2008 for the work on the Development of fiber-fiber hybrid composites for Aerospace Applications. Dr AC Niranjanappa, Joint Secretary, ISAMPE presented the memento, citation and cash prize to Sri. Indusekhar at the 22nd Annual General Meeting of ISAMPE at Sir Valluri Auditorium, NAL, Bangalore on 20.06.2008.\nNABL Accreditation\nDEBEL has been granted accreditation to National Accreditation Board for Testing & Calibration Laboratories (NABL) in accordance with ISO/IEC 17025:2005 for Chemical Testing with effect from 30 Jan 2010.\nYoung Scientist Award 2010\nBrig SK Mazumdar Memorial Trust conferred Young Scientist Award 2010 to Shri RG Revaiah, Sc D for his presentation on \"Development of battery heated cold weather clothing for protecting our protectors from extreme cold climate\".\nISAMPE Award 2011\nThe Indian Society for Advancement of Materials and Process Engineering (ISAMPE) for Outstanding Design/ Process development - 2011 to Smt. SN Vijayalakshmi Sc 'E' and team during the 25th Annual General Body Meeting at NAC on 29th July 2011.\nScientist of the Year 2012\nDRDO Scientist of the Year Award for the year 2012 for his outstanding contribution in the field of Aeromedical Life Support Technology for fighter & transport aircraft was conferred on Dr. PP Krishnapur, Sc 'G' in Oct 2012..\nBest Performance Award 2011\nThe Best Performance Award 2011 for providing excellent secretarial support to the Director in his techno managerial work was conferred on Shri N Hoysala, PA ‘C’ on 20 Mar 2012.\nScientist of the Year 2013\nDRDO Scientist of the Year Award for the year 2013 for significant contributions towards the design, development, certification and induction of technical textile based protective clothing for fighter pilots of Indian Air Force and Protective Equipment for other Services was conferred on Dr. TM Kotresh, Sc 'F' in May 2013.\nYoung Scientist Award 2013\nThe Young Scientist Award for the year 2013 was awarded by Brig SK Mazumdar Trust, New Delhi, to Shri D Selvakumar, Sc 'E'.\nYoung Scientist Award 2014\nDr Jayanth Daniel, Sc 'D' was awarded the best Young Scientist for the year 2014 for his meritorious contribution towards Design and Development of SpO2 based Wearable Oxygen Controller System during the Brig SK Mazumdar Memorial Lecture held in Delhi on 17 November 2014.\nScientist of the Year 2015\nThe Scientist of the year Award for the year 2015 was conferred on Dr NS Kumar, Sc F by Sh Arun Jaitley, Hon'ble Defence Minister, on 24 Feb 2016 for his significant contribution towards Design, development and large scale induction of NBC Protection Equipment, and establishing unique test setup for evaluation of materials and filters to ensure safety of individual onboard underwater vessels.\nDefence Technology Spinoff Award for the Year 2016\nDesign & Development of appropriate, affordable and accessible External Counter Pulsator as an alternative to Interventional Cardiology by adapting the defence technology of Anti-G Suit and Anti-G Valve combination developed to ameliorate the effect of G-forces encountered by the Fighter Pilots.\nYoung Scientist Award 2017\nMrs Sugunashree, Sc 'D' was awarded the best Young Scientist Award for the year 2017 for her meritorious contribution towards ''Electronic Control Unit for ILSS'' during the Brig SK Mazumdar Memorial Lecture held in Delhi on 13 November 2017."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-awards/defence-electronics-application-laboratory-deal", "content": "Quality Management System ISO 9001 Certification (First ISO Certified R&D laboratory of INDIA)\nDRDO realized the need for implementation of the Quality System based on ISO 9001: 1994 for its laboratories. DEAL became the first laboratory to go for ISO 9001 certification and became the first R&D laboratory in INDIA due to its strong Product Assurance activities and Project Management. Dr APJ Abdul Kalam, than SA to RM, and DGR&D received first ISO 9001 certificate for DEAL in a function held at Sena Bhawan, New Delhi and during his speech he stressed the need for all the laboratories to establish the Quality System and go for ISO 9001 certification. During early 1995, DEAL created an organization structure and initiated its actions for aligning of the existing quality setup in accordance with the ISO 9001 for the projects and technical activities. Strengths & weaknesses of Quality System in our projects & technical activities were analyzed and the gaps were plugged in reference to ISO 9001. DEAL Quality System was offered for the assessment to STQC, Dept. of Electronics (accredited by the Dutch Council for certification) during Jan 1996 and on 25th July 96, DEAL became first R&D laboratory of India to achieve ISO 9001, 1994 Certification for its Quality System and subsequently which was re-certified during 1999, 2002. During 2003 DEAL QMS was certified for ISO 9001, 2000 during 2003 and re-certified during 2007.\nGolden Peacock National Quality Award\nDefence Electronics Applications Laboratory, Dehradun was adjudged winner for the Golden Peacock National Quality Award 1997 (GPNQA-97) for special category R&D for outstanding achievement in pursuit of Total Quality.\nAt the 8th World Congress on Total Quality in Mumbai on 12.02.98, Shri Asok Sen, Additional Director received the award from Shri PC Alexander, Governor of Maharashtra and Shri Prakash Chand, Head Quality System presented the achievements due to good quality practices followed by DEAL.\nDEAL Quality System was assessed by a panel of judges led by Shri N.Vittal, Chairman, PESB for this award on the following points.\nDEAL has adopted good Quality practices since inception of the laboratory and it is the implementation of these Quality practices that has resulted in achieving Golden Peacock National Quality Award.\nOrganization Leadership\nStrategic Quality Planning\nHuman Resources Development and Management\nCompetitive Benchmarking\nProduct Quality and Services Quality Assurance\nSuppliers Quality Progress\nCustomer Satisfaction\nImpact on society\nBusiness Results.\nNABL Accreditation of Metrology Laboratory\nMetrology Laboratory of Center for Advance Mechanical Engineering (CAME) is contributing towards the development of precision millimeter wave components, through metrology and calibration work. Recently, the competence of the laboratory has been formally recognized by National Accreditation Board for Testing and Calibration Laboratories (NABL), which has awarded accreditation to the laboratory with effect from 4th Oct 2006. Qualifying the requirements of ISO/IEC 17025:2005, Metrology Laboratory of CAME has become the first lab of DRDO to get prestigious NABL accreditation, in the field of Mechanical Calibration. NABL being a signatory of Mutual Recognition Arrangement (MRA) of Asia Pacific Laboratory Accreditation Cooperation (APLAC), which in turn is a signatory of International Laboratory Accreditation Cooperation (ILAC) MRA, the measurement and calibration data of the laboratory would have international recognition.\nScope of NABL accreditation covers calibration of 11 types of measuring instruments and standards of different ranges and accuracies, which includes calibration of Block Gauges, Step Gauge, Micrometer and Vernier Check Sets, Dial Gauges, Pin Gauges, Surface Plates etc. If the BMC (Best Measurement Capability) of the various instruments / standards are to be considered the Metrology Laboratory of DEAL is today among the top few NABL accredited laboratories, in the field of Mechanical Calibration, in India.\nMetrology Laboratory, DEAL & NABL Certificate\nGolden Peacock Quality Awards\nThe laboratory is the first R & D set up in the country to be certified as the ISO-9000 certified establishment. This was recognized at the National Level when it was Awarded the prestigious Golden Peacock Quality Award (R & D) for the year.\nNRDC Awards Winners\nThe team of Scientists Comprising of Dr K D Nayak, Shri Virpal Singh, Shri Ashok Mittal and Shri Ajay Malik were Awarded a cash prize of Rs 50000/- in the Highly Recommended category for “Development of Three Channel Monopulse Receiver at Ka Band (Milimeter Waves) in the year 1998.”\nTeddy bear collectors\nYear\nTeam Leader\nMembers of the Team\nAmount\nCitation\n1980\nDr. E. Bhagiratha Rao, Sc-G\nGp Capt SC Basu, VCM\nSh C Rama Rao, Sc-E\nSh CK Chaterjee, Sc-E\nSh Harbhajan Singh, Sc-E\nSh. C Appa Rao, Sc-D\nSh MM Sharma, Sc-D\nSh YP Sehgal, Sc-C\nSh CVKS Sastri, Sc-C\nSh Asok Sen, Sc-D\nSh RS Mishra, Sc-C\nRs. 5000/- (Rs. 500/-each to every member of the team excluding the team leader)\nDevelopment of troposcatter Communication Equipment under the programme for installing a long haul communication system, utilizing Forward scatter by troposcatters in the Microwave frequency band.\n1990 - 1994\nSh VB Mathur, Sc-E\nSh NS Chhabra, Sc-E\nSh Gyanesh, Sc-D\nSh SS Sarin, Sc-D\nSh RP Dixit, Sc-D\nSh VP Dutta, Sc-D\nSh Hari Singh, Sc-D\nSh Virpal Singh, Sc-D\nSh SusheelVerma, Sc-D\nSh B Burman, Sc-C\nSh RB Singh, Sc-C\nSh Kartar Singh, JSO\nRs. 10000/-\nThe Defence Research & Development Organization Technology Award of Rs. 10000is given to Shri VB Mathur, Scientist-F and his team of eleven members from the Defence Electronics Application Laboratory, DehraDun. This Award is in recognition of their contributions towards development of millimeter wave communication system\n1995\nSh RS Misra, Sc-F\nSh K Siva Kumar, Sc-E\nSh AK Shukla, Sc-E\nSh DK Dutta, Sc-D\nSh RC Kargeti, Sc-D\nSh Ashok Kumar, Sc-D\nSh PK Mittal, Sc-C\nSh SRama Krishnan, Sc-C\nSh Satish Kumar, Sc-C\nRs.20000/-\nThe Outstanding Contributions in f millimeter waves for communications, missile seeker heads and top attack smart munitions.\n1996\nSh Prakash Chand, Sc-E\nSh Girja Shankar, Sc-E\nSh PP Khanna, Sc-E\nSh K Siva Kumar, Sc-E\nDr BS Jassal, Sc-E\nSh Gyanesh, Sc-E\nSh Jindal SK, Sc-E\nSh KP Rangari, Sc-E\nSh PK Sharma, Sc-D\nSh RS Pundir, Sc-D\nSh GH Kumar, Sc-D\nSh VP Dutta, Sc-D\nSh Vineet Dwivedi, Sc-D\nSh PL Sehgal, Sc-C.\nRs.20,000/-\nThis Award is in recognition of their contribution in the area of Quality Assurance and in establishing and maintaining quality system management in the laboratory to international Quality Standards.\nDRDO Awards Winners in DEAL\nTeddy bear collectors\nName\nYear\nCitation\nShri Harbhajan Singh(Scientists of the year award)\n1983\nHas been Awarded for his outstanding contribution in the development of VLF receiver.\nShri Ved Prakash Sandals(Sci entists of the year award)\n1988\nOustanding Contribution in satellite communication systems, image processing hardware and illimetric wave guidance technology\nDr Amarjit Singh Bains(Sci entists of the year award)\n1993\nOutstanding Contributions in f millimeter waves for communications, missile seeker heads and top attack smart munitions.\nShri RC Chakraborty(Sci entists of the year award)\n1995\nOutstanding Contributions in Image Processing.\nShri Asok Sen(Sci entists of the year award)\n1998\nSignificant Contributions in development \"Jam resistant data links, tracking links and tracking system for mini RPV-NISHANT\"\nShri Kishan Lal(Young scientists award)\n1998\nDevelopment of Video Coder-Decoder(CODEC)\nShri Krishan Murari Lal(Best performance award)\n1998\nSignificant Contribution in development of systematised accounting system.\nShri Vipin Kumar Kaushik(Young scientists award)\n1999\nOutstanding Contribution in the field of Image Processing."},
