{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-awards/defence-institute-high-altitude-research-dihar", "content": "Lab awards\nCSIR award for S&T Innovations for Rural Development (CAIRD) for the year 2010.\nInnovation for India Awards 2010 by Marico Innovation Foundation\nTitanium Trophy in 2008 and 1997 for best R&D laboratory of Defence R&D Organisation, Ministry of Defence, Govt of India.\nDefence Technology Spin-off Award 2007 and 2003 of Defence R&D Organisation, Ministry of Defence, Govt of India.\nIndira Priyadarshini Vriksha Mitra Award for the year 1993 by Ministry of Environment and Forestry, Govt. of India.\nGuinness World Record\nThe extreme altitude research station at Changla is in the Guinness World Records (2017) as the highest altitude terrestrial research station (17,664 ft) in the world.\nLimca Book of Records\nThe only institute in the world at an altitude of 11,500 feet above mean sea level working in the area of high altitude agro-animal technologies.\nGrowing of 101 types of vegetables in a single season in the same field in Leh Ladakh.\nDocumented growing of extra large size of vegetables in Ladakh."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-awards/defence-institute-physiology-allied-sciences-dipas", "content": "Lab Awards\nTitanium Trophy (2013)\nDIPAS has been awarded with Titanium Trophy for the year 2013 for the outstanding contribution in improving performance and health of soldiers deployed under environmental extremes especially High and Extreme Altitudes using translational research in Human Physiology.\nDefence Technology Spinoff Award (2006)\nDIPAS has designed and developed ALOCAL- an Aloe vera cream as an antifrost bite preparation for use of military personnel as well as civilians working in cold areas a HA.\nDefence Technology Spinoff Award (2005)\nDIPAS has designed and developed Carbogen breathing system for military personnel working in noisy environment. This can also be used by civilian population like traffic police and industrial workers working in steel and rolling."},
