{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-awards/high-energy-materials-research-laboratory-hemrl", "content": "The contributions of HEMRL scientists and scientific staff have been recognized invariably at various forums. They have been honoured with many prestigious National and International Awards including Padma shree, Scientist of the Year, Technology Leadership award etc. Awards conferred to various scientists of HEMRL from time to time are given below:\nTrophies\nSr. No.\nTrophy Name\nLab Name\nYear\n1\nTitanium Trophy\nERDL\n1984\n2\nSilicon Trophy\nERDL\n1989\n3\nTitanium Trophy\nHEMRL\n2007\n4\nTitanium Trophy\nHEMRL\n2019\nScientist of the Year\nSr. No.\nName & Designation\nYear\n1\nDr Haridwar Singh, Sc D\n1983\n2\nDr Haridwar Singh, Director\n1994\n3\nShri PG Shrotri, Sc G\n1995\n4\nDr SN Asthana, Sc F\n2003\n5\nShri A Subhananda Rao, Director\n2005\n6\nShri B Bhattacharya, Sc G\n2007\n7\nDr Amarjit Singh, Sc G\n2008\n8\nShri KPS Murthy, Sc-F\n2008\n9\nShri A Apparao, Sc G\n2009\n10\nDr Manoj Gupta, Sc G\n2010\n11\nShri N P N Rao, Sc G\n2018\n12\nShri Arvind Kumar, Sc G\n2020\nYoung Scientist Award\nSr. No.\nName & Designation\nYear\n1\nMrs Geetha Maddala, Sc C\n2001\n2\nShri H Shekhar, Sc D\n2004\n3\nShri PK Adak, Sc C\n2005\n4\nShri Sushanta Das, Sc B\n2006\n5\nDr S Radhakrishnan, Sc C\n2007\n6\nShri Ramesh Kurva, Sc C\n2009\n7\nShri J Upadhyay, Sc D\n2017\n8\nShri M S Katore, Sc 'D'\n2018\n9\nShri P K Pandey, Sc 'D'\n2019\n10\nShri Navin kumar Dahiwale,  Sc 'D'\n2020\nAgni Award for Excellence in Self Reliance\nSr. No.\nName & Designation\nYear\n1\nDr. Haridwar Singh, Director Shri JS Karir, Asso. Director Shri RGK Nair, Asso.Director Shri S Jayaraman, Jt. Director\n1998\n2\nShri VL Narasimhan, Sc F\nShri B Bhattacharya, Sc F Dr. Manoj Gupta, Sc E Shri KK Radhakrishnan, Sc D Shri PP Singh, Sc D Shri SP Mane, Sc C Shri PS Kumbhar, Sc C Shri H Shekhar, Sc C Shri SB Navale, Sc B\n2001\n3\nShri AK Mondal, Sc F (Team member)\n2004\n4\nShri K P S Murthy Shri RD Wasnik, Sc D (Team member)\n2005\n5\nShri VL Narasimhan, Sc G Shri SC Bhattacharyya, Sc E Shri AK Mandal, Sc D Shri LD Chavan, Sc C Shri AK Nandi, Sc C Mrs S Basu, Sc C Shri VVJadhav, TO A Shri VB Sutar, STA B\n2006\n6\nShri PP Singh, Sc E\n2007\n7\nDr. AK Sikder, Sc F & team\n2008\n8\nShri K P S Murthy, Sc-F Shri SR Vadali, TO D (Team member) Shri SS Samudre, TO C (Team member)\n2009\n9\nShri B Bhattacharya, OS & Director (Team member) Dr Manoj Gupta (Team member)\n2011\n10\nShri K P S Murthy, Sc-G Dr RK Sinha, Sc G (Team member) US Prasad, Sc F (Team member) Dr J Saji, Sc D (Team member)\n2014\n11\nDr PB Navle & Team\n2015\n12\nDr Manoj Gupta, OS & Team\n2017\n13\nShri Arvind Kumar, Sc G,  Team Leader and Team\n2017\nScientist of the Year\nSr No\nName and Designation\nYear\n1\nDr. (Mrs.) UR Nair, Sc 'D' and Ms. HimaPrasanth, Sc 'D'\n2008\n2\nShri N Pandarinath Rao, Sc 'E' and Mrs. Reny M Roy, Sc 'C'\n2009\n3\nShri Arvind Kumar, Sc 'E'\n2010\n4\nShri SudhirBabu, Sc. 'C' and Shri R S Patil, Sc. 'D' (ACEM) Nasik\n2011\n5\nDr. P.B Navle, Sc. 'F' and Shri SC Aglawe, Sc. 'F'\n2012\n6\nShri CGururaja Rao, Sc, 'F' and Dr. A K Mandal, Sc 'E'\n2013\n7\nShri PP Singh, Sc,C and Shri K K Mishra Sc, 'C'\n2014\n8\nShri AvinashChander, Sc 'F' and Shri B K Bihari, Sc 'D'\n2015\n9\nShri K P C Rao, Sc 'F' and Shri V D Raut, Sc 'D'\n2016\n10\nShri M P Kulkarni, Sc 'E' and Dr S Gogoi, Sc 'E'\n2017\n11\nShri S Nandagopal, Sc 'E' and Shri Anirudha Sane, Sc 'D'\n2018\n12\nMsKamakshi Gupta, Sc 'E' and Shri Sandeep Kumar, Sc 'C'\n2019\n13\nShri Bikash Ghose, Sc 'F' and Mrs Darshana Singh, Sc 'E'\n2020\n14\nShri, Rohit, Sc 'F' and Shri Amitesh Pratap Singh, Sc 'E'\n2021"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-awards/institute-nuclear-medicine-allied-sciences-inmas", "content": "Award\nYear\nDescription\nTOLIC Award\n2018\nInstitute of Nuclear Medicine and Allied Sciences (INMAS), Delhi, has been awarded for outstanding Rajbhasha implementation at INMAS during 2017-2018 in the large institution category by Town Official Language Implementation Committee (TOLIC), North Delhi, on 22 June 2018. Dr Anil Kumar Srivastava, Chairman Agriculture Scientists Recruitment Board and TOLIC, North Delhi, awarded various central government institutes for the outstanding contributions in implementing the Official Language in their respective offices. INMAS received award for Best Home Magazine ‘Prastuti’ and Encouragement Award for Outstanding Rajbhasha Implementation.\nDRDO “Scientist of the year\" award -2017\n2017\nDr GuruduttaGangenahalli, Sc ‘G’, Institute of Nuclear Medicine & Allied Sciences (INMAS) has been honored with the prestigious DRDO “Scientist of the year” award 2017. Hon’bleRakshaMantri (RM) SmtNirmalaSitharaman gave the awards to various DRDO scientists for their outstanding contributions. Ceremony held at DRDO Bhavan on 14 May 2018.\nDRDO “Scientist of the year” Award -2016\n2016\nDr. Manju Guptahas been honoured with the prestigious DRDO “Scientist of the year” award 2016. The award is conferred for developmental work on a safe and potential radioprotective drug which can save more than 85% animals against radiation induced 100% mortality. The drug will be of great value for our Armed forces to biologically shield them while rescuing victims exposed to radiation due to accidental/terrorist activities.\nBrig. S.K. Mazumdar Young Scientist Award\n2016\nDr. Amit Kumar, Scientist 'D' received Brig. S.K. Mazumdar Young Scientist Award- 2016 in competition organized by Brig. S.K. Mazumdar Memorial Trust, Delhi on 20 Sep 2016.\nDRDO “Scientist of the year\" award -2009\n2009\nDr RP Tripathi, Sc ‘H’ & Director, Institute of Nuclear Medicine & Allied Sciences (INMAS) has been honored with the prestigious DRDO “Scientist of the year” award 2009, by the then Prime Minister of India.\nBrig. S.K. Mazumdar Young Scientist Award\n2000\nDr. Anil Kumar Mishra, Scientist 'D' received Brig. S.K. Mazumdar Young Scientist Award- 2000 in competition organized by Brig. S.K. Mazumdar Memorial Trust, Delhi.\nDRDO Young Scientist Award-1998\n1998\nDr. Anil Kumar Mishra, Scientist `D’ was awarded DRDO Young Scientist Award- 1998 by the then Prime Minister of India, honourable Shri AtalBihari Vajpayee for his contributions in the area of development of a new radiopharmaceutical (Bz-EDTMPA) which had wide application in the area of nuclear medicine and magnetic resonance imaging.\nNational Science Day Awards (28th February of Every Year)\nNational Technology Day Awards\nName of the Orator\nYear\nTopic\nDr Himanshu Ojha, Sci ‘E’\n2022\nNovel hydrogel based topical formulations for traumatic injuries\nDr Ratnesh Singh Kanwar, Sci 'F'\n2021\nCOVID-19: A major challenge to humanity’\nDr Anant Narayan Bhatt, Sc ‘E’\n2020\nMetabolic modification and Cell signaling approaches for obviating radio-protection\nDr. Rashmi Agarwal, Scientist ‘E’\n2019\nDeveloping a deeper insight into the changing etiologies and varied clinical presentation of the metabolic master: The Thyroid Gland\nDr. Sudhir Chandna, Scientist ‘G’\n2018\nDousing the fire within: newly discovered ‘smart’ radio protective signaling mechanisms\nDr. Raj Kumar, Scientist ‘E’\n2017\nDevelopment of Radiation Countermeasures using Radio resistant bacteria to protect biological systems against nuclear radiation\nDr. Manju Bala Popli, Scientist ‘F\n2016\nRecent Technical Innovations for Imaging of Cancer Breast: A summation of Engineering and Medicine\nDr. Madhu Bala, Scientist 'F'\n2015\nNew Paradigms in Radio biology- Implications in Developing medical Radiation Countermeasures\nDr. Manju Gupta, Scientist ‘F’\n2014\nHuman health protection against radiation: A challenging Task\nDr. Rajiv Vij, Scientist ‘F’\n2013\nDefence Science Forum: Initiatives and Strategies\nfor Scientific Communication for the Future\nDr. Anupam Mondal, Scientist ‘F’\n2012\nEvolution of Nuclear Medicine to State of Art PET-CT Facility\nDr. AK Mishra\n2011\nMultimodal Imaging agent with special reference to MR for molecular imaging\nDr. NK Chaudhury, Scientist ‘F’\n2010\nInnovations through S&T projects: An experience\nDr. Subash Khushu, Scientist ‘F’\n2009\nEvolution of NMR: from molecules to human behaviour\nDr. Aseem Bhatnagar, Scientist ‘E’\n2008\nPharma coscintigraphy: The Hidden Wheel and Fire of Nuclear Medicine\nDr. BS Dwarakanath, Scientist ‘F’\n2007\nConceptual biology and literature based discovery: Impact on biomedicine\nBrig. RK Marwaha\n2006\nIs vitamin D deficiency a national health problem? Current perspective\nDr. M. Sahoo, Scientist 'F'\n2005\nRole of FNAC in the diagnosis of thyroid diseases\nDr. Ravi Kashyap, Scientist ‘F’\n2004\nNovel approaches to assess infection by using nuclear medicine\nBrig. RP Tripathi\n2003\nNew frontiers in non-invasive cardio vascular imaging\nBrig. JK Bansal\n2002\nMedical ethics implication and prevention\nLt. Gen. T. Ravindranath\n2001\nIndigenous development of maxillo-facial devices\nDr. HC Goel, Sci ‘F’ Prof. NK Mishra, AIIMS\n2000\nPerspectives in Biomedicine Current trends in interventional Neuroradiology\nNational Technology Day Awards (11th May of Every Year)\nNational Technology Day Awards\nName of the Orator\nYear\nTopic\nDr. Rashmi Aggarwal, Sci 'F'\n2022\nMedical strategies for enhancing physical and cognitive performance of combat operators and civilian population by optimizing their vitamin-D status\nDr. Anant Narayan Bhatt, Scientist 'E'\n2019\nDevelopment of cell signaling and inflammation based radiation countermeasure strategy for armed forces\nDr. Paban Kumar Agrawala, Scientist 'E'\n2018\nDevelopment of radiation countermeasure agents: a novel approach\nShri Dhruv Kumar Nishad, Scientist 'D'\n2017\nDevelopment of NBC medical emergency kit for strategic warfare\nDr. Amit Kumar, Scientist 'D'\n2016\nHaemostasis in combat causality management\nDr. PC Gupta, Scientist ‘E’\n2015\nDesign and development of an automated external Radiological & Nuclear (RN) contamination monitoring cum decontamination device (named SUSNAN)\nDr. PoonamRana, Scientist 'D'\n2014\nMetabolomics in Military Applications\nDr. KailashManda, Scientist ‘E’\n2013\nBehavioral Models in preclinical Neuro-psycopharmacology\nDr. Rajnish Sharma, Scientist ‘F’\n2012\nSpectrum of Neuro-cognitive Dysfunction on FDG PET/CT Imaging\nDr. I. PremKumar,Scientist ‘C’\n2011\nHigh throughput screening approaches using zebrafish as a vertebrate organism model for identification of promising radio protectors and suspended animation inducers\nDr. GU Gurudutta, Scientist ‘E’\n2010\nStem Cell therapeutics: Cutting Edge Technological inventions\nDr. AK Mishra, Scientist ‘F’\n2009\nSmart chemical approaches to develop multivalent probes in imaging sciences\nDr. Sudhir Chandna, Scientist ‘E’\n2008\nSimplified Cell Embedding and Micro-Electrophoretic Techniques for Analysis of Cellular Pathophysiology, Cell Death and Drug Responses: Applications in Radiation Sciences and Biomedical Investigations\nDr. SubashKhushu, Scientist ‘F’\n2007\nDevelopment of functional MRI: Applications in Neuro-science\nSh R S Rautela, Scientist 'B'\n2006\nAuto tuned bilateral coil for MRI and MRS\nDr. BS Dwarakanath, Scientist ‘F’\n2005\nTechnology for improving cancer therapy\nBrig. RK Marwaha\n2004\nThyroid epidemiolog: countrywide screening of residual goitre in the post iodisation phase\nDr. Arun Batra, Scientist ‘C’\n2003\nPerfusion MR Imaging\nDr. S. SenthilKumaran, Scientist ‘C’\n2002\nImage visualization software on PC platform\nDr. MadhuBala, Scientist ‘E’\n2001\nPulsed-field Electrophoresis: Technological developments and Genomics research\nDr Anil Kumar Mishra\n2000\nNew Diagnostic Radio pharmaceuticals"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-awards/institute-systems-studies-analyses-issa", "content": "Lab awards\nOver 10 Commendation Awards received from the Armed Forces."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-awards/instruments-research-development-establishment-irde", "content": "Agni Award for Excellence in Self-reliance\nSh. Sudhir Khare, Scientist ‘F’ & his Team for the Year 2014\nSh. S P Gaba, Scientist ‘G’ & his team for the Year 2013\nDr. Ajay Kumar Scientist ‘F’ & his Team for the Year 2011\nDr. S S Negi Scientist. ‘G’ & his team for the Year 2009\nScience & Technology Excellence Award by Uttarakhand Science & Technology Congress for 2014-15 - Dr S S Negi, OS & Director\nSilicon Trophy to IRDE for the Year 2011.\nDRDO Scientist of the Year Award\nSh. Sudhir Khare, Scientist ‘G’ for the Year 2017\nSh. Manvendra Singh, Scientist ‘F’ for the year 2015\nDr. A K Gupta, Scientist ‘G’ for the Year 2008\n5th Uttarakhand State Science & Technology Congress-2010, Young Scientist Award\nSh. Ram Prakash Nautiyal Sc. ‘B’.\nDRDO Young Scientist Award\nSh. Neeraj Pandey, Scientist ‘D’ for the year 2015\nSh. K K Pant, Scientist ‘C’ for the year 2013\nSh. Ajay Mishra Sc. ‘C’ for the year 2009\nDRDO Best Performance Award\nSh. Ajay Kumar Sharma, TO ‘B’ for the Year 2018\nSh. Kuldeep Singh, DEO ‘D’ for the Year 2018\nSh. B P Dimri, TO ‘C’ for the Year 2017\nSh. Mohan Chandra, PA ‘C’ for the Year 2014\nSh. M.S. Bangrania PS ‘A’ for the Year 2009"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-awards/naval-materials-research-laboratory-nmrl#top", "content": "Young Scientist of the year award for the year 2017\nShri Vivek Shrivastava, Sc-D receiving the Award\nPath Breaking Research / Outstanding Technology Development for the year 2017 :-\nDr Suman Roy Choudhury, Sc-G and his team\nESAB India Award-2018 for best paper\n: Dr A. Gourav Rao presented the paper entitled “Thermal Assisted Friction Stir Welding Of HSLA Steel: A Novel Approach To Mitigate Lower Toughness And Ductility” at the International Congress 2017 (IC-2017) held at the Chennai Trade Centre, Chennai during 7th-9th December, 2017. The paper has been adjudged as the winner of ESAB India Award-2018 for the best paper across all categories\nDRDO@60 Online Innovation Challenge\n: NavRachna Award: Shri Vivek Shrivastava, Sc-D & Dr Sangram K Rath, Sc-E had participated in the DRDO @60 Online Innovation Challenge: NavRachna and their ideas have been appreciated and recommended for implementation.\nShri Vivek Shrivastava, Sc-D receiving the Award\nNATCOM-2018 Best Paper Presentation Award :\nDr Vijay M Nimbalkar, Scientist ‘D’ has received “BEST PAPER” presentation (FIRST PRIZE) AWARD on “Development of Al-Alloys NRC Cast Components for Defence and Automobile Industries.” This paper was presented in Customer Engagement –Technology Aspirations for NextGen Supply Chain & Manufacturing (NATCOM-2018) 4th MAT SELECT, Organized by Indian Institute of Materials Management, Aurangabad, during 22nd & 23rd Nov 2018.\nBest Performance Award for the year 2018 :\nShri U G Suryawanshi, TO-C receiving award\nDRTC Award for Excellence in Technical Performance for the year 2018 :\nDr. Vikas Katkar, TO-B receiving award"},
