{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/advanced-systems-laboratory-asl", "content": "1. DRDL, ASL and RCI Constitute the Missile Complex.\n2. Design and Development of Missiles, Missile Defence Systems and Related Technologies\n3. Technology Development as per the Charter of Individual Laboratories\n4. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n5. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n6. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n7. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n8. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n9. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n10. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/aerial-delivery-research-and-development-establishment-adrde", "content": "1. Design & development of aerial delivery systems and constituent technologies.\n2. Research & development of advanced deceleration technologies & systems.\n3. Research & development of advanced airships and inflatable systems.\n4. To create necessary infrastructure & test facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n5. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n6. To support upgrades throughout product life cycle.\n7. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n8. To develop the spin-off technologies.\n9. To provide support and work with govt. Agencies, academia and industry.\n10. To undertake life assessment and extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/aeronautical-development-establishment-ade#top", "content": "1. Research and Development of Advanced Aeronautical Systems.\n2. Design & Development of Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) & Aerial Targets.\n3. Stealth Shaping Designs and Development of Flight Simulators\n4. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n5. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n6. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n7. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n8. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n9. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n10. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/centre-air-borne-system-cabs", "content": "1. Design and Development of Airborne Intelligence, Surveillance & Reconnaissance Systems and Constituent Technologies.\n2. Development & Exploitation of Instrumented Flight Test Bed\n3. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n4. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n5. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n6. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n7. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n8. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n9. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/centre-artificial-intelligence-robotics-cair", "content": "1. Research & Development of Advanced Artificial Intelligence and Cognitive Technologies & Systems.\n2. Design and Development of Information and Communication Security Systems\n3. Design & Development of Advanced Net Centric Decision Support Systems\n4. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n5. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n6. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n7. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n8. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n9. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n10. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/centre-fire-explosive-and-environment-safety-cfees", "content": "1. Research & Development of Fire, Explosives and Environment Safety Technologies and Systems including Clearance for Constructing new facilities, Process Safety Audit and playing Advisory Role for MoD Establishments & Security Agencies\n2. Promulgation of Explosive Safety Regulations (STEC) for MoD Establishments\n3. Training in Fire Prevention, Fire Fighting and Allied Subjects\n4. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n5. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n6. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n7. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n8. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n9. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n10. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/combat-vehicles-research-development-estt-cvrde", "content": "1. Research & Development of Advanced Tracked Armoured Vehicles (T-AV), Constituent Technologies & Support Systems.\n2. Design & Development of Aircraft Landing Gear Systems for Aerial Platforms\n3. Research & Development of Internal Combustion Engine, Transmission and Related Systems\n4. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n5. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n6. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n7. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n8. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n9. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n10. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-bio-engineering-electro-medical-laboratory-debel", "content": "1. Design & Development of Advanced Life Support and Protective Systems.\n2. Design and Development of Biomedical and Engineering Systems for Augmentation of Soldier Capabilities\n3. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n4. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n5. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n6. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n7. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n8. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n9. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-electronics-application-laboratory-deal", "content": "1. Design & Development of Advanced Secure Communication Systems and Constituent Technologies.\n2. Design & Development of Advanced Satellite Terminals and Hubs.\n3. Development of Regenerative Payloads for Satellite and Aerial Platforms\n4. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n5. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n6. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n7. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n8. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n9. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n10. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-electronics-research-laboratory-dlrl", "content": "1. Design, Development and Integration of Advanced Electronic Warfare (EW) Systems.\n2. Design, Development and Integration of Advanced Avionics Systems, Sensors and Payloads for Airborne Platforms.\n3. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n4. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n5. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n6. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n7. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n8. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n9. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-food-research-laboratory-dfrl#top", "content": "No active record(s) available currently for this section."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-geoinformatics-research-establishment-dgre", "content": "1. Development of Technologies for Data Gathering, Processing, Forecasting, Monitoring, Control and Mitigation of Landslides & Avalanches.\n2. Research & Development in Geo-informatics\n3. Data Dissemination\n4. Development of Digital Atlas of Different Terrains\n5. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n6. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n7. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n8. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n9. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n10. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n11. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-institute-high-altitude-research-dihar", "content": "1. To Evolve the Requirements for High Altitude & Cold Region Military Support Systems and Coordinate the Development.\n2. Establishment of High Altitude Test Range and Test & Evaluation Support\n3. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n4. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n5. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n6. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n7. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n8. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n9. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-institute-physiology-allied-sciences-dipas", "content": "1.    R&D on Human Performance Enhancement for Combat Operations through Integrated Physiological Approaches and Human Machine Integration.\n2.    To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n3.    To generate all the necessary documentation.\n4.    To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n5.    To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n6.    To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n7.    To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n8.    To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-institute-psychological-research-dipr", "content": "1. Research & Development of Psychological Tools for the Selection Process of Armed Forces and Central Armed Police Forces (CAPF) Personnel.\n2. Research & Development in Psychological Warfare, Social Engineering, Motivation, Attitude, Morale, Leadership and Organisational Behaviour.\n3. Development of Tools and Methodologies for Psychological Adaptation in Extreme Environments\n4. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n5. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n6. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n7. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n8. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n9. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n10. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-laboratory-dlj", "content": "1. Research & Development in Camouflage & Low Observable Materials, Decoy & Countermeasures Technologies\n2. Research & Development of Nuclear and Radiological Surveillance, Detection and Protection Technologies\n3. Research & Development of Desert Survival, Support & Warfare Technologies\n4. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n5. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n6. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n7. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n8. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n9. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n10. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-materials-and-stores-research-and-development-establishment-dmsrde", "content": "Research & Development of Advanced Polymers and their Composites, Stealth Materials, Nano-materials, Advanced Fibres and Technical Textiles.\nResearch & Development of Speciality Materials, Lubricants & Synthetic Fuels, Special engineering fluids, Ceramics and Ceramic Matrix Composites (CMCs).\nResearch & Development on speciality coatings and paints.\nDesign and Development of Advanced Personal Protection Systems.\nTo create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\nTo generate all the necessary documentation e.g. ToT documents, Technical Reports etc.\nTo support upgrades throughout the Product Life Cycle.\nTo develop the Spin-Off technologies.\nTo provide technical support and work with Govt. Agencies, Sister labs, Academia and Industry.\nTo publish patents and papers in International and National Forums.\nTo undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/lab-charter/defence-metallurgical-research-laboratory-dmrl#nolink", "content": "1. Research & Development in Metallic Alloys, Intermetallic, Ceramics and their Composites Leading to Production\n2. Process Development, Product Engineering, Surface Engineering and Production Support for Alloys and Composites.\n3. Research & Development in Extractive Metallurgy of Critical Metals and Metallurgical Failure Analysis\n4. To create Necessary Infrastructure & Test Facilities for R&D and LSP, as applicable.\n5. To generate all the necessary documentation.\n6. To support upgrades throughout product Life Cycle.\n7. To utilise technologies developed by other labs.\n8. To develop the Spin-Off technologies.\n9. To provide support and work with Govt. Agencies, Academia and Industry.\n10. To undertake Life Assessment and Extension activities, wherever required"},
