{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/technologies/defence-electronics-research-laboratory-dlrl", "content": "DLRL continuously monitors the ever-changing threat perception across the globe and aims at development of State-of- the-art technologies to be on par with the advanced countries. A number of new technologies like EW Antennas and Radomes, Microwave Super Components, Radar finger printing Systems, DRFM, high sensitivity and high accuracy Digital Receiver, Complex signal processing algorithms for estimation of DF and characterization of radar and communication signals are extensively explored, analyzed and implemented with the latest techniques in the field. These technologies have been developed as modules and can be configured on any platform based on the requirements of the services. Important technologies which the Lab has developed are given below:\nBroad Band EW Antenna and Radome Technologies\nHomodyne Receivers, Quad Superhet Receivers, Quad Digital Receiver, Channelized Receiver, Switch Matrix Units, Power Amplifiers, T/R Modules LTCC Filter Banks\nSystem Controller & Display Technologies – Dual Monitor\nRadar finger printing system (RFPS)\nSignal analysers and processors - FPGA\nSearch & monitoring receivers\nSolid state power amplifiers and digital exciters for jamming HF, V/UHF tactical communication Radios\nCommunication signal direction finders and signal analysers\nSatellite signal interception, monitoring, analysis & recording"},
