{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/technologies/defence-research-development-establishment-drde", "content": "Technologies and Products\nMany of the technologies developed by DRDE are available for civil use as a spin off and have been transferred to private sector for commercial exploitation.\nProducts for Services\nAutoject Injectors MK –II\nCR Grenade\nDecontamination Solution (DS-2)\nFirst Aid kit - CW type A MK - I & type B MK- II\nFixed Chemical Agent Detector (FCAD)\nNBC Canister Neelkantha ’A’\nNBC Filters\nNBC Permeable Suit MK-V\nOleoresin Grenade\nPersonal Decontamination Kit (PDK)\nPortable Chemical Agent Detector (PCAD)\nPortable Decontamination Apparatus (PDA)\nPortable Gas Chromatograph (PGC)\nResidual Vapour Detection Kit (RVD)\nThree Colour Detector (TCD) Paper\nDiagnostic Kits\nAnthrax Detection Kit\nBrucellosis Antibody Detection Dot ELISA (Human)\nChikungunya Antigen ELISA\nChikungunya Bio-Lamp\nChikungunya IgM ELISA\nGlanders Antibody ELISA (Equines)\nJE IgM Elisa\nSwine flu H1N1 Nu-Lamp\nProducts and Process Technologies\nBiodigester (Biodgester for Low Temperature High Altitude Areas, Biodigester for Tropical Plane Areas, Railway Biodigester)\nDiethyl Phenyl Acetamide - A Muliti-Insect Repellent (DEPA Cream and DEPA Spray)\nMoth Proofing Of Woolen Fabric\nSlow Release Insecticide Paint\nWater Poison Detection Kit (WPDK)\nWater Testing Kit (Microbial)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/labs-establishment/technologies/defence-research-development-laboratory-drdl", "content": "Missile Systems designed and developed by DRDL have been inducted and operationalized. These include, Underwater Launched Missiles, and AKASH Family of Surface to Air Missile Systems, the Long Range Supersonic Cruise Missile BRAHMOS developed through the Indo-Russian Joint Venture, and the Medium Range Surface to Air Missile System MRSAM-IN developed through the Indo-Israel Collaboration Project. Many other systems such as the NAG family of Anti-Tank Guided Missiles, ASTRA family of Air-to-Air Missiles and the Quick Reaction Surface to Air Missile (QRSAM) are in the advanced stage of induction."},
