{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/liquid-hiden-fuel-jp-10#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nLiquid HIDEN fuel (JP-10)\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nJP-10 is HIDEN fuel for missile application as per MIL-DTL-87107D standard."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/long-term-potato-storage-technology-extreme-winters-ladakh", "content": "Back to Listing\nLong term potato storage technology for extreme winters in Ladakh\nLabs\nDefence Institute of High Altitude Research (DIHAR)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nKeeping in view the potential of supplying locally grown potatoes to Army, DIHAR has developed a “Net-Zero Energy Based Potato Storage Technology” suitable for cold desert area of Ladakh. This technology has potential for assured local availability of fresh potato supply up to seven months (November-May) in winters to the Army deployed in Ladakh sector. With this technology, army can procure their demand of potatoes locally from the local farmers during the whole winter months, thereby shortening the conventional supply chain without compromising on quality. As a spin-off effect large number of local employment may also be generated across the border region of Ladakh and will help develop better fraternization between army and locals for effective border management. During the winter months of 2017-18, DIHAR in collaboration with HQ 14 Corps and local Cooperative Marketing Society (CMS), undertook a successful demonstration of this technology in the 3 Div Karu sector of Ladakh."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/low-frequency-dunking-sonar-lfds#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nLow Frequency Dunking Sonar (LFDS)\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nLow Frequency Dunking Sonar (LFDS) is an advanced version of MIHIR. The development of an airborne winch for deployment and retrieval of dome is a significant technology leap in this sonar system. LFDS is capable of both active as well as passive sonar operations. It is presently fitted on an Advanced Light Helicopter (ALH)."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/low-level-transportable-radar#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nLow Level Transportable Radar\nLabs\nElectronics & Radar Development Establishment (LRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nLow Level Transportable Radar (LLTR) is a ground based rotating Active Phased Array Radar System for air space surveillance to detect and track air targets, under hostile EW operational environments. The radar is fully programmable from the local operator work station."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/mahila-kalyan-manch/about", "content": "Name:\nThe name of the Association DRDO Mahila Kalyan Manch For the sake of brevity, referred as Manch\nRegistered Address\nDRDO Mahila Kalyan Manch\nc/o DRDO Guest House\nDevelopment Enclave\nRao Tula Ram Marg\nNew Delhi - 110 010\nEmail ID:\nmkm_delhi2004[at]yahoo[dot]com\nThe Manch has its Headquarters at Delhi with local branches at other cities wherever major laboratories, establishments are located. Each of these local branches will be governed by the rules and regulations of the Manch."},
