ic Veils\nDMSRDE\nLow-frequency material solutions (L and S Bands)\nDLJ\nPlume IR Signature Suppression Technology\nDLJ\nRadar Absorbing Coatings for Radar Cross Section (RCS) reduction\nDLJ\nStealth Materials, Components and Technologies for Aero applications\nDMSRDE\nThermoelectric materials for infrared cloaking\nDYSL-SM\nTextile\nAuxetic textiles, Biodegradable textiles & E-textiles\nDMSRDE\nGel Spinning Technology for the Production of Ultra High Molecular weight Polyethylene (UHMWPE) Fibers\nDMSRDE\nHigh performance blended fabrics for  uniforms of Indian Armed Forces\nDMSRDE\nLightweight Multifunctional Activated Carbon Fabric (ACF) (woven & non-woven) for Chemical Biological Radiological & Nuclear (CBRN)\nDMSRDE\nMicroporous Carbon and Graphene Based Materials for Antistatic Textiles\nDMSRDE\nComposites\nExperimental development of cork-based composite as Thermal Protection System\nASL\nProcessing/ Fabrication\nDevelopment of processing Technology of high density materials such as Mo, Ta & W-Cu for defence applications\nDMRL"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/medium-power-radar#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nMedium Power Radar\nLabs\nElectronics & Radar Development Establishment (LRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nMedium Power Radar (MPR) is fully active, rotating, multifunction phased array radar. It is a ground based 4D surveillance radar for generation of true air picture, with accurate and precise measurement of aerial targets for air defense operation. It can operate in rotation mode with 360° azimuth coverage or staring mode with 120° azimuth coverage with higher update rate. Radar can survive intense ECM environment and possible electromagnetic interference. It is fully programmable from the local operator work station and also remotely from Remote Operator Work Station Unit."},
