{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/our-luminaries", "content": "DR DS Kothari\nSA to RM and DG DRDO\n(12.07.1948 – 18.03.1961)\nProf. S Bhagavantham\nSA to RM and DG DRDO\n(01.07.1961 – 13.10.1969)\nDr BD Nagchaudhuri\nSA to RM & DG DRDO\n(01.07.1970 – 01.07.1974)\nProf. MGK Menon\nSA to RM & DG DRDO\n[17.08.1974 – 10.07.1978]\nDr Raja Ramanna\nSA to RM & DG DRDO\n[10.07.1978 – 15.02.1982]\nDr VS Arunachalam\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[15.02.1982 – 10.07.1992]\nDr APJ Abdul Kalam\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[10.07.1992 – 29.12.1999]\nDr VK Aatre\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[29.12.1999 – 31.08.2004]\nShri M Natarajan\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[01.09.2004 – 31.08.2009]\nDr VK Saraswat\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[01.09.2009 – 31.05.2013]\nDr Avinash Chander\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[01.06.2013 – 31.01.2015]\nDr S Christopher\nChairman, DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[29.05.2015 – 28.05.2018]"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/p7-heavy-drop-system", "content": "Back to Listing\nP7 Heavy Drop System\nLabs\nAerial Delivery Research and Development Establishment (ADRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nP-7 Heavy Drop System is used for Para drop of military stores (vehicle/ ammunition/ equipment) of 7 Ton weight class. Heavy Drop System (P-7 HDS) for IL-76 Aircraft consists of a platform & specialised parachute system. (Parachute System is a multi-stage parachute system comprises of 5 Main canopies, 5 Brake chutes, 2 Auxiliary chutes, 1 Extractor parachute and platform is a metallic structure made up of Aluminium/steel alloys). System has been developed successfully with 100% indigenous resources. P-7 HDS has been inducted in the Army."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/panchi#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nPanchi\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nPanchi is a variant of Nishant (launcher based tactical UAV) with capability of conventional take-off and landing. Panchi is integrated with  an  all  composite  landing  gear  and  has  improved  flight envelope and endurance. Panchi carries a stabilized payload platform. It carries payloads like daylight camera, infrared camera and laser designator. It is powered with an indigenously developed rotary Wankel engine. It has state of art systems, capable of surveillance, reconnaissance, target location detection and artillery fire correction.\n\n\n\nFive flights of Panchi have been successfully completed proving the concept of conventional takeoff and landing. Data for aerodynamic, structure integrity and Flight control studies have been generated and analyzed."},
