{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/pilotless-target-aircraft-lakshya", "content": "Back to Listing\nPilotless Target Aircraft – LAKSHYA\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nLakshya is a cost effective re-usable high subsonic aerial target system powered by a gas turbine engine and launched either from land or ship. It carries two tow targets of tow lengths of 1.5 km each having radar, IR or visual signature augmentation and Miss Distance Indication Scoring System. These tow targets are used for training of land or ship based gun and missile crew and combat aircraft pilots in weapon engagement. The Lakshya was inducted into the Indian Air Force, Indian Navy and Indian Army in 2000, 2001 and 2003 respectively."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/pinaka-ammunition-support-vehicles", "content": "Back to Listing\nPINAKA Ammunition Support Vehicles\nLabs\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nLoader cum Replenishment Vehicle (LCR) and Replenishment Vehicle (RV) are designed as Logistics Support Vehicles for Pinaka Multi Barrel Rocket System (MBRS). Currently in service with Indian Army."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/pocket-water-filtration-cartridge#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nPocket Water Filtration Cartridge\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nPocket water filtration cartridge, which fits into plastic water/cold drinks bottle of standard nozzle size, is based on nanofiber-based membrane and changeable prefilters to provide prolonged uninterrupted supply of potable water."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/polymeric-seals-hydro-pneumatic-control-system-ground-and-aircraft-system#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nPolymeric seals for hydro-pneumatic control system for ground and aircraft system\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nElastomeric and thermoplastics seals are intended to use to resist the leakage of air/ oil between the annular space of the shaft and housing."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/popular-science-and-technology-series#top", "content": "Search for PST\n(4.23 MB)\nCorona's battle with DRDO (Hindi)\nYear of Publishing:\n2020\nView\n(5.46 MB)\nMission Shakti Ebook (Anti-Satellite Missile)\nYear of Publishing:\n2020\nView\n(1.96 MB)\nToxicology and Human Life\nYear of Publishing:\n1989\nView\n(1.11 MB)\nSuper Vision\nYear of Publishing:\n1982\nView\n(1.16 MB)\nSatellites\nYear of Publishing:\n1989\nView\n(7.28 MB)\nSagar main Sangram (Hindi)\nYear of Publishing:\n1991\nView\n(5.2 MB)\nKindling Creativity\nYear of Publishing:\n1996\nView\n(4.77 MB)\nGuided Missiles\nYear of Publishing:\n1990\nView\n(3.86 MB)\nElectronic Warfare\nYear of Publishing:\n1988\nView\n(9.3 MB)\nComputers and Defence Applications\nYear of Publishing:\n1991\nView\n(4.36 MB)\nComposite Materials\nYear of Publishing:\n1990\nView\n(9.86 MB)\nBattle with Barnacles\nYear of Publishing:\n1987\nView"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/power-take-shaft-lca-tejas-0", "content": "Back to Listing\nPower Take Off shaft of LCA Tejas\nLabs\nCombat Vehicles Research & Development Establishment (CVRDE)\nCVRDE developed Power Take Off (PTO) Shaft for LCA Tejas couples the Engine mounted accessory gear box with Aircraft mounted accessory gear box. PTO shaft is capable of transmitting very high peak starting torque and high rpm. This technology is transferred and productionised through industry partners. Obtained clearance for Indigenously developed Power Take-off (PTO) shaft for flight fitment. Successfully completed Engine ground run Test and LSTT in LCA-Tejas. ToT imparted to two Indian manufacturers."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/press-release?title=&page=20#top", "content": "View Archive\nSearch for Press Release\nRM Reviews Progress on R&D in Area of Critical Defence Technologies\n15/06/2019\nRM Reviews Progress on R&D in Area of Critical Defence Technologies\n14/06/2019\nDRDO successfully test fires AKASH – MK -1S\n28/05/2019\nDRDO successfully test fires AKASH MK -1S\n28/05/2019\nएसयू-30 एमकेआई एयरक्राफ्ट से ब्रह्मोस एयर मिसाइल ने सफल फायरिंग लॉन्च की\n23/05/2019\nSuccessful Firing of BrahMos Air Launched Missile from Su-30 MKI Aircraft\n23/05/2019\nDRDO successfully test fires AKASH – MK -1S\n28/03/2019\nPagination\nFirst page\n« First\nPrevious page\n‹‹\n…\nPage\n13\nPage\n14\nPage\n15\nPage\n16\nPage\n17\nPage\n18\nPage\n19\nPage\n20\nCurrent page\n21"},
