{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/products-civilian-sector#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nProducts for the Civilian Sector\nLabs\nCentre for Artificial Intelligence & Robotics (CAIR)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nCAIR_ICR, an Intelligent Character Recognition system for the automated processing of application forms with handwritten entries.\nIntelligent wheel chair for the physically challenged persons: - A low cost, semi-automatic, motorized wheel chair.\nSimulator based Laparoscopic surgery trainer based on VR and Haptics.\nSelective Compliant Assembly Robot Arm or Selective Compliant Articulated Robot Arm (SCARA) for educational institutions. The design focuses on low-cost manufacturing versatile actuation technologies, safety and open customized servo loops, kinematic calculations, and trajectory generation schemes, greatly aiding students in understanding fundamentals of robotic systems.\nRobots for hot slug handling: - A six axes articulated robotic system developed for NMRL for the transfer of a 600 degree Celsius hot slug from an induction furnace to a die casting machine.\nRobot for inspection of steam generator tubes of power plants.\nLanguage Independent Speaker Identification System (LISIS), functioning as the name suggests, for Central Forensic Science Laboratory (CFSL), Chandigarh."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/products#top", "content": "Search for Product\nSort by\nAsc\nDesc\n500kg Prefragmented Bomb\n120 mm Armaments for ARJUN MBT\n120 mm Penetration Cum Blast (PCB) AND Thermobaric (TB) Ammunition For MBT Arjun\n125mm FSAPDSMk-II Ammunition\n130mm SP Gun - CATAPULT\n155 mm x 52 Cal Advanced Towed Artillery Gun System (ATAGS)\n180 Hp Diesel Engine for UAV\n250 KW Silver Oxide-Zinc Battery\n2D Low Level Light Weight Radar (LLLR): BHARANI MK I\n3 D Medium Range Surveillance Radar for Airforce- Rohini\n3D Car (Central Acquisition Radar)\n3D Low Level Light Weight Radar Aslesha Mk I\n3D Surveillance Radar for Indian Navy -Revathi\n3D Tactical Control Radar\n3G UWACS\n40mm Under Barrel Grenade Launcher (UBGL)\nPagination\nCurrent page\n1\nPage\n2\nPage\n3\nPage\n4\nPage\n5\nPage\n6\nPage\n7\nPage\n8\nPage\n9\n…\nNext page\n››\nLast page\nLast »"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/programme-divya-drishti#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nProgramme Divya Drishti\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nIt is a ground based distributed, passive Communication Intelligence System for Interception, Monitoring, Direction Finding, Analysis and Recording of communication emitters in HF, V/UHF and MW frequency bands. It is a joint DRDO - SI Directorate Programme. The system is integrated through a secured communication network for voice and data fusion across the system. This integrated advanced Communication Intelligence gathering system consists of 25static and 4 Mobile Surveillance Stations spread across the country. The system provides Real-Time Situational Awareness about adversary flying activities."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/programme-samudrika#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nProgramme SAMUDRIKA\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nProgramme SAMUDRIKA aims at the design and indigenous development of a family of Seven Electronic Warfare Systems meeting the requirements of Navy for different platforms viz., Ships, Helicopters and Aircrafts, with a firm commitment from Navy for quantity production and induction of these Systems. Seven EW/ESM systems are grouped under two projects namely Ship-Borne projects & Air-Borne Projects. Ship-borne systems are SHAKTI, NAYAN and TUSHAR. Air-Borne systems are SARANG, SARAKSHI, SARVADHARI and NIKASH.Order has been placed by Indian Navy for 12 Nos. of Shakti and 07 Nos. of Nayan systems."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/programme-samyukta#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nProgramme Samyukta\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nIt is a joint Army-DRDO integrated Electronic Warfare Programme. It is acomplex Ground Based Mobile EW System for Tactical operations. The system is configured on 145 vehicles for deployment in an area of 100 km by 70 km for Surveillance, Interception, Direction Finding & Jamming of various Communication & Radar Signals."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/programme-sangraha#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nProgramme Sangraha\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nIt is a joint DRDO-Navy Programme which envisaged design and development of five different types of indigenous EW systems consisting of KITE, EAGLE and HOMI ESM systems for airborne platforms, PORPOISE ESM System for submarine and EW suite ELLORA for ships. The systems are being used for Coastal & Maritimes EW Surveillance and Self-protection requirements of Naval Platforms. 62 KITE Systems, 20 EAGLE Systems, 5 HOMI Systems, 13 PORPOISE Systems and 10 ELLORA Systems have been delivered to Indian Navy. All these systems are installed on respective platforms and are being exploited extensively."},
