{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/retractable-landing-gear-system-rustom-ii-tapas-uav-0", "content": "Back to Listing\nRetractable Landing Gear System for  Rustom II (TAPAS) UAV\nLabs\nCombat Vehicles Research & Development Establishment (CVRDE)\nCVRDE has designed & developed Tri-cycle Nose Wheel Type Retractable Landing Gear System for 2.85 ton class TAPAS(RUSTOM II) UAV. The retractable landing gear (RLG) system consists of  hydro-gas based shock absorber struts, wheel & brake, nose wheel steering, hydraulic system, retraction & deployment mechanism and landing gear controller with DO 178B safety Level A software. The salient features of the RLG system are given below.\nThe indigenously designed & developed airworthiness(CEMILAC cleared) landing gear system has been integrated into the 2.85 ton class TAPAS UAV and completed more than 100 flight trials successfully so far."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/robotic-kit-automated-driving-rkad", "content": "Back to Listing\nRobotic Kit for Automated Driving (RKAD)\nLabs\nVehicles Research and Development Establishment (VRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nThe purpose of Robotic kit is to convert in-use/in-service Manned Vehicle into Unmanned Vehicle for facilitating safer operation in risky zones. In conventional unmanned ground vehicle, driving controls are modified by Drive-by-Wire System, which is vehicle specific design and conversion from manned to unmanned is lengthy. In contrast, Robotic Kit for Automated Driving (RKAD) is a generic & modular solution offering “on demand, faster and easier” mode of conversation into remotely – operated/ autonomous- driving systems. RKAD comprising of modular Drive- by- Robots (along with associated h/w & s/w), can be retrofit on a manned vehicle & removed on need basis, thus providing versatility and flexibility of without being restricted to a particular/ specialist chassis. This has potential to be used for combat support & CI/CT ops, route clearance, road-opening, border patrolling, perimeter surveillance, etc."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/rti-cell/contact-us#top", "content": "Head RTI, DRDO & CPIO, DRDO HQ\nRoom No. 237\n2ndFloor , - B- Wing\nDRDO HQr, DRDO Bhawan\nRajaji Marg, New Delhi- 110011\nTel\n: 23015433, 23007718\nFax\n: 011-23015437\nEmail\n: cpio[dot]hqr[dot]hqr[at]gov[dot]in\nContact details: RTI purposes only. Kindly do not use any of the contact numbers for general inquiry.\nDRDO is placed in Second Schedule of RTI Act, 2005 and is exempt from disclosure of information under Section 24(1) except information pertaining to the allegations of corruption and human rights violations.\nKindly note that DRDO being an organization placed in Schedule II of RTI Act has been granted an exemption by DOP&T from receiving & replying online applications, hence DRDO does not entertain RTI Applications/Appeals through e-mail/ any other electronic media and a Hard copy of the same is mandatorily required to be submitted"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/rti-cell/home#top", "content": "DRDO is placed in Second Schedule of RTI Act, 2005 and is exempt from disclosure of information under Section 24(1) except information pertaining to the allegations of corruption and human rights violations.\nDuring the Period 2024-2025:\nNo. of RTI Applications received and disposed are 491 and 472 respectively.\nNo. of RTI First Appeals received and Order issued are 68 and 65 respectively.\nNo. of RTI Second Appeals received and disposed are 17.\nNo. of questions asked in the Parliament and replies given are 178 and 129 respectively.\nHow To Submit RTI Application (Hindi)\n732 KB\nPublic Authorities Under DRDO\n651 KB\nRTI Act, 2005 (Ministry of Law and Justice)\n1.2 MB Hindi and English\nExemption under RTI Act, 2005\n157 KB Hindi and English\nGuidelines for Information Seekers (English & Hindi)\n773 KB\nHow to submit RTI Application\n732 KB\nFrequently Asked Questions on RTI\n293 KB\nSuo Motu disclosures u/s 4(1)(b) of the ACT\n265 KB\nImportant Decisions/orders\n915 KB"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/rti-cell/rti-officials-drdo#top", "content": "RTI Officials at DRDO HQ\nTransparency Officer\nDr. B.K. Das\nDS and DG (ECS)\nRoom No. 439, DRDO Bhawan\nRajaji Marg, New Delhi-110011\nTel.\n: 011-2301 4372\nFax\n: 011-2301 5437\nFirst Appellate Authority\nDr. Manu Korulla\nOutstanding Scientist & Director General (R&M)\nRoom No. 235, 2nd Floor, DRDO Bhawan\nRajaji Marg, New Delhi – 110011\nTel : 011 – 2301 1860\nFax : 011 – 2301 5437\nHead RTI, DRDO, Nodal Officer, DD(R&D)\n& CPIO, DRDO HQ\nShri Deepak Mishra, Scientist 'G'\nRoom No. 237, 2\nnd\nFloor , B- Wing\nDRDO HQr, DRDO Bhawan\nRajaji Marg, New Delhi- 110011\nTel\n: 011-2301 5433\nFax\n: 011-23015437"},
