{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/sms-x#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nSMS-X\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nSubmarine Sonar Suite is an integrated suite of sonar systems for installation onboard submarine. It is a compendium of multiple sensors for passive detection, which collates different characteristics of the same target and provides target data through information fusion.\nSalient Features\nAll-round superior performance with simultaneous panoramic surveillance coverage\nCapable of detecting, localizing, tracking multiple surface and subsurface targets"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/smt-u-jeya-santhi#top", "content": "Smt U Jeya Santhi\nOutstanding Scientist & Director General - Human Resources (HR)\nSmt U. Jeya Santhi, OS has been appointed as DG(HR), DRDO HQrs, New Delhi with effect from 01 July 2023."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/snake-repellent", "content": "Back to Listing\nSnake Repellent\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nIndia is estimated to have the highest snakebite mortality in the world. World Health Organization (WHO) estimates the number of bites to be 83,000 per annum with 11,000 deaths\nMain Features\nHerbal and ethnic herbs mainly from NE India\nNon-toxic, non-hazards repels all type of terrestrial snake"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/snake-robot#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nSnake Robot\nLabs\nCentre for Artificial Intelligence & Robotics (CAIR)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nThis robot demonstrates concepts of whole body locomotion. The snake robot has 14 active joints. Lateral undulation, side winding, and rolling gaits have been implemented on this robot. A color camera mounted in the hood of this robot provides video feedback."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/software-defined-radio#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nSoftware Defined Radio\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Application Laboratory (DEAL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nSDR is a secure indigenous system with legacy communication support and secure digital voice/data communication for Naval application with 3 channel (2V/UHF band and 1 HF band), 4-channel (2V/UHF band and 2L-band)for Tactical Communication and single channel operation in V/UHF (Manpack role) and UHF band (Handheld role)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/software-radio-development-programme#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nSoftware Radio Development Programme\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Application Laboratory (DEAL)\nHandheld Radio\nVoice and Data Communication\nTarget User : Soldier\nOperate while in Action\nMain Features\nSoftware based\nEmbedded GPS Receiver\nSMS for Situation-Awareness\nPower output up to 5W\nMan pack Radio 5 Watt/ 25 Watt\nSoftware based having similar technology as of CNR (AFV)\nLow power consumption\nSmall size and light weight ( 200X160X65 mm , 2.5kg)\nCompatible with existing AFV/ non AFV radios\nAirborne Radio\nUHF (225-400MHz) and VHF(30-88MHz & 108-174MHz)\nRadiated Power : 20W\nMMI: MIL-STD-1553 & GAU\nNetworking the Battlefield\nSDR\nImages\nManpack Radio\nSoftware Radio Development Programme\nSoftware Radio Development Programme"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/soldier-support#top", "content": "Technology Category\nTechnology Development Task\nLab\nAcclimatization\nMonitoring and prediction of high altitude acclimatization status of troops\nDIPAS\nH2S Prodrug & mi RNA based therapeutics\nDIPAS\nAnimal Cyborg\nAnimals Cyborgs for military applications\nDYSL-AT\nAnimal Training\nCharacterization based on phenotypic, physio-biochemical, and molecular parameters of endurance of Double-humped camel for load carrying & patrolling\nDIHAR\nBrain Computer Intefrace (BCI)\nBrain Computer Interface\nR&DE(E)\nCognitive Technology based Threat warning system for Brain Computer Interface  (BCI) for Military Applications\nDEBEL & INMAS\nElectroencephalography (EEG) based Drone(s) Control for Brain Computer Interface  (BCI) for Military Applications\nDEBEL & INMAS\nCognitive Communication\nFast and secure brain-brain communication using online  physiological data of brain mapping and integration with hardware\nDEBEL & INMAS\nDatabase\nCreating data sets for bioeffects of RF/MW/DEW/ammunition/nanoparticles/bird-strike/noise & vibrations\nDIPAS\nExoskeleton\nExoskeleton based Soldier Augmentation Systems\nR&DE(E)\nHuman Machine Interface force/torque & Interactive control for exoskeleton\nDEBEL\nPsycophysiological evaluations for exoskeleton\nDEBEL\nAI/ML based GAIT Kinetics & Kinematics Estimation & Prediction for Exoskeleton\nDEBEL\nAI/ML based Activity & Task detection for Exoskeleton\nDEBEL\nLight weight High density Battery for walking & flying exoskeleton\nDEBEL\nPassive Exoskeleton for Military Load Carriage\nDIPAS\nGeo Hazard Training\nModelling and Simulation system to train the person in geo hazardous area\nDGRE\nHealth Management\nWearable Sweat-analysis device for fatigue monitoring\nDIPAS\nOmics of altitude tolerance and High Altitude Illness (HAI) and Sudden Death Syndrome\nDIPAS\nHuman Machine Interface\nCognitive Exoskeleton - Integration of humans with complex machines using AI tools\nINMAS\nMental Workload  Analysis\nEstimation of pilot mental work load in Flight Simulator\nDIPR\nMilitary Field Space Heating\nHeating devices for space heating in high altitude and glaciated regions\nDIPAS\nSpace heating module for shelters in high altitude\nDIHAR/DIBER\nOdour Mitigation\nMicroencapsulated materials for signature mitigation (human odour) for troops during emergency operations\nDRL\nOff Road Mobility\nAssess trafficability for strategic planning and movement of man, machine and materials in off road areas\nDGRE\nPersonal Hygiene\nBathing Sponge (Fire retardant Foam with embedded antimicrobial & antifungal property) for Armed Forces\nDRL\nPersonnel Protection Equipment\nSmart vest for identification of Friend or Foe (IFF) for Armed Forces\nDRL\nSurvival Hammock (with FR and shrapnel protective layer) for Armed Forces\nDRL\nPhysiological Analysis\nAnalysis of redeployment to high altitude after de-induction based on Physiological, biochemical data\nDIPAS\nGeneration of data base of physiological responses of female soldiers\nDIPAS\nStress Management\nMindfulness Based Cognitive Therapy (MBCT) based digitized training modules for enhancing psychological wellbeing of junior leaders of Indian Army\nDIPR\nElectromagnetic Brain stimulation to induce sleep in stressed armed personnel.\nDIPAS\nVector Management\nSyndrome based detection for vector-borne, water-borne and food-borne diseases\nDRL\nVector-borne disease rapid-diagnostics using  silicoanalysis\nDRL\nTo Establish a molecular signature database for vector management\nDRL\nWater Purifier\nAdvanced materials for adsorption/ sensing of emerging contaminants for Water Purification System\nDLJ\nAI based Modular Water Purification System (WPS) to minimize inventory, spares & enable Unit level assembly & maintenance\nDLJ\nAI based system configuration & Operation of Water Purification, Decontamination & Generation\nDLJ\nAll-theatre Soldier/Section Water generation & purification kits\nDLJ\nAll-theatre Water Purification & Desalination Systems\nDLJ\nChemical Biological Radiological & Nuclear (CBRN) Water Purification System\nDLJ\nEasy-to-carry emergency water purification system for armed forces\nDRL\nFuturistic membranes for Water Purification System (eg. Graphene, Forward Osmosis, etc)\nDLJ\nWearable\nWearable Computational Devices with wireless interfaces for dismounted crew operation\nCVRDE"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/sonar#top", "content": "Technology Category\nTechnology Development Task\nLab\nAcoustic Transmitter\nActive Transmitter using low frequency projector arrays\nNPOL\nFaired Tow Cable\nFaired Tow Cables for deployment of active transmitter array\nNPOL\nHandling Systems\nHandling Systems for deployment and retrieval of active transmitter array\nNPOL\nWinch and Handling systems for deployment and retrieval of twin arrays\nNPOL\nPower Amplifiers\nHigh capacity power amplifiers for active transmitter\nNPOL\nSignal Processing\nSignal Processing techniques and systems for Active & Passive Receivers\nNPOL\nTowed Receiver Arrays\nTwin-line low frequency towed receiver arrays\nNPOL"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/space-heating-device-bukhari-himtapak#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nSpace Heating Device Bukhari (Himtapak)\nLabs\nDefence Institute of Physiology & Allied Sciences (DIPAS)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nPRODUCT HIGHLIGHTS\nThis Bukhari, designed and developed by DIPAS (DRDO) is a kerosene fuelled, safe and efficient vented space heating device.\nSafe:\nMultiple level safety against back-draft generated blasts.\nBack-draft resistant exhaust vent.\nThree impact braking plates between two chambers.\nNo auto ignition of burner if extinguished.\nNo build-up of harmful gases and fumes in the room.\nEfficient:\nUses only 500-700 ml kerosene/hr.\nMaximal extraction of heat, no thermal wastage in exhaust gases.\nKeeps the room comfortably warm by both convective and radiative heating.\nEnvironment Friendly:\nEach bukhari prevents about one ton of CO2 and 0.3 tons of black carbon per year from going to environment.\nSalient features:\nTwo chambered design, one for hot air blower and other for flue gases.\nThe hot air is circulated in the room with the help of a DC fan that is operated with power generated from a solar panel and stored in a small battery.\nAn improved maintenance free exhaust vent has been provided which works on Bernaouli’s principle and does not allow air coming from any direction to extinguish the burner and thus prevent fire hazard.\nFor the efficient heating a three burner stove has been developed that can also be used for cooking or warming food, heating water, etc.\nControllable blue flame, so no soot formation.\nBukhari has been designed to extract maximum heat so that there is less wastage of heat at the exhaust level\nToT Holders:\n1.\nOrdinance  Equipt Factory\nPost Box 76, Phool Bagh, Kanpur 208001\n2.\nM/s  Miltex Equipments\n, Plot No. 146, Patparganj Ind Area, New Delhi – 110092.  Contact: 9811100294\n3.\nM/s  Vishwa Traders\n, 74/215, Dhankutti, Kanpur . Contact: 7408444488\n4.\nM/s  Madnani Engineers\nWorks, 100B, Co-operative Ind Estate, Udyog Nagar, Kanpur.  Contact:0521 2296130\n5.\nM/s  Krishna Allied\nInd Pvt Ltd, 9/25 A Chandwadi, 138, CP Tank Road, Mumbai –  400 004. Contact:022 42203800-99\n6.\nM/s  Shakti Engineering\nInd A-1, Ashok Vihar Colony, Tansen Road, Gwalior –  474002. Contact: 0751 2381213\n7.\nVijay  Aluminium Works\n, 123/433 Fazal Ganj Kanpur. Contact:9968310040/ 9336114193\n8.\nM/s Ajit Technoplast Pvt.Ltd.,\n104/430, P  Road, Kanpur-208012, Uttar Pradesh, India. Contact No.: 9335036523/991839697\nImages\nSpace Heating Device Bukhari (Himtapak)"},
