{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technical-staff#top", "content": "The selection of candidates for direct recruitment for Technicians and Senior Technical Assistants in DRDO is through Centre for Personnel Talent Management (CEPTAM), Metcalfe House Complex, Delhi - 110054. All the laboratories/establishments under DRDO report the vacancies, together with the relevant details, including the reservation break-up, to CEPTAM.\nCEPTAM is responsible for doing all the connected work such as obtaining clearance from concerned Division for Retraining and Re-Deployment of Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pension, the advertisement in Employment News, national and regional newspapers, contacting local employment exchanges wherever required, receipt and scrutiny of applications, preparations of database of applications, screening as well as short listing, preparation of question papers for written test (wherever required), constitution of selection committees, conduct of written test(CBT) and trade test/skill test , preparation of the list of selected candidates, etc. The aforesaid activities is carried by CEPTAM following the rules, regulations, guidelines and other instructions issued by the Govt. from time to time regulating the subject matter.\nCEPTAM has evolved its own system and procedure so as to ensure transparency, accountability and fairness at every stage of the process of selection of candidates. The final select list of the candidates is recommended by CEPTAM to the respective appointing authorities in the laboratories/establishments, who issue the offer of appointment to the selected candidates after completing all the requisite pre-appointment formalities including verification of the certificates/documents etc. CEPTAM also informs the candidates about their provisional selection.\nAn application fee of Rs. 100/- through Net Banking, Credit/Debit Card or other e-payment modes from applicants for all the posts of Group B and Group C category excepting from those who have been exempted for the purpose by Govt. of India."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1011/192", "content": "Back to Listing\nHAPO chamber\nLabs\nDefence Bio-Engineering & Electro Medical Laboratory (DEBEL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nOne man HAPO chamberis a life saving device that provides emergency treatment to HAPO victim by enhancing the partial pressure of the breathing air inside the chamber.300 chambers have been inducted into Army and induction of 642 is under process.\nImages\nHAPO Chamber2"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1015/140#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nComputerized Pilot Selection System (CPSS)\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nDefence Institute of Psychological Research (DIPR)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nA state-of-the-art embedded micro controller based CPSS with built-in security features has been indigenously designed and developed by DIPR & ADE against the sanctioned project of IAF. The system is used to evaluate the candidates’ psychomotor skills Information processing skills (speed and accuracy), coordination, visualization, time-sharing along with cognitive information processing skills. By subjecting large number of candidates simultaneously to perform concurrent multiple tasks. The system consisting of 20 Nos. of Psychomotor systems and 100 Nos. of Cognitive systems each has been delivered and inducted to the 3 Air Force Selection Boards @ Mysore, Varanasi & Dehradun. It has replaced the earlier British selection process called Pilot Aptitude Battery Test (PABT).\nOR\nComputerised Pilot Selection System (CPSS) replaces the age-old pilot aptitude battery test. The project was also aimed at addressing the issue of the alarming rate of flying accidents in the IAF attributed to pilot error. In addition to flying skills, the future pilot is required to function as a systems manager, controlling various functions of the aircraft systems. The CPSS has new psychomotor and cognitive tests. These tests comprehensively evaluate the qualities required for military pilots, such as psychomotor skills, information, processing skills (speed and accuracy), coordination, visualisation, and time-sharing, by subjecting the candidates to perform concurrent multiple tasks. The CPSS has been jointly developed by the Defence Institute of Psychological Research (DIPR) and the Aeronautical Development Establishment (ADE), both premier organisations of the DRDO, through a decade long research. The new selection system places special emphasis on psychomotor skills and cognitive abilities of the candidates while screening them for selection into the flying branch of the IAF. The computerized pilot selection system ensures objectivity in results and uniformity in the degree of difficulty faced by the candidates.\nImages\nComputerized Pilot Selection System (CPSS)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1015/197", "content": "Back to Listing\nComputerized Pilot Selection System (CPSS)\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nDefence Institute of Psychological Research (DIPR)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nA state-of-the-art embedded micro controller based CPSS with built-in security features has been indigenously designed and developed by DIPR & ADE against the sanctioned project of IAF. The system is used to evaluate the candidates’ psychomotor skills Information processing skills (speed and accuracy), coordination, visualization, time-sharing along with cognitive information processing skills. By subjecting large number of candidates simultaneously to perform concurrent multiple tasks. The system consisting of 20 Nos. of Psychomotor systems and 100 Nos. of Cognitive systems each has been delivered and inducted to the 3 Air Force Selection Boards @ Mysore, Varanasi & Dehradun. It has replaced the earlier British selection process called Pilot Aptitude Battery Test (PABT).\nOR\nComputerised Pilot Selection System (CPSS) replaces the age-old pilot aptitude battery test. The project was also aimed at addressing the issue of the alarming rate of flying accidents in the IAF attributed to pilot error. In addition to flying skills, the future pilot is required to function as a systems manager, controlling various functions of the aircraft systems. The CPSS has new psychomotor and cognitive tests. These tests comprehensively evaluate the qualities required for military pilots, such as psychomotor skills, information, processing skills (speed and accuracy), coordination, visualisation, and time-sharing, by subjecting the candidates to perform concurrent multiple tasks. The CPSS has been jointly developed by the Defence Institute of Psychological Research (DIPR) and the Aeronautical Development Establishment (ADE), both premier organisations of the DRDO, through a decade long research. The new selection system places special emphasis on psychomotor skills and cognitive abilities of the candidates while screening them for selection into the flying branch of the IAF. The computerized pilot selection system ensures objectivity in results and uniformity in the degree of difficulty faced by the candidates.\nImages\nComputerized Pilot Selection System (CPSS)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1048/144", "content": "Back to Listing\nAirborne Early Warning and Control (AEW&C)\nLabs\nCentre For Air Borne System (CABS)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nAirborne Early Warning & Control System (AEW&C), is a force multiplier system of systems for detecting & tracking of enemy/hostile aircrafts/ UAVs etc. It also enables operators onboard and on ground to identify, assess the threat and take actions to guide our interceptors to those for neutralizing those threats. The system is fully net centric, with complete command and control functions not only providing the available information to ground through its multiple data links but also can receive information from ground, integrate and fuse them onboard to provide the operators onboard a composite picture of environment. As a command centre, it enables onboard operators to select, command and guide specific interceptor aircrafts towards enemy threat efficiently and neutralize them."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1050/140", "content": "Back to Listing\nMicro/Mini Air Vehicles\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nMAVs and Mini UAVs have been developed by ADE along with CSIR-NAL. These vehicles have an endurance of 20 mts to 1 Hr. Three MAVs namely Black Kite, Golden Hawk and Pushpak have been designed and developed. These are fully autonomous air vehicles. Two variants of 2 Kg class FWMUAV are developed - the Imperial Eagle and Slybird. A gimbaled payload provides ISR information and a video tracking system ensures the continuous ISR information during the flight & a state of the art Ground Control station controls the entire mission from launch to recovery. An Image processing system that provides the processed data in near real time to take action on the available ISR information. Imperial Eagle and Slybird are comparable in the same class such as RAVEN.\nImages\nMicro/Mini Air Vehicles\nSLYBIRD"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1051/140#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nCombat Aircraft Systems- Systems & Subsystems for LCA\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nADE is the prime design, development and support agency for digital fly by wire (DFBW) Flight Control System (FCS), Digital Flight Control Computer (DFCC)- a quad-redundant flight critical system, OFP software, pilot-in-the-loop flight simulation facility to support the handling quality evaluation for the flight control Laws of the aircraft and mission planning by the Test pilots before each flight of LCA, Engineering Test Station (ETS) used for the functional verification of the FCSand cockpit display system to include the Display Processor (DP), Head-up-Display (HUD) and Multi-Function Display (MFD) units, Flight Control System Test Unit (FTU), Flight Control Panel (FCP), Rear Cockpit FTU (RCFTU) for Light Combat Aircraft program.\nImages\nCombat Aircraft Systems- Systems & Subsystems for LCA"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1052/140#nolink", "content": "Back to Listing\nAvionics Part Task Trainer (APTT) for upgraded MIG-27\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nThe APTT is a Real-Time Part Task Trainer used for providing training to the pilots of upgraded aircraft. The main emphasis in the APTT is to provide functional simulation of all the avionics subsystems of the upgraded aircraft, EW systems and weapon release systems. It provides training under normal flying (take off, landing and en route navigation) and under failure conditions.  APTT was delivered to Indian Airforce in the year 2012.\nImages\nAvionics part time trainer"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1077/173", "content": "Back to Listing\nKaveri Core Engine – Kabini\nLabs\nGas Turbine Research Establishment (GTRE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nKabini engine comprising of high pressure compressor, combustor and high pressure turbine is used for demonstrating hot end parts technology and study the aero-mechanical behaviour of High Pressure spool of the kaveri engine."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1078/140", "content": "Back to Listing\nRUSTOM-1\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nRUSTOM-1 is an all composite, 800 kg class Short Range Remotely Piloted Aircraft System (SR-RPAS) having capabilities of Intelligence, Surveillance, Reconnaissance, Target Acquisition/ Tracking and Image Exploitation. Rustom-1 is the first Indian RPAS to have conventional take-off and landing capability. It has autonomous flight mode and Get-To-Home features. Rustom-1 RPAS has completed 65 flights and demonstrated flight endurance of 10 hrs, range of 200 km and an altitude of 20,000 ft. Up-gradation of SR-RPAS with Automatic Take-off & Landing (ATOL), Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) and Store carrying capability is achievable."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1079/140#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nABHYAS\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nAbhyas is a High-speed Expendable Aerial Target (HEAT) being developed at ADE. It offers a realistic threat scenario for practice of weapon systems. Abhyas is designed for autonomous flying with the help of an autopilot, under development at ADE. Abhyas has RCS, Visual  and  IR  augmentation  systems  required  for weapon practice. Abhyas was successfully flight tested on 13 May 2019."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1129/192", "content": "Back to Listing\nCBRN Defence\nLabs\nDefence Bio-Engineering & Electro Medical Laboratory (DEBEL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nThere is an ever increasing threat of Chemical, Biological, Radiological and Nuclear (CBRN) warfare by state adversaries as well as non-state actors. To counter this threatLife Sciences laboratories are endeavoring towards the development of NBC equipment for the last two decades. A large number of items have been developed and inducted into Services. Several other DRDO Labs belonging to other technology clusters have been participating in the NBC defence R&D under the leadership of LS cluster.\nThe products in the area of detection, protection and decontamination systems have been developed by life sciences laboratories and delivered to the Armed Forces. At the present day, the entire NBC inventory of the Army except one item (Chemical Agent Detector) comprise of DRDO developed products.\nNBC Suit Mk V\nNBC Suit Mk V developed based on US military standard MIL DTL 32102.It provides cover to protect individual soldiers from chemical vapour and droplet, biological agents and radiological dust. After successful trials the product has been inducted to Army. Army has placed supply order for 50000 suits.\nIntegrated Hood Mask\nis for use by the personnel having\nPatka\nor cut/ injury on their cheeks. It consists of Respiratory Mask, Canister and the hood. The Hood is made up of three-layered fabric. The head, parts of face and neck, which are not covered by the mask is detachable and is for one time use only.\nResuscitator\nis for the resuscitation of the personnel having inhaled the CW agents. The standard set comprises of rubber bladder, non-rebreathing valve system, facemask having transparent face piece and inflatable rubber lining and canister which purifies the air and allows pure air into the bladder. The canister contains activated carbon, which absorbs the toxic gases.\nLeak Tester forms\nan Integral part of NBC warfare test equipment. It is used to test the integrity of the respiratory mask before issue to soldiers. The tester is provided with digital display and a logic circuit, which indicates within 40 seconds whether a mask has passed/failed.\nRespiratory Mask\nMk I and II protect the wearer’s lungs by providing the air free from the suspected\nCW agents.\nIt provides wide field of vision and has swivel drinking water facility that provides the means for taking liquid refreshments while wearing the respirator. It is available in small, medium and large size and is compatible with other NBC protection equipment used in field operations.\nAutomatic Chemical Agent Detector & Alarm (ACADA) and Chemical agent Monitor (CAM)\nhave been developed indigenously as per JSQR specifications for point detection. They are used for On-site detection for countermeasures against chemical warfare (CW) agents. Third Party Evaluation of CAM & ACADA carried-out in Year 2018 at TNO, which is an OPCW (Organization for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons) designated laboratory located at The Netherlands.\nDetection Kits\nIn order to check the potability of the water streams, ponds, sources, etc, a Water Poison Detection Kit has been developed which can detect water poisons and chemical Warfare agents in water based on specific chemical reactions with impregnated substrates and reagent papers that impart specific colour change. Similarly, Residual Vapour Detection (RVD) Kit can detect vapours and gases of chemicalwarfare agents based on specific chemical reactions with impregnated silica gel that imparts specific colour change.\nImages\nIntegrated Hood\nResuscitator\nLeak Master\nRespiratory Mask\nACADA\nCAW\nDetection Kits for Water Poison & Residual Vapour"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1158/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nटॉरपीडो और उप-प्रणालियाँ\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nTorpedo Advanced Light (TAL) is a light weight torpedo capable of launch from ships and helicopters to attack submarines in shallow and deep waters. TAL performs pre-programmed search patterns, detects the target and homes on to the submarine.\nSalient Features\nLaunch Platform: Ships & Helicopters\nPropulsion: Electrical, Mg-AgCl Battery\nContra-rotating propellers\nHoming: Acoustic (Active, Passive and Mixed)\nM/s BDL has produced 25 torpedoes for Indian Navy.\nImages\nTORPEDOES & SUB-SYSTEMS"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1169/169", "content": "Back to Listing\nContamination Monitoring Systems\nLabs\nDefence Laboratory Jodhpur (DLJ)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nWater/Liquid/Food Contamination Monitoring System, Laundry Monitoring System, and Mobile Station for Personal Monitoring etc. for monitoring of contamination in terrain, people and other materials like food, water, other eatables etc."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1171/169", "content": "Back to Listing\nElectrochromic Panel\nLabs\nDefence Laboratory Jodhpur (DLJ)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nA new Electrochromic Window Technology (smart window) provides protection from intense heat during hot and bright sunny days by reducing glares produced over the windows of buildings by way of modulating incoming light. The technology can be effectively utilized in the military vehicles."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1172/169", "content": "Back to Listing\nBeta light\nLabs\nDefence Laboratory Jodhpur (DLJ)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nBeta light using tritium isotopes and ZnS phosphor are self illuminating low intensity light devices."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1180/169", "content": "Back to Listing\nFast Setting and High Strength Polymer Concrete Composites (PolyCC) For Rapid Repair of Runways\nLabs\nDefence Laboratory Jodhpur (DLJ)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nThe PolyCC is based on Unsaturated Polyester Resin system as the binder resin. It is prepared by mixing the binder resin with locally available desert / river / sea sand or with a mixture of sand and gravel / aggregates as filler in the presence of certain initiator and accelerator. It develops very good compressive strength within two hours due to three-dimensional cross-linking of the resin. The technology does not require any water at all."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1195/172", "content": "Back to Listing\nAircrew Parachutes\nLabs\nAerial Delivery Research and Development Establishment (ADRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nAircrew parachutes are designed to provide safe landing to the pilot in case of emergencies. This type of parachutes have been designed & developed for all types of fighter aircrafts available with Indian Defence forces."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1202/172", "content": "Back to Listing\nAircraft Arrester Barrier System\nLabs\nAerial Delivery Research and Development Establishment (ADRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nAircraft Arrester Barrier System is a perfect blend of experience and technology to prevent Air Force flying losses. It offers safe and reliable arresting solutions for combat aircrafts during landing and take-off overrun.\nArrester Barrier system is available in two variants:\nFor 6 to 20 ton class aircraft\nFor 20 to 40 ton class aircraft"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1211/172", "content": "Back to Listing\nAkashdeep Medium class Aerostat\nLabs\nAerial Delivery Research and Development Establishment (ADRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nUnder Akashdeep project, design & development of aerostat surveillance platform having net payload of 200 kg at 1 km AMSL has been successfully demonstrated with following sub-systems - Aerostat Balloon, Aerostat Health Monitoring System (AHMS), Data Transfer System, Winch & Mooring System, Gas Management System"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1212/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nMINES - Processor Based Ground Mine (PBGM)\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nThe PBGM is a bottom sea mine capable of detecting and destroying surface and sub-surface targets based on the Acoustic/Magnetic/Pressure influence anomaly in littoral and blue waters.\nSalient Features\nDeployable from surface ships in depth upto 300m\nPre-set Moored Depth Sea Mine against surface targets\nSensors – Flexural Acoustic Hydrophone, Flux Gate, Magnetometer.\nComposite construction to evade Mine hunting of SONAR\n150 Nos - Combat versions Inducted in 2005 and positioned at ENC & WNC."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1216/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nMINES - Processor Based Exercise Mine (PBEM)\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nCombat sea mines require an exercise version for drill and practice in peace time. The PBEM is a sea bottom exercise mine with capabilities identical to that of the combat sea mine PBGM in detecting the target ships and submarines by means of the acoustic/magnetic/pressure influences.\nSalient Features\nExercise version of the combat PBGM\nDeployable from Surface ships, Torpedo Tubes & Mine saddles of Submarines\nDetection of Target by Acoustic, Magnetic, Pressure influence, Data recording and storage.\nRecovery system – HE Bolt, Flasher, Smoke marker and Plunger.\nHanded over to Indian Navy on 11/04/2018."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1217/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nMINES - Processor Based Moored Mine (PBMM)\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nThe PBMM is the Sea Mine for Blue Seas capable of detecting and destroying Surface / Sub-surface by the Acoustic/ Pressure influence anomaly generated by targets passing in proximity\nSalient Features\nSea bottom mine 533mm dia. X 3000mm long\nDeployable from Ships and Submarines\nActuates by Acoustic, Magnetic, Pressure influence of targets\nFibre glass body to evade mine hunting SONAR\nSafety for Electrical power, Explosive & Torpedo tube\nSensors – Hydrophone, Flux Gate, Magnetometer, Depth Sensor"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1220/172", "content": "Back to Listing\nAerostat Health Monitoring System\nLabs\nAerial Delivery Research and Development Establishment (ADRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nAHMS is a vital sub system of Aerostat, it provides active aerodynamic shape maintenance of the aerostat during various phases of flight. By virtue of pressure sensors, air blowers and release valves, controller of AHMS regulates the air pocket in the ballonet of the aerostat to always maintain the desired aerodynamic shape of the aerostat at all times during flight and provides values of all health parameters continuously to the Ground Control Station."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1225/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nMINES - Advanced Exercise Mine (AEM)\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nSalient Features\nDeployable from ships and submarines.\nActuates by Acoustic, Magnetic Pressure influence of targets.\nCommunication through fibre optical cable.\nSONAR insonification detection.\nAEM 15 Nos: - Exercise version Inducted in 2009 and positioned at ENC/WNC/SNC."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1227/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nMINES - Multi Influence Ground Mine (MIGM)\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nSalient Features\nProject name : Multi Influence Ground Mine(MIGM).\nTechnologies : Composite casing, safety devices, Fire Logics.\nTechnology Demonstration completed by DSR & committed to induct 500 MIGMs."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1229/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nSubmarine Fired Decoy (SFD)\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nAnti Torpedo Defence System (ATDS) is a part of ATDS suite which is effective against modern and vintage Torpedo fired against a Ship or submarine. The idea of Expendable acoustic decoy is to confuse and/ or seduce torpedo by mimicking like a target ship.\nSalient Features\nMode of operation: echo repeat, Jammer and mixed.\nLong endurance time.\nLaunched at any operating depth at maximum submarine speed.\nEffective against passive and active homing Torpedoes"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1233/203", "content": "Back to Listing\nAutomatic Electronic Switch (AES)\nLabs\nCentre for Artificial Intelligence & Robotics (CAIR)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nThe Automatic Electronic Switch (AES) provides automatic trunk switching facilities for voice, teleprinter, and computer data. It is a stored program trunk exchange used as a node switch in an Area Grid Tactical Communication Network which provides automatic, fast, secure and reliable communication."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1236/203", "content": "Back to Listing\nAutonomous Navigation System\nLabs\nCentre for Artificial Intelligence & Robotics (CAIR)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nThe Autonomous Navigation System (ANS) established on the in-house tracked test-platform was ported to the teleported BMP-II and successful summer tests were conducted at the Mahajan Field Firing Range (MFFR).\nImages\nANS1"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1238/203", "content": "Back to Listing\nAutonomous Search Robot\nLabs\nCentre for Artificial Intelligence & Robotics (CAIR)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nThe Autonomous Search Robot can perform 3D mapping of an indoor area on its own. In addition to localization, mapping, and path planning, it employs an exploration algorithm which searches for all unknown areas until they have been mapped. Apart from a LiDAR, it uses a RGB-D sensor for 3D depth data capture. With the help of these sensors this robot can indentify 3D obstacles and avoid them during navigation. It can continuously create a 3D map of the indoor scene, which is displayed on a remote user device. The user can select an object to be searched, which are then marked by the robot when they are found in the scene. It uses algorithms for object detection to perform the search. The user can fly through the map and interactively locate searched objects in the map.\nThe Autonomous Search Robot is useful for indoor counter insurgency operations, search and rescue operations, and remote mapping of indoor environments with NBC hazard, when mounted with a NBC sensor."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1242/168#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nIntegrated Anti Submarine Warefare Complex\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nSalient Features\nInterfaces to present Weapon and Sensor fit of SNF class of ships\nGenerates Fire Control Solution for Launching Rockets (RB 600) & Torpedoes by performing Target Tracking using state-of-the-art CMA Algorithms\nCompleted FATS & Ground Trials at ASW School Kochi. Installed on INS RANJIT for sea trials\nIndigenous System costs Rs 4 Cr as against Rs 30 Cr for an Imported System"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1244/168#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nAnti Torpedo Decoy System (ATDS)\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nSalient Features\nFire Control System and Decoy Launch Control Panel developed for use with Indigenous Anti Torpedo Decoy (MAAREECH)\nInterfaces to Ship’s Towed Array SONAR & Hull Mounted SONAR\nSupports Torpedo Tracking and Automatic/ Manual release of Decoys.\nRecommends Escape Maneuver for the Ship during a Torpedo Attack\nDecoy Launch Control Panel also supports Standalone Operation for ships without an FCS & Capable of Programming the Decoy.\nD&E system completed FATS and fitted on INS DUNA GIRI for Evaluation Trials of Decoy."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1246/168#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nAutonomous Underwater Vehicle (AUV)\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nSalient Features\nIntelligence, Surveillance Reconnaissance (ISR):\nIntelligence Collection\nSearch & Surveillance\nDeployment of leace-behind Sensors\nShip Escort Scouting (Reconnaissance)\nCombat Engagements\nDelivery system for torpedoes, mines or other weapons\nTarget for torpedo trials\nExpendable mine / neutralization device."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1247/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nStealth Signature Management\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nSalient Features\nInfrared Signature Suppression Systems (IRSS)\nInfrared Imaging for Threat Assessment.\nInfrared Signature Prediction.\nDegaussing System.\nMagnetic Signature Mitigation.\nUnderwater Magnetic Signature Measurement.\nRadar Cross Section Prediction, Measurement & Mitigation.\nAcoustic Stealth Techniques."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1250/140", "content": "Back to Listing\nLCA Air Force Version\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1267/175", "content": "Back to Listing\nAircraft Mounted Accessory Gear Box\nLabs\nCombat Vehicles Research & Development Establishment (CVRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nAircraft Mounted Accessory Gear Box (AMAGB) is a critical Line Replacement Unit (LRU) and forms a very important part of Secondary Power System (SPS) of LCATejas. AMAGB was first time designed and developed in the country with important technical features, such as, lightweight, compact, high speed, single input and multioutput gearbox of aeronautical standards. The gearbox has self-contained lubrication system which ensure the safe functioning of the gearbox."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1279/140", "content": "Back to Listing\nLAKSHYA-2\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nAdvanced Pilot less Target Aircraft - Lakshya-2 is an advanced version of Lakshya-1. It is a target for weapon systems like radar guided and heat seeking Surface to Air missiles, Air to Air missiles. It has a Scoring systems capable of calculating the miss distance of the weapon accurately. This advanced PTA has enhanced endurance, autonomous and low level flight capability, salvo flying and automated  test  equipment.  It  has  Integrated  digital  flight control processor, Autonomous flight capability, Low level flight, Passive RCS augmentation of Lakshya in front and side aspects for firing of Beyond Visual Range (BVR) missiles, Augmentation of Lakshya air vehicle with active repeater system for firing of BVR missiles,  capability  to  fly  two  air  vehicles  simultaneously  from single GCS, Automated test equipment and Improved visual augmentation on tow body. Transfer of Technology has been given to L&T. \nLakshya Weapon Delivery Configuration is also developed for weapon delivery at known Coordinates. The tow bodies in Lakshya-2 Weapon Delivery Configuration carry High Energy Weapon Payload. Ballistic, Unguided weapon delivery is achieved using Cotntinuosly Computed Release Point (CCRP). 9 Lakshya Weapon Delivery sorties have been completed with 16 weapons (4 Live) dropped."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1285/140", "content": "Back to Listing\nNISHANT\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nNishant is a multi-mission Unmanned Aerial Vehicle launched using a Mobile Hydro pneumatic Launcher with Day/Night capability used for battlefield surveillance and reconnaissance, target tracking & localization, and artillery fire correction. A sophisticated image processing system is used for analyzing the images transmitted from the UAV. The air vehicle has autonomous flight capabilities and is controlled from a user friendly Ground Control Station. Nishant is a highly mobile, compact and easily deployable system. It is recovered with Aero Conical Parachute and impact attenuation system.  An onboard flight control and navigation system enables the aircraft to fly in autonomous Way Point Navigation mode. Nishant has been inducted in Indian Army.\nImages\nNISHANT\nNISHANT"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1288/140", "content": "Back to Listing\nPilotless Target Aircraft – LAKSHYA\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nLakshya is a cost effective re-usable high subsonic aerial target system powered by a gas turbine engine and launched either from land or ship. It carries two tow targets of tow lengths of 1.5 km each having radar, IR or visual signature augmentation and Miss Distance Indication Scoring System. These tow targets are used for training of land or ship based gun and missile crew and combat aircraft pilots in weapon engagement. The Lakshya was inducted into the Indian Air Force, Indian Navy and Indian Army in 2000, 2001 and 2003 respectively."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1302/177", "content": "Back to Listing\n81 mm Anti-thermal Anti-laser (AT-AL) Smoke Grenade\nLabs\nHigh Energy Materials Research Laboratory (HEMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nAn instantaneous smoke screen capable of obscuring Electro-optic equipments has been developed by deploying a 81 mm caliber grenade. Similar performance can be achieved by filling this composition in ammunition of different calibers."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1319/203", "content": "Back to Listing\nAir Defence Control and Reporting System (ADC & RS)\nLabs\nCentre for Artificial Intelligence & Robotics (CAIR)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nThe Air Defence Control and Reporting System (ADC & RS) is used to detect all aerial targets and neutralize the threat well away from the vulnerable area/vulnerable point (VA/VP) by effective integration of all AD Weapon Systems."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1322/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nIR Signature Suppression\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nInfrared Signature Suppression (IRSS) devices are fitted in the exhaust system of ship propulsion and power generation equipment that keeps exhaust metal ducts at considerable low temperature and cools the exhaust. The device has been inducted into the services."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1323/173", "content": "Back to Listing\nKaveri\nLabs\nGas Turbine Research Establishment (GTRE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nGTRE is entrusted with the design and development of Kaveri Engine which is low bypass twin spool turbo fan engine of 80 kN thrust class. The engine incorporates flat rated characteristics to mitigate the thrust drop due to high ambient intake temperature and / or high forward speed. Twin lane full authority digital engine control with an adequate manual backup is a salient design feature of Kaveri Engine.\nImages\nKaveri Engine"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1328/140", "content": "Back to Listing\nLCA TEJAS\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nIndigenously built Light Combat Aircraft Tejas, the lightest multi role combat aircraft in its class, has been inducted into the Indian Air Force."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1344/182", "content": "Back to Listing\nHelina\nLabs\nDefence Research & Development Laboratory (DRDL)\nTechnology Cluster\nMissiles and Strategic Systems (MSS)\nHELINA (Helicopter based NAG) is a third generation fire and forget class anti-tank guided missile (ATGM) system mounted on the Advanced Light Helicopter (ALH). The system has all weather day and night capability and can defeat battle tanks with conventional armour as well as explosive reactive armour. The HELINA missile can engage targets both in direct hit mode as well as top attack mode. HELINA Weapon Systems is being inducted into the Indian Army (IA). A variant of HELINA Weapon System called DHRUVASTRA is being inducted into the Indian Air Force (IAF)."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1357/191", "content": "Back to Listing\n2D Low Level Light Weight Radar (LLLR): BHARANI MK I\nLabs\nElectronics & Radar Development Establishment (LRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\n2D Low Level Light Weight Radar (LLLWR) is a light weight battery powered compact sensor which provides 2D surveillance in mountainous terrain against hostile aerial targets like UAVs, RPVs, helicopters and fixed wing aircraft flying at low and medium altitudes. The radar can be transported by vehicles, animals, group of men or as helislung loads. It can be dismantled into packages to facilitate quick relocation and installation in mountainous terrain. It acts as an early warner to air defence weapon systems employed to provide protection to vulnerable areas or vulnerable points. The radar detects and tracks short-range air-to-ground threats with a high probability of detection. The radar has an integrated IFF that can detect, confirm, classify and attain IFF status on every target in the battle space under surveillance. The radar has an integral GPS and it supports display of tracks over tactical map overlay. The radar with modular architecture, ruggedness as per Mil standards can be operated in varied conditions including extreme climatic and geographical conditions and in battlefield situations."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1366/191", "content": "Back to Listing\n3D Low Level Light Weight Radar Aslesha Mk I\nLabs\nElectronics & Radar Development Establishment (LRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\n3D Low Level Light Weight Radar (LLLWR) is a multi-beam ground based 3D Surveillance Radar for deployment in diverse terrains like plains, deserts, mountain tops and high altitude regions. This radar detects and tracks heterogeneous air targets, including helicopters, fighters and UAVs at low and medium altitudes. This semi-distributed active aperture radar uses advanced VLSI and high-speed digital technologies like high efficiency TRMs, DDS, digital receiver and programmable signal processor to provide 3D air space awareness with high accuracy, resolution and reliability. The radar is engineered in multiple packages to enable easy transportability in mountainous terrain by vehicles, group of men, or as an under­slung carriage by a helicopter. The remote operation of the radar through Commander Display Unit provides safety to the crew during operation. The facility also enables the Commander to deploy the radar at a tactically favourable point. The quadripod-mounted radar is built to operate in networked or stand-alone mode to support joint or independent operations. The 3D LLLWR being compact, lightweight and modular, can be used in different roles like air space surveillance in urban areas for VVIPs and large critical installations."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1398/481", "content": "Back to Listing\nLand Wargaming Systems\nLabs\nInstitute for Systems Studies & Analyses (ISSA)\nTechnology Cluster\nMissiles and Strategic Systems (MSS)\nImages\nDiv Level\nCorps Canvas"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1434/175", "content": "Back to Listing\n130mm SP Gun - CATAPULT\nLabs\nCombat Vehicles Research & Development Establishment (CVRDE)\nThe Self Propelled Medium Artillery Gun was developed on Vijayanta Chassis for firing both HE and AP ammunitions. Maximum range of the gun is more than 25 km."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1442/175", "content": "Back to Listing\n5 kW Brushless DC Generating System for LCA Tejas\nLabs\nCombat Vehicles Research & Development Establishment (CVRDE)\nState-of-the-art 5 kW Brushless Generator is developed for LCA-Tejas to support critical electrical loads for flight safety during emergency when main AC generator fails.Generator comprises multi stages, namely Permanent Magnet stage, Main Exciter and Main Generator facilitating autonomous mode.FPGA/DSP based embedded controller featuring precise voltage regulation with BITE facility to meet stringent MIL standards of voltage regulation."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1483/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nDirecting Gear\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nEquipment for rotating and hoisting the transducer array for purposes of calibration and training of the sonar system."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1484/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nANALON\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nANALON is Own Noise measurement & Analysis (ONMA) system. ONMA is a modular system used for continuous monitoring and localizing of the abnormal noise levels of the platform, condition monitoring of machineries, radiated noise around passive sonar array and for the measurement of cavitation noise. The system consists of accelerometers on-board and hydrophones distributed around the platform for monitoring and capturing the real time radiated noise around the platform"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1485/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nMR Mount\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nMagnetorheological fluid mount (MR Mount) is developed for isolating low frequency vibrations of on-board machinery from the hull of the ships. This real-time active vibration control mount consists of a load bearing elastomer, MR fluid chamber, MEMS based vibration sensor and a controller for closed loop feedback control mechanism. The mount can control low frequency vibrations both in passive and active modes. MR mount was manufactured by KELTRON, Kuttippuram. The mount is accepted by Indian navy for on-board applications."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1501/170", "content": "Back to Listing\nCermet Composites for Aircraft Brakes\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nIt is friction that stops aircraft safely after landing. This friction is generated by mating the brake pads with bimetallic sectors. A superior, indigenous version of brake pads for the MiG-21 fighter aircraft was developed, in which the rotor pad is a powder metallurgy product of metallo-ceramic composition with a high coefficient of friction and the stator pad is an alloy cast iron bimetallic. Based on the technology developed by DMRL, a full scale production plant was set-up at HAL, Hyderabad, for the rotor segments, and at HAL, Bengaluru, for the stator pads.\nFriction materials have been developed and productionised for other aircraft, viz., the HS-748 Dornier, etc., as well. The technology for iron-based friction clutch pads for the synchronised power transmitting gear of marine turbines of the SNF class ships has also been developed for Indian Navy. A range of brake units are being manufactured at HAL that meet the entire defence and considerable civilian requirements in the country.\nImages\nCermet Composites for Aircraft Brakes\nCermet Composites for Aircraft Brakes\nCermet Composites for Aircraft Brakes\nCermet Composites for Aircraft Brakes"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1503/170", "content": "Back to Listing\nArmour Materials & Modules: MBTs and Other Combat Vehicles\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nIntense R&D in the area of armour materials at DMRL has generated a few totally indigenous materials and solutions and also provided for timely improvements of armour for imported equipment. More than 40,000 tons of various armours comprising steels, titanium alloys, ceramics and composites have been produced through this effort.\nKey developments at DMRL include:\nA low alloy steel, named Jackal, for Infantry Combat Vehicles (ICV), light vehicles and body armour\nState-of-the-art Kanchan compound armour for MBT Arjun Mark-I\nAn improved version of Kanchan armour is under development for MBT Arjun Mark-II\nA modified and continuously cast SPADE M1 steel for T-72, MBT Arjun and T-90 tanks\nArmour for BMP-II Urban Survival Kit (BUSK) has been developed meeting multi-hit protection requirements\nJackal Steel Armour\nDevelopment of advanced grade high strength low alloy steel Jackal is a spin-off from a decade long research to\ndevelop technology of superior grade steel armour for ICV (BMP-I), Missiles Carrier Armoured Vehicles (MICA) as well as\ntanks, which are currently under production in the country. Jackal steel was accepted for these applications after a series\nof tests including user trials of a prototype BMP. The technology of Jackal steel has been passed on to Steel Authority of\nIndia Limited (SAIL) and MIDHANI for its bulk production and a few thousand tons of Jackal steel plates have already been\nmanufactured for various requirements. This unique armour, with the active participation of internal security organisations,\nhas been adapted for use on other security vehicles.\nKanchan—The Invincible\nDMRL has developed a unique composite material, named Kanchan, to be used as armour for MBT Arjun and for\nup-armouring the existing Vijayanta tanks. In the firing trials, involving a variety of anti-tank ammunition of extreme\nseverity, Kanchan’s performance was highly commended. This world-class armour is being used extensively as the main\narmour for pre-production series of Arjun Mark-I and also for up-armouring of Vijyanta.\nImages\nArmour Materials & Modules: MBTs and Other Combat Vehicles\nArmour Materials & Modules: MBTs and Other Combat Vehicles"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1504/170", "content": "Back to Listing\nArmour Materials & Modules: Other Platforms\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nHelicopters\nDMRL has successfully developed new generation layered composite armour, named RANAKALI, for Lancer helicopters. Titanium alloy-Ceramics-Polymer-based lightweight composites provide protection against 7.62 ball, 7.62 AP and 12.7 AP ammunitions to critical parts of the helicopters. While in service, this armour has received and withstood attacks successfully.\nDMRL has also developed indigenous ceramic armour, which is substantially lighter than imported steel armour, for Mi-17-1V helicopter. This armour fulfilled desired specifications of the Indian Air Force, which accorded provisional clearance for its use in helicopters. The technology has been transferred to MIDHANI and production has commenced. DMRL is also working on the development of lightweight ceramic armour for Light Combat Helicopter (LCH).\nBody Armour\nDMRL has developed and delivered Jackal body armour for the military and paramilitary forces to protect the precious lives of our jawans from the threat of small arms fire. The development of Jackal steel has filled a major gap in meeting the strategic and critical security requirements for bulletproof applications. The Rakshak Jackets, made of Jackal steel, are found to be far more effective in trapping bullets of 7.62 SLR and AK-47 rifles when fired from a close range. Thousands of these jackets are already in use, thus saving precious human lives as well as foreign exchange.\nDevelopment of processing technology of this steel and fabrication of a few Light Commercial Vehicles (LCVs) at DMRL, followed by successful user trials by the Paramilitary Forces, have also paved the way for the production of bulletproof vehicles, indigenously.\nImages\nArmour Materials & Modules: Other Platforms\nArmour Materials & Modules: Other Platforms"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1516/170", "content": "Back to Listing\nHigh Energy Rare Earth Permanent Magnets\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nRare Earth Permanent Magnets (REPMs) possess high energy density and performance stability, due to which they have great potential in high technology areas like defence, space, atomic energy and medical diagnostics. DMRL has developed the technology for magnetic components of SmCo5 and Nd-Fe-B with high energy product (18-35 MGOe), thereby enabling device miniaturisation. The technology involves compaction of powder in magnetic field followed by sintering/annealing under vacuum/inert atmosphere. Several system laboratories of DRDO (DRDL, RCI, SSPL, MTRDC, NPOL, NSTL, CVRDE), ISRO (VSSC and LPSC) and DAE (BARC and IGCAR) have used magnets developed at DMRL for strategic applications. The technology offers great promise considering the abundant reserves of rare earth minerals in India.\nOther areas of applications are beam control (travelling wave tubes, magnetrons), inertial navigation (gyroscopes, accelerometer, instrumentation), electro-mechanical devices (actuators, RF switches) and permanent magnet alternators, brushless motors, high speed rotors, etc.\nImages\nMagnetostriction Measurement Set-up for Thin Films\nNd-Fe-B and Samarium Cobalt (SmCo5) Permanent Magnets\nUHV Sputtering Unit"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1518/170", "content": "Back to Listing\nDevelopment of Wrought Al Alloys for Defence Applications\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nMost of the wrought Al alloys required for Indian defence are currently being imported. DMRL has developed four different grades of Al alloys, viz., AA2219, AA6082, AA6061 and AA5086 on industrial scale in the form of sheets, plates and rods as required for Army, Navy, Air Force and DRDO’s missile programmes. Type certification of these Al alloy semi-products are near completion. The AA2219 and AA6082 extruded rods (f = 40-150 mm) were produced at Ordnance Factory Ambajhari, Nagpur, for missile and armament applications, respectively. While, AA2219 plates, both unclad and Alclad, in the thickness range of 2-30 mm for missiles, AA6061 sheets (t = 1.2-2.4 mm) for aerospace applications, and AA5086 sheets (t = 2 mm) and plates (t = 12-30 mm) for naval applications have been produced at BALCO, Korba.\nDMRL has also successfully developed DTD 5124 (composition close to AA7075) T651 extrusions at Ordnance Factory Ambajhari, Nagpur, and produced hard anodized tail fin and sabot for FSAPDS ammunition.\nDMRL has actively participated in indigenizing five different advanced Al alloys in the form of extrusions, profiles, forgings, rolled rings and seamless pipes and tubes for missile applications. The cast billets were produced at HINDALCOAlmex Aerospace Limited, Aurangabad, and subsequent extrusion processing, ring rolling, forging and manufacturing of seamless pipes and tubes took place at Century Extrusions Limited (CEL), Kharagpur; CHW Forge Limited, Greater Noida; Steel and Industrial Forgings Limited, Thrissur; and Nuclear Fuel Complex, Hyderabad, respectively.\nImages\nWrought Al Alloy Semi-Products\nAlclad AA2219 Plate\nHard Anodized Tail Fin\nAdvanced Al Alloys in the form of Extrusions, Rolled Rings, Seamless Pipes and Forgings for Missile Applications"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1521/170", "content": "Back to Listing\nAluminium Foams\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nAluminium foams are ultra lightweight materials (hence greater weight saving) which can be used to absorb impact, vibration and blast energy efficiently. DMRL has successfully established laboratory scale technology for the production of closed cell aluminium foams. Foams with density varying from 0.3-0.9 g/cc (i.e. having density less than water) have been produced in cylindrical (up to 220 mm diameter), plate (30-50 mm thick) and other complex shapes. DMRL foams, evaluated at other laboratories, have shown promise for applications requiring blast protection, impact absorption and drop impact protection. Typical applications include crash resistant structures (for defence and civilian automobile bumpers, engine mounting brackets, A-pillars), blast resistant anti mining boots, bunkers, jackets, tank under-belly protection and composite armour.\nImages\nAluminium Foams\n220 mm Diameter Cylindrical Shape\nFoam Cell Structure"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1523/170#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nAluminium Alloy Armour Plates for Infantry Combat Vehicle\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nAl‐Cu‐Mg based AA2519 alloy is used in state‐of‐the‐art Advanced Amphibious Assault Vehicle (AAAV). The AAAV is an amphibious armoured personnel carrier wherein this aluminium alloy is utilized to reduce the weight of the vehicle. The alloy contains high Cu and small amounts of Mg. Because of the presence of Mg, the procedure of melting and casting of the alloy differs considerably from those of the Mg‐free, Cu containing alloys.\nChemical Composition of AA2519 Alloy (wt %)\nMajor Alloying Elements (Balance Al) Impurities\nCu\nMg\nMn\nTi\nZn\nV\nZr\nFe\nSi\n5.3–6.4\n0.05‐0.40\n0.1–0.5\n0.02–0.10\n0.10 max\n0.05–0.15\n0.10–0.25\n0.30 max\n0.25 max\nTechnology Developed at DMRL\nThe technology developed at DMRL involves optimization of alloy composition, casting parameters, homogenization schedule and aging heat treatment for the production of plates for armoured vehicle applications. DMRL has also established a novel method of imparting cold work prior to artificial aging, which greatly reduces the difference in strength properties between longitudinal and long‐transverse directions of the peak‐aged plates.\nThe 15 mm thick plates of the alloy were subjected to ballistic tests against 7.62 x 54 mm AP (I) ammunition. The tests showed 6 % superior results with reference to MIL‐STD‐46192C (MR).\nTensile Properties of Indigenized AA2519‐T87 Plates\nAlloy & Temper\nOrientation\n0.2 % PS (MPa)\nUTS (MPa)\n% Elongation\nAA2519 – T87\nL\n430‐440\n480‐485\n13‐16\n(t = 15 mm)\nLT\n415‐435\n470‐480\n12‐14\nApplications\nThis technology has been developed and demonstrated at the industrial scale. The technology has been assessed in terms of ballistic tests against the prevailing threat level of the armoured vehicles. These alloy plates may be utilized in combination with other armour materials for similar applications."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1530/481", "content": "Back to Listing\nNaval Wargaming System\nLabs\nInstitute for Systems Studies & Analyses (ISSA)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1531/481", "content": "Back to Listing\nSystems Analysis Tools\nLabs\nInstitute for Systems Studies & Analyses (ISSA)\nImages\nNaval Weapon Evaluation\nAlgorithms for Estimation of Target Motion Parameter\nNetwork Centric Warfare – Integrated Air Defense Simulation Testbed\nTactical tool for ECM mission planning"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1536/170", "content": "Back to Listing\nFused Silica Radar Domes by Cold Isostatic Pressing & Sintering Technology\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nSilica Radar Dome (Radome) is a critical component of target seeking Missile as it protects the navigation system of the missile from adverse environment. Slip/Gel casting methods are generally adopted for fabrication of silica Radomes, but the component rejection rate is very high due to several technical reasons. DMRL has developed Radome technology indigenously in view of its strategic nature and long term application.\nSalient Features of Technology Developed at DMRL\nDMRL has carried out innovation driven R&D and established an Indigenous technology based on cold isostatic pressing (CIP) and sintering route for manufacture of silica Radomes.\nThe CIP processed Radomes have shown excellent EM performance.\nDuring the structural load testing, the CIPed Radomes could withstand 240 % and 400 % of the required load at room temperature and at elevated temperature, respectively.\nThe CIP + sintered Radomes also passed through the lightening and vibration tests.\nThe Radomes are required in large numbers to fulfil the current and future requirements of missile applications."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1538/170#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nAl Alloy Sheets & Plates for Superstructures in Naval Warship\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nAluminium alloys in the form of sheets and plates are extensively used for the manufacture of superstructures of naval warship. Such alloys must be weldable and having a combination of medium strength and virtual immunity to stress corrosion cracking and exfoliation corrosion. Aluminium‐magnesium alloys are, therefore, used for such applications.\nTechnology Developed at DMRL\nThe technology involving optimization of DMR291A alloy composition, formulation of various thermal and deformation process parameters including homogenization treatment, hot rolling parameters to realize plates in M temper, cold rolling parameters and post cold rolling annealing cycle to realize sheets in H24 temper has been developed. The process parameters at all the stages have been optimized. The grain structure of the alloy is suitably developed so as to avoid the exfoliation corrosion.The resultant materials are weldable and not susceptible to stress corrosion cracking and exfoliation corrosion.\nApplication Areas\nSuperstructures of naval warship\nSpace applications in different heat treatment tempers\nThe products made using the indigenous technology have achieved the entire range of properties for the targeted applications equivalent to those of the imported materials.\nTensile Properties of Indigenized Al Alloy AA5086\nAlloy & Temper\n0.2 % PS (MPa)\nUTS (MPa)\n% Elongation\nDMR291A‐H24 Sheets (t = 2 mm)\n265‐270\n335‐345\n11‐14\nDMR291A‐M Plates (t = 30 mm)\n125‐130\n275‐280\n22‐27\nImages\nAs Cast Ingots\nSheet in Coil Form\nH24 Sheets (t = 2 mm)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1539/170", "content": "Back to Listing\nAluminium Alloy Components for Anti‐Tank Ammunition\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nAl‐Zn‐Mg‐Cu base DTD5124 alloy is utilized for the manufacturing of tail fin and sabot components of Fin Stabilized Armour Piercing Discarding Sabot (FSAPDS), an anti‐tank ammunition used by Indian army. Typically, these components are machined out of heat treated (T651) DTD5124 alloy round bar extrusions and hard anodized prior to its use.\nChemical Composition of DTD5124 Al Alloy (wt %)\nMajor Alloying Elements\nZn\nMg\nCu\nMn\nCr\nZr+Ti\nFe\nSi\nAI\n5.1‐6.4\n2.1‐2.9\n1.2‐2.0\n0.3 max\n0.1‐0.25\n0.2 max\n0.4 max\n0.5 max\nBalance\nTechnology Developed at DMRL\nThe DTD5124 alloy is Direct Chill (DC) cast and subjected to thermal and extrusion processing. The fully heat treated extrusions were machined to manufacture the final components. The components are then subjected to hard anodizing. Hard anodizing provides thermal barriers to the components during exposure to high temperatures for a few milliseconds during firing, and also protects the material against general corrosion during long term storage.\nTensile Properties of Indigenized DTD5124‐T651 Al Alloy Extrusions\nExtrusion Diameter\n0.2 % PS (MPa)\nUTS (MPa)% Elongation\n% Elongation\n81 mm\n540‐600\n590‐625\n8‐11\n116 mm\n525‐575\n585‐625\n7‐11\n135 mm\n510‐520\n570‐585\n7‐9\nDMRL has indigenized this technology which is currently in use for the manufacture of components of FSAPDS – an anti‐tank ammunition for Indian Army. FSAPDS ammunitions fitted with tail fin and sabot made out of indigenized DTD5124 materials have been successfully test fired.\nImages\nHard Anodized Tail Fin and Sabot Petals"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1541/170#nolink", "content": "Back to Listing\nAl Alloy Sheets & Plates for Military Bridging System\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nAluminium alloys in the form of sheets, plates and extrusions are extensively used in the manufacture of military bridging system for the Indian Army. Such alloys must be weldable and must have a combination of desired strength and high stress corrosion cracking (SCC) resistance. Accordingly, the copper‐free, weldable Al‐Zn‐Mg based 7xxx series alloys are an obvious choice for such applications.\nTechnology Developed at DMRL\nSuitable changes in composition such as maintaining specific Zn : Mg ratios and Zn + Mg contents, addition of suitable recrystallization inhibiting elements, and heat treatments involving overaging are made to substantially improve the SCC resistance of these alloys. The improvement in SCC resistance by overaging is always accompanied by a considerable decrease in the strength. A novel artificial aging heat treatment was, therefore, formulated in order to attain the desired strength, as well as high SCC resistance (indicated by a minimum electrical conductivity of 40 % IACS). A combination of the above metallurgical solutions is incorporated for manufacturing the alloy in various semi‐product forms for military bridging systems.\nTensile Properties of Indigenized Copper‐Free 7xxx‐T7x51 Alloy Sheets & Plates (without Novel Aging Treatment)\nAlloy & Temper\nElectrical Conductivity (% IACS)\n0.2 % PS (MPa)\nUTS (MPa)\n% Elongation\n7xxx‐Tx51\n\t\t\tt = 6 mm\n39.20\n345‐350\n385‐390\n10‐11\n7xxx‐Tx51\n\t\t\tt = 20 mm\n39.40\n320‐325\n365‐370\n16‐18\nTensile Properties of Indigenized Copper‐Free 7xxx‐T7x51 Alloy Sheets & Plates (with Novel Aging Treatment)\nAlloy & Temper\nElectrical Conductivity (% IACS)\n0.2 % PS (MPa)\nUTS (MPa)\n% Elongation\n7xxx‐Tx51\n\t\t\tt = 6 mm\n40.6\n320‐345\n375‐390\n10‐13\n7xxx‐Tx51\n\t\t\tt = 20 mm\n40.2\n315‐330\n360‐375\n14‐16\nImages\nParts of the Bridge Fabricated using Sheets and Plates of Indigenized Al Alloy\nParts of the Bridge Fabricated using Sheets and Plates of Indigenized Al Alloy"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1544/170#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nAA2219 Alclad Sheets and Plates for Missile Applications\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nThe Aluminium alloy AA2219 is extensively used for a wide variety of strategic applications because of a combination of good weldability and high stress corrosion cracking resistance. However, owing to the high copper content, the general corrosion resistance of the alloy is relatively inferior, and therefore, the alloy sheets are always used in the Alclad form.\nChemical Composition of AA2219 Alloy (wt %)\nMajor Alloying Elements (Balance Al)                                                                           Impurities\nCu\nMg\nMn\nTi\nV\nZr\nFe\nSi\n5.8 ‐ 6.8\n‐\n0.2 ‐ 0.4\n0.02 ‐ 0.10\n0.05 ‐ 0.15\n0.10 ‐ 0.25\n0.3\n0.2\nTechnology Developed at DMRL\nThe technology involving optimization of parameters like alloy composition, homogenization schedule, hot and cold rolling parameters and method of imparting cold work prior to artificial aging for the production of AA2219 Alclad sheets and plates has been developed at DMRL. Optimization of the process parameters enabled the production of Alclad AA2219 sheets and plates having thicknesses ranging from 2 mm to 30 mm having reproducible tensile properties and reduced in‐plane strength anisotropy.\nThis technology has been developed and demonstrated at the industrial scale. It has been assessed in terms of structural tests wherein 4 mm thick Alclad AA2219 sheets were formed and joined to form a structural part of a major load bearing section of a missile.\nThe products made using this innovative technology have achieved the entire range of properties for the specific applications. In order to realize reduced in‐plane anisotropy in the strength properties of Alclad plates, the hot rolled Alclad plates are solution treated and subjected to a novel procedure of cold working between solution treatment and artificial aging\nTensile Properties of Indigenized Alclad AA2219 Sheets & Plates\nAlloy & Temper\n0.2 % PS (MPa)\nUTS (MPa)\n% Elongation\nAlclad AA2219‐T83 sheets\n\t\t\t(t = 2 mm)\n325‐370\n425‐470\n12‐13\nAlclad AA2219‐T87 plates\n\t\t\t(t = 12 mm)\n375‐385\n465‐470\n8‐12\nImages\nCladding alloy AA7072\nCladding alloy AA7072"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1545/170", "content": "Back to Listing\nAluminium Foam for Blast & Impact Force Mitigation\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nAl foams are ultra light weight materials with typical densities between 0.3 to 0.9 g/cm3. These foams can be used to absorb impact and blast energy efficiently at low transmitted stresses. They exhibit superior stiffness to weight ratio, vibration damping and resistance to fire in comparison to polymer foams. A technology to make closed cell aluminium foam blocks through liquid metallurgy route is available in DMRL.\nPRODUCT PROFILES\nRegular shapes ‐ cylindrical foam ingots of up to 220 mm diameter and plates of 400 mm x 300 mm x 100 mm size\nFoam components of various geometries to address any specific product requirement\nFoam sandwich panels with required Al alloy face sheets with foam core\nAPPLICATION AREAS\nBlast resistant structures for bunkers, tank under‐belly protection, jackets and antimining boots\nComposite armour (as back up panel for explosive reactive armour) in tanks\nCrash resistant structures, automobile side & front bumpers, engine mounting brackets, A‐pillars & nuclear transportation casks.\nLight weight structures like foam filled beams and channels for commercial vehicles\nPROPERTIES OF FOAMS\nHigh energy absorption per unit weight under compression at low transmitted stresses\nHigh specific stiffness\nVibration damping\nBetter fire retardation behaviour in comparison to polymer foams\nCompressive Properties\nDensity : 0.3‐0.8 g/cc\nPlateau Strength : 1.0‐15 MPa\nElastic Modulus : 0.2‐0.8 GPa\nEnergy Absorbed : 1‐10 MJ/m3\nImages\nCylinders\nFoam Cell Structure"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1550/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nAPSOH\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nAdvanced Panoramic Sonar Hull Mounted (APSOH) was the first SONAR from NPOL that was inducted in to Indian Navy. The induction of the sonar was followed by the commissioning of a training simulator, APSIM at SNC, Kochi. M/s Bharat Electronics was the production agency for the system."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1552/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nHUMSA\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nHull Mounted Sonar Advanced (HUMSA) was the second generation of frigate sonar. HUll Mounted Variable Depth (HUMVAD) sonar is another version of APSOH where the Sonar array depth can be varied for tactical purposes. M/s Bharat Electronics was the production agency for both the systems."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1553/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nHUMSA NG\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nHUMSA-NG is the third generation indigenous, ship borne, hull mounted, Sonar system designed by Naval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory, DRDO, Kochi and productionised by Bharat Electronics, Bangalore. HUMSA-NG is a state of the art Active cum Passive Integrated Ship Sonar system designed to be installed on a variety of naval surface platforms such as Frigates, Destroyers, ASW Corvettes and other classes of ships."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1554/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nHUMSA UG\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nHUMSA UG\nUpgrade of HUMSA Sonar for Ships - HUMSA UG is an advanced integrated active cum passive sonar system designed for ASW platforms. It is specifically designed for up grading the existing Humsa system of Indian Naval platforms and also as an advanced Sonar for new platforms."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1563/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nNAGAN\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nNagan is a towed array sonar system that consists of a transmitter body and a long passive array towed behind the ship. The towed array can be deployed up to 200 m depth. It is useful in Anti-Submarine Warfare (ASW) operations and is the apt sensor for warships to locate silent submarines capable of launching high speed torpedoes."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1564/185", "content": "Back to Listing\nBaffle Range\nLabs\nTerminal Ballistics Research Laboratory (TBRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nMissiles and Strategic Systems (MSS)\nFor small arm firing practice large area range is required. By using BR technology, the requirement of the land can be reduced to as low as one hundredth of original land"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1565/167#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nALTAS\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nAdvance Light Towed Array Sonar (ALTAS) is a sensing system for the detection, localisation and classification of submarines operating especially in the below sonic layer. It is useful in Anti-Submarine Warfare (ASW) operations and is used as a sensor for warships to locate silent submarines capable of launching high speed torpedoes."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1569/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nMIHIR\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nMIHIR is a first generation helicopter sonar system, comprising of dunking sonar and a four channel sonobuoy processor. It was designed for Advanced Light Helicopter (ALH) type platform with limited , weight, space and power resources."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1570/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nLow Frequency Dunking Sonar (LFDS)\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nLow Frequency Dunking Sonar (LFDS) is an advanced version of MIHIR. The development of an airborne winch for deployment and retrieval of dome is a significant technology leap in this sonar system. LFDS is capable of both active as well as passive sonar operations. It is presently fitted on an Advanced Light Helicopter (ALH)."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1573/167#top", "content": "Back to Listing\n3G UWACS\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nThe Under Water Acoustic Communication System (UWACS) enables the half duplex communication between submerged and surface platforms through Analog (SSBSC-AM in the NATO and EKM bands) and Digital (CSK, OFDM, FSK modulations) means. In the event of radio silence (in RF bands) during operational requirements, communication between surface platforms also can be done through the same system."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1577/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nIntegrated Coastal Surveillance System (ICSS)\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nThe Integrated Coastal Surveillance System (ICSS) is a system developed for guarding India's coastal territory for quick detection, location and monitoring of movements of suspect dhows, motorized and traditional vessels in a given controlled area, round the clock without any physical presence."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1578/167", "content": "Back to Listing\nMDB\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nIt is a general purpose multiplexed data network designed and developed for the communication needs for a wide variety of naval platforms. It is compatible to IEEE 802.3 (Ethernet). The system consists of three Ethernet coaxial cable data buses interconnecting up to maximum of 32 modular units called the Modular Transput Controllers."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1592/173", "content": "Back to Listing\nEngine Fuel Control System\nLabs\nGas Turbine Research Establishment (GTRE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nIndigenous design and development of Hydro Mechanical fuel control systems for aero gas turbine engine application through Technology Development route. The EFCS contains pumping unit, fuel metering unit and variable guide vane actuation system for fan and compressor respectively.\nImages\nEngine Fuel Control System"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1593/173", "content": "Back to Listing\nAdvanced Full Authority Digital Electronic Controller\nLabs\nGas Turbine Research Establishment (GTRE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nA-FADEC comprises engine-mounted Digital Electronic Control Unit (DECU) with control laws embedded in it, engine fuel metering units, hydraulic actuation systems, engine sensors and a dedicated permanent magnet power generation unit. A-FADEC being the safety critical system, has several levels of redundancies built-in both in terms of electrical and hydraulics. Design features specific to meet safety requirements of a single engine aircraft application.\nModel based control philosophy\nIntegrated engine health management functions for life and usage monitoring\nControl loops for fuel flow rate, exhaust nozzle area, compressor and fan variable geometry\nEngine mounted fuel cooled chassis with vibration / shock isolators\nDO 178B level A compliant software design process\nInterfaces for coordinated flight and propulsion system control\nDual Electrical and Hydraulic redundancy with Cross Channel Data Link (CCDL)\nFault detection, isolation and accommodation logics with gracefully degraded control modes\nImages\nATE commissioned at GTRE"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1721/177", "content": "Back to Listing\n84 mm High Temperature Suffocating Smoke (HTSS) Ammunition\nLabs\nHigh Energy Materials Research Laboratory (HEMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\n84 mm HTSS round is a multipurpose round. It is optimized for close combat in urban as well as field operational areas and is effective against lightly protected fortifications, brick walls and wooden structures. The round after penetrating target creates high temperature and suffocating smoke. The fragments burn with high temperature setting on fire combustibles and spews out smoke that suffocates human beings. The combined effects can force the enemy to abandon safe hiding place and be captured."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1725/177", "content": "Back to Listing\n500 kg GP Bomb\nLabs\nHigh Energy Materials Research Laboratory (HEMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nTNT based high explosive composition for main filling and RDX based booster composition has been developed for 500 kg General Purpose Bomb. The bomb has blast, fragmentation and penetration capabilities.\nPerformance parameter met quality requirements."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1727/177", "content": "Back to Listing\nAdvanced Air Defence (AAD) Warhead\nLabs\nHigh Energy Materials Research Laboratory (HEMRL)\nHMX based high performance high explosive composition for main filling has been developed for Advanced Air Defence warhead. HE filling technique has been established for the warhead. Performance evaluation trials completed in static mode. Explosive train functioned satisfactorily during flight trial. Performance parameters met quality requirements."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1783/187", "content": "Back to Listing\nData-Link System – Nishant UAV\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Application Laboratory (DEAL)\nPrimary Role (UAV)\nBattle-Field Surveillance and Reconnaissance\nReal-Time Target Engagement\nBattle-Field Damage Assessment\nRobust Data Links for Remotely Controlled Air vehicles form vital elements\nLSP Completed,  User’s Confirmatory Trials -Underway\nImages\nData-Link System – Nishant UAV\nData-Link System – Nishant UAV"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1787/187", "content": "Back to Listing\nCombat Net Radio (CNR)\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Application Laboratory (DEAL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nCNR-AFV (50/5W)\nVHF Frequency Hopping Radio For AFV Role\nImages\nCombat Net Radio (CNR)\nFitment inside Tank"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1792/174", "content": "Back to Listing\n500kg Prefragmented Bomb\nLabs\nArmament Research & Development Establishment (ARDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nARDE has designed the 500 kg Preformed Fragmentation Bomb with Steel spheres as fragments (10,300 nos. of 15 mm steel spheres). The bomb is designed to be compatible with Russian as well as Jaguar aircraft by providing dual suspension lugs of 250 mm and 14 inch spacing. The Bomb is configured with Proximity Fuze with nose initiation. Lethal performance of the bomb in Blast would create Peak-Over-Pressure of more than 0.2 kg/cm2 at 20 meter distance from poin t of burst and preformed fragments would perforate 12 mm Steel plate at 50 m radius with fragment density of >1 hit/m2."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1813/187", "content": "Back to Listing\nCommunication support in disaster relief :\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Application Laboratory (DEAL)\nProvided communication support to Tsunami victims at Nagapattinam - Briefcase Satcom terminal setup at affected site for providing PSTN connectivity\nProvided Communication support to Earthquake hit areas of Uttarkashi (Uttarakhand) and Latur (Maharashtra)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1816/187", "content": "Back to Listing\nConnecting Continents-Mission Antarctica:\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Application Laboratory (DEAL)\nDEAL entrusted with total communication support for Indian Antarctic station, MAITRI since 1995.DEAL has also started the communication support for the new research station BHARTI in Antarctica’s Larsemann Hills Region. This activity supports multi-institutional scientific endeavor of the nation.\nImages\nConnecting Continents-Mission Antarctica:\nConnecting Continents-Mission Antarctica:"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1842/196", "content": "Back to Listing\nAlocal Cream for Prevention of Cold Injuries\nLabs\nDefence Institute of Physiology & Allied Sciences (DIPAS)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nHerbal, Non Freezing, Safe, Non Toxic, Non greasy and Aloe Vera based cream “ALOCAL” developed to prevent, protect & cure Cold injuries/Frostbite at extreme cold regions Bacterial infections, burns, ulcers, wound and cuts Sunburns, chaffing of cheeks, lips and fingers"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1843/196", "content": "Back to Listing\nErgo Back Pack\nLabs\nDefence Institute of Physiology & Allied Sciences (DIPAS)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nThis is extremely useful to carry military loads during marching, training and other operations with both hands free for postural stability while a separate pouch carries the rifle.\nSalient Features\nBack Pack is an ergonomically designed single compact unit with carrying capacity of 30-50 kilograms in the 75 liter volume.\nDesign allows the adjustability of the back support for different sizes.\nProvides compartmentalization for easy access of frequently used items.\nHydration pack of 1.5 liter capacity is built-in to provide drinking water."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1868/195", "content": "Back to Listing\nDouble Humped Camel for carrying load\nLabs\nDefence Institute of High Altitude Research (DIHAR)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nSimilar to the Zanskar ponies, as per requisition from HQ 14 Corps, a trail is being undertaken by DIHAR to check the feasibility of using the locally available Bactrian (double humped) camels for patrolling and load carrying purpose, especially in the eastern sector bordering China. The initial trial has shown encouraging results and the report will be submitted soon."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1869/195", "content": "Back to Listing\nCattle Development\nLabs\nDefence Institute of High Altitude Research (DIHAR)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nOut of native livestock resource in Ladakh area, Ladakhi cattle play an important role due to survival and adaptability at cold as well as hypobaric hypoxic conditions. Ladakhi Cattle constitutes 56% of total cattle population in Ladakh. The local cattle is a unique germplasm having excellent adaptation potential and a natural source of A2 milk. DIHAR in collaboration with ICAR-NBAGR, Karnal has conducted studies on Ladakhi cattle and is in the process of registering it as 42nd  breed of India. Further, institute is working on the breeding and productive traits of Ladakhi Cattle for selective breeding and thereby producing pool of high producing Ladakhi cattle which in turn will increase milk production of Ladakh. Milk produced by local farmers will be purchased by Army through Cooperatives, thus there will be availability of fresh milk supply to the troops deployed in L-Sector."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1880/195", "content": "Back to Listing\nHigh  altitude adapted cattle\nLabs\nDefence Institute of High Altitude Research (DIHAR)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1882/195", "content": "Back to Listing\nHigh  altitude adapted chicken\nLabs\nDefence Institute of High Altitude Research (DIHAR)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1955/179", "content": "Back to Listing\n5m Short-span Bridging System (SSBS)\nLabs\nResearch & Development Establishment (Engrs.)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nShort Span Bridging System 5m - is a mechanically launched bridging system of MLC-70 load class to bridge small gaps and canals. In addition to bridging the smaller gaps, this bridging system will be compatible with SARVATRA bridging system.\nSalient Features:\nPick and place bridge over gap\nQuick construction with minimum crew\nImages\nSHORT-SPAN BRIDGING SYSTEM (SSBS)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1967/179", "content": "Back to Listing\nBar Mine Layer (BML) Mk-II\nLabs\nResearch & Development Establishment (Engrs.)\nThis is used for quickly creating minefield by burying anti-tank bar mines. The system can carry about 500 bar mines and lay/bury them at intervals of 6m to 30m. Subsequent to the completion of design reviews, prototype is presently under realization.\nImages\nDeployment Mode"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1997/189", "content": "Back to Listing\nElectro-Optical Fire Control System for armoured vehicles and naval ships\nLabs\nInstruments Research & Development Establishment (IRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nElectro-Optical Fire Control System for armoured vehicles and naval ships."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/1998/189", "content": "Back to Listing\nGap Measuring Device Mk III\nLabs\nInstruments Research & Development Establishment (IRDE)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2003/189", "content": "Back to Listing\nCommander’s TI for T-90 Tank\nLabs\nInstruments Research & Development Establishment (IRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nCommander’s TI for T-90 Tank"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2004/189", "content": "Back to Listing\nCommander’s TI (MK-II) for T-72 Tanks & BMP II\nLabs\nInstruments Research & Development Establishment (IRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nCommander’s TI (MK-II) for T-72 Tanks & BMP II"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2008/191", "content": "Back to Listing\n3 D Medium Range Surveillance Radar for Airforce- Rohini\nLabs\nElectronics & Radar Development Establishment (LRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\n3D Medium Range Surveillance Radar is a ground based mechanically scanning Pulse Doppler radar for air space surveillance to detect and track air targets under hostile EW operational environment. early warning for air defence weapon system, air defence sensor at airbases."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2031/166#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nCorrosion-resistant catalyst for acid Fuel cells\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nNMRL has developed a method for production of high surface area; high metal loading electro catalyst on graphitic support for acid fuel cells. The commercial graphitic support is modified to facilitate deposition of noble metal and to increase the durability of support and the catalyst."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2035/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nRubber Nanocomposites for Bushes and Gaskets\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nA special rubber-nanoclay formulation has been developed having superior thermal stability, mechnical properties and adhesion bonding with metal compared to the conventional rubber bushes."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2039/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nPZT-Polymer Elements for Advanced Sonar Transducers\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nPZT polymer composite (Piezocomposite elements and linear arrays for advanced sonar transducers developed by NMRL as a high promise alternative for conventionally used PZT piezoceramic material having the limitation like high acoustic impedance, higher weight factor and poor mechanical properties. The Piezocomposite based sonar transducers exhibit enhanced receiving and transmitting response over a large frequency bandwidth and narrow beam width\nImages\nPZT-Polymer Elements for Advanced Sonar Transducers\nPZT-Polymer Elements for Advanced Sonar Transducers"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2040/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nTransparent Armour\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nTechnology for transparent armour a ceramic material (magnesium aluminates spinel) has been developed. The maximum size of 100 mm × 100 mm × 4 mm (Square) as technology demonstration has been produced using Hot Isostatic Pressing (HIP). This has been tested against 7.62 AP bullet. Technology can be upscaled for any size requirement"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20420/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nRadar Absorbing Structural (Ras) Composites\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nCarbon Veils (CV) and Frequency Selective Surfaces (FSS) based radar Absorbing Structural (RAS) Composites provide stealth capabilities with simultaneously meeting structural and environmental requirements of airborne platforms."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20421/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nMultispectral Personnel Camouflage Equipment (Mspce)\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nMultispectral personnel camouflage equipment (MSPCE), consisting of Suit, Poncho & Screen, provide protection against detection to soldiers operating in different terrains e.g. green belt & jungle, desert and semi desert areas."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20422/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nMobile Camouflage System For Armoured Vehicles\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nMobile Camouflage System (MCS) is an add on system for armoured vehicles to provide multispectral camouflage cover during static and moving conditions."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20423/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nThermally Conducting Light Weight Nanocomposite-Based Structures\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nElectrically insulating and thermally conducting nanocomposites have lower weight, higher viscoelasticity and better dimension stability in comparison to contemporary metal alloys being used for propulsion motor applications."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20424/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nShear Stiffening Gel\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nShear Stiffening Gel shows the change in viscosity as a function of shear force and holds a great promise for damping and shock energy dissipation."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20425/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nPocket Water Filtration Cartridge\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nPocket water filtration cartridge, which fits into plastic water/cold drinks bottle of standard nozzle size, is based on nanofiber-based membrane and changeable prefilters to provide prolonged uninterrupted supply of potable water."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20426/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nQuick Drying Specialty Primer\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nThe quick drying specialty primer is based on acrylic polymer and chromate (ACB – Primer). It has properties at par with the Russian Primer AK – 070."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20427/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nVisual Camouflage Coatings With Laser Absorbing Properties\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nCoatings in twelve different camouflage shades (as per IS-5 standard) prevent or delay the detection of objects by the sensors working in the Visual region and LASERs [ND:YAG (1.060 µm)  and ND:GLASS (1.540 µm]"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20429/171", "content": "Back to Listing\nBallistic Helmet\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20431/171", "content": "Back to Listing\nAnti Personal Mine Blast Protective Suit (APMBPS) For Indian Army\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nAnti Personal Mine Blast Protective Suit is for demining operation under kneeling and prone positions. It Provides protection against accidental blast of APNM M14 mines during demining."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20432/171", "content": "Back to Listing\nACF based CBRN Suit\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nCBRN suit is a multi-component system comprising of an inherent flame retardant with antistatic including oil & water repellent, and outer fabric stitched with adsorbent media."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20438/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nMulti-Spectral Camouflage System\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nMSCS developed for providing protection to the fighter aircrafts MIG-21 & 27, Sukhoi- 30 and Rafale against Visual, EO/IR, Thermal and SAR radar detection devices"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20439/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nModular Gloves\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nModular Gloves that Provide protection to the hands of soldiers under sub-zero temperatures i.e. - 50 ⁰C."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20440/171", "content": "Back to Listing\nAdvanced Riot Protection Suit\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nAdvanced Riot Protection Suit ensuring comprehensive safety to the security personnel in low-intensity conflicts and riot situations. It absorbs the impact and shock load from stone and also against hard objects like batons, knives, and daggers."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20442/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nPEEK Insulator Tube\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nPEEK insulator tube for the fuel line of LCA Tejas. The tube protects the fuel line from thunder and lightning during flight by providing strong insulation on the surface, thus protecting it from any fire-related incident."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20443/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nNuclear Shielding Pads for Combat  Vehicles\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nNuclear Shielding Pads for Infantry combat vehicles (BMK-II and BMK-IIK) and Combat Vehicles (T72 and T90) for protection against nuclear radiation."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20446/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nPolymeric seals for hydro-pneumatic control system for ground and aircraft system\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nElastomeric and thermoplastics seals are intended to use to resist the leakage of air/ oil between the annular space of the shaft and housing."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20448/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nThermally conductive nanofluid\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nThermally conductive nanofluid mitigates the excess heating concern of specific parts of automobiles, mechanical instruments, electronic & electrical device and also engineering process like grinding, material cutting, milling etc."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20449/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nNanolubricants\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nA high performance nanoparticle based nanolubricant is for internal combustion engines (IC engines) to reduce energy loss and enhance overall engine’s efficiency, durability, longevity for smoother operation."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/20451/171#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nLiquid HIDEN fuel (JP-10)\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nJP-10 is HIDEN fuel for missile application as per MIL-DTL-87107D standard."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2046/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nSpecial Alloyed Wire for Submerged Arc and Gas Metal Arc Welding of DMR Grade Shipbuilding Steels\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nWelding wires for submerged arc welding and gas metal arc welding of special grade naval steel has been developed for ships & submarine construction programs of Indian Navy.\nImages\nNMR221/223 GMAW Wire"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2048/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nMagneto Hydrodynamic (MHD) Technique for Grain Refinement of casting\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nA non contact magneto hydrodynamics stirring system has been developed for breaking down undesirable dendritic grain structure and converts into globular fine grains to improve mechanical propertied of cast components and billets\nImages\nLab scale MHD unit\nLM25 MHD billets\nConventional Dendritic cast Microstructure\nGlobular Microstructure  after MHD stirring"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2050/166#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nAmorphous Nano-structured Erosion Corrosion Resistant Coating\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nIron based amorphous/ nano-structured erosion –corrosion resistance coating based on multi-element alloy formulation has been developed for sea water application. Such amorphous / nano structured powders HVOF (High Velocity oxyfuel ) coating provides high strength, high hardness and corrosion-erosion resistance due to absence of crystalline grain defects generally present in conventional metallic coatings\nImages\nMorphology of Iron base amorphous powder\nAmorphous Nano-structured Erosion Corrosion Resistant Coating"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2051/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nFriction Stir Processed Aluminum-Silicon Alloy for Electronic Packaging Application\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nBulk ultrafine grained hypereutectic Al-35% Si and Al-50% Si alloy has been developed by Friction Stir Processing (FSP) technology. The Al -35% Si and Al-50% Si alloy produced by FSP technology possesses ultrafine microstructure and excellent combination of strength, toughness & ease of machining."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2056/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nHigh Performance Exterior Paint\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nA high performance exterior paint having prolonged durability for application on superstructure of ship and excellent resistance to marine environment has been developed."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2057/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nSelf Stratifying Coating\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nA special paint scheme called self stratified coating has been developed for ship superstructure application. In a single coating application, the paint separates into two layers. The bottom layer has excellent anticorrosive property and top exterior coat has excellent weather resistant property."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2058/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nSelf Cleaning Coating\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nA special hydrophobic self cleaning paint formulation has been developed. This is based on polydimethyl siloxane (PDMS) / epoxy system which provides anticorrosive and self cleaning properties in single coat application. Such coating gives dirt free, clean paint surface with reduced maintenance cost.\nImages\nSpreading of dirt Dirt not adhering to coating"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2059/166#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nAnticorrosive and Antifouling Paint for application under Immersed Condition\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nAn anticorrosive and antifouling paint composition has been developed and patented. This can be applied on submerged structures in afloat condition without bringing ships to dry dock.\nImages\nAntifouling and anticorrosive paint Application under immersed condition"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2060/166#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nDeck Overlay Coating\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nCoating for preventing deterioration of floor surfaces of ship due to movement of personnel, materials, vehicles, chemical spillage and cleaning detergent\nImages\nDeck Overlay Coating\nDeck Overlay Coating"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2061/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nSilicone Based Hydrophobic Potting Material\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nNMRL developed silicone based hybrophobic material to avoid polarisation of ICCP reference electrodes, fitted on INS, due to shorting to the hull and ease to maintenance"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2062/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nPeelable Coating\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nRubber based peelable coating used for temporary protection of structures / spares from corrosion /scratches/seepage of water has been developed"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2064/166", "content": "Back to Listing\nImpressed Current Cathodic Protection (ICCP) anodes\nLabs\nNaval Materials Research Laboratory (NMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nImpressed current cathodic protection (ICCP) anodes have been developed for protection of ships using non-consumables inert electrodes in systems. Lead- silver alloy anode are being used for majority of Naval ships while platinised titanium anode are being used in Naval ships requiring higher current density\nImages\nLead-Silver Alloy ICCP Anode\nPlatinised Titanium anode"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2092/182", "content": "Back to Listing\nAkash\nLabs\nDefence Research & Development Laboratory (DRDL)\nTechnology Cluster\nMissiles and Strategic Systems (MSS)\nAKASH is a Short Range Surface to Air Missile system to protect vulnerable areas and vulnerable points from air attacks. AKASH Weapon System can simultaneously engage Multiple Targets in Group Mode or Autonomous Mode. It has built in Electronic Counter-Counter Measures (ECCM) features. The entire weapon system has been configured on mobile platforms. AKASH Weapon Systems has been inducted and is operational with the Indian Air Force (IAF) as well as the Indian Army (IA)."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2093/182", "content": "Back to Listing\nASTRA\nLabs\nDefence Research & Development Laboratory (DRDL)\nTechnology Cluster\nMissiles and Strategic Systems (MSS)\nASTRA is a Beyond Visual Range (BVR) class of Air-to-Air Missile (AAM) system designed to be mounted on fighter aircraft. The missile is designed to engage and destroy highly manoeuvring supersonic aircraft. The missile has all weather day and night capability. The missile is being developed in multiple variants to meet specific requirements. The ASTRA Mk-I Weapon System integrated with SU-30 Mk-I aircraft is being inducted into the Indian Air Force (IAF)."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2099/182", "content": "Back to Listing\nMan-Portable Anti Tank Guided Missile\nLabs\nDefence Research & Development Laboratory (DRDL)\nTechnology Cluster\nMissiles and Strategic Systems (MSS)\nThis missile is for infantry and Parachute (Special Forces) of the Indian Army. It is 'Soft' launched from a canister using an Ejection Motor. It uses a state-of-the-art IIR seeker for homing on to the target.\n \nThe man portable missile, and launched using a tripod is designed for a max. range of 2.5 Km with a launch weight less than 15 Kg, Control Flight Tests have been successfully carried out and Guided Flight Tests (with IIR Seeker) are planned."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2121/188", "content": "Back to Listing\nAJANTA\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nAJANTA is a shipborne Electronic Warfare (EW) system. The system is a single operator, computer controlled Integrated Electronic Support Measure (ESM) & Electronic Counter Measures (ECM) system, designed for installation on frigates.The ESM system covers wide frequency range and has capability to process both pulse and CW type of emissions. The ECM system of Ajanta Operates in noise and deception jamming modes. Twenty systems have been successfully inducted into the Navy since 1991."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2122/188", "content": "Back to Listing\nCOIN-A\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nIt is a vehicle mounted Communication Intelligence (COMINT) system developed for the Indian Air Force. The system is capable of surveillance, interception, monitoring, analysis and direction finding of hostile communication signals in the VHF/UHF bands. Two systems have been successfully inducted into the Indian Air Force in 1995."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2124/188", "content": "Back to Listing\nCATCH\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nIt is an airborne SIGINT system to cater for communication and radar intelligence. It covers UHF to Microwave frequency band and provides high sensitivity employing superhet receiver. Two systems have been inducted on IAF aircrafts."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2137/188", "content": "Back to Listing\nAEW&C (CSM) and Indigenous ESM & RWR Systems for AEW&C\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nThe Communication Support Measures for AEW&C systemhas been successfully developed. The system has the capability for Surveillance of communication signals in V/UHF bands, Interception, Analysis of Voice and Data Signals, Direction Finding and Location Fixing of Communication threats, identification of threats through correlation of Signal Database and Reporting in Real-time. It can also Intercept and Record wideband Signals in Microwave band.Installation and performance evaluation of Indigenous ESM & RWR Systems on AEW&C platform is completed. The system is under user evaluation for acceptance."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2153/184", "content": "Back to Listing\nNavigation Technologies & Systems\nLabs\nResearch Centre Imarat (RCI)\nTechnology Cluster\nMissiles and Strategic Systems (MSS)\nFiber Optic Gyros (FOG), Ring Laser Gyros (RLG) and MEMS Gyro Systems based Navigation Systems integrated with SATNAV receivers have been developed in house to meet the requirements of various projects.\nFOG based INS for tactical applications.\nNavigation Systems for Land, Ship and Airborne applications.\nRedundant Navigation Systems for Long Range applications.\nHybrid Navigation Systems with integrated GNSS receivers.\nTransfer alignment schemes for airborne, ship borne and underwater missiles."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2155/184", "content": "Back to Listing\nControl Systems Technologies & Products\nLabs\nResearch Centre Imarat (RCI)\nTechnology Cluster\nMissiles and Strategic Systems (MSS)\nControl Actuation Systems (Pneumatic/Hydraulic/Electrical) have been successfully developed for various Aerospace Applications including Ballistic missiles, Unmanned Aerial Vehicles, Cruise missiles and fighter aircraft.\nElectro Hydraulic Servo Actuator\nElectro Hydraulic Servo Valve (Flapper Nozzle & Jet Pipe)\nElectro Mechanical Servo Actuator (Linear & Rotary)\nQuick Response Solenoid Valve\nLinear Variable Differential Transformer (LVDT) Sensor"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/21569/21422", "content": "Back to Listing\nChilli Spray (CapsisprayTM)\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nThe product is novel and eco-friendly non-lethal weapon, based on oleoresin extracted from Bhut Jolokia, which is one of the hottest chilli in the world and endemic to North Eastern States of India including Assam\nMain Features\nEco-friendly non-lethal & Severe Irritant\nSuitable for Low Intensity Conflict areas & Riot Control\nPersonal Protection and self-Defence\nAvailable in different sizes from 50 ml cane to 50 liters Cylinder\nTrolley mounted & back pack for easy transportation"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/21570/21422", "content": "Back to Listing\nChilli Grenade (CapsigrenadeTM)\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nCapsigrenade, an indigenous product, has been formulated using oleoresin extracted from Bhut Jolokia which is one of the hottest chilli in the world and endemic to North Eastern States of India including Assam.\nMain Features\nSuitable for Low Intensity Conflict areas\nMob Dispersal & riot control\nEffective for use in\"Hostage Crisis Management"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/21577/21422", "content": "Back to Listing\nDearsenification Unit (DAU)\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nIn recent days, the arsenic contamination in ground water of NE India is an alarming condition. DRL had developed Dearsenification unit to provide arsenic free drinking water\nMain Features\nRemoval Efficiency: Arsenic:    500 ppb to < 10 ppb [desirable limit set by WHO/BIS]\nIron: 50 ppm to < 0.3 ppm [desirable limit set by WHO/BIS]\nStructure: Cylindrical: Made of mild steel (MK I) & FRP (MK II)\nFiltration rate             : 200L/Hr"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2157/184", "content": "Back to Listing\nFlight Instrumentation Technologies & Products\nLabs\nResearch Centre Imarat (RCI)\nTechnology Cluster\nMissiles and Strategic Systems (MSS)\nTelemetry, Tele command, Transponder and Data Communication Systems, essential for real time performance monitoring of flight vehicles have been successfully developed and produced and used in various projects.\nCompact & high bandwidth Datalink and Telemetry.\nTele-Command & Transponder for missile applications."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/21582/21422", "content": "Back to Listing\nDRDO Biotoilet for Floating conditions\nLabs\nDefence Research Laboratory (DRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nDue to human excrements, river and lakes are getting contaminated and eutrophication is happening. Many a lake (as per example Dal lake, Srinagar) can be saved from incorporation of human excreta through DRDO based Biotoilet technology. This variants DRDO Biotoilet for Floating condition can address the issue.\nMain Features:\nDesigned for treatment under floating conditions in lakes and rivers with easy serviceability and toeing (if required).\nHouseboat sanitation (eg. Dal Lake, Kashmir) can appropriately be addressed.\nProvision for working in freezing condition.\nEffluent water quality as per environmental norms."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2210/201", "content": "Back to Listing\nAlGaN/GaN Multifinger HEMT\nLabs\nSolid State Physics Laboratory (SSPL)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/22157/18589", "content": "Back to Listing\nInfantry Protected Mobility Vehicle (IPMV)\nLabs\nVehicles Research and Development Establishment (VRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nWheeled 8x8 Configuration, 600 hp engine, fully automatic transmission, 7.62 mm RCWS, Ballistic protection with composite add-on Armour & blast protection for the crew. Order directly placed by Indian Army for Infantry Protected Mobility Vehicle (IPMV) after successful trials of WhAP at Leh-Ladhak region."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/22161/18589", "content": "Back to Listing\nCBRN Recce Vehicle Mk-II (Tracked)\nLabs\nVehicles Research and Development Establishment (VRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nThe CBRN Recce vehicle (Tracked) Mk-II is a reconnaissance platform capable of detecting, identifying, monitoring and marking of areas contaminated with CBRN agents and transmit this information to the supported formations. The vehicle is based on BMP-II platform re-engineered to accommodate different systems required for CBRN Recce purpose. The CBRN Reconnaissance Vehicle (Tracked) Mark- II will be used in plains and desert/semi deserts terrains."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/22167/18589", "content": "Back to Listing\n70 T Tank Transporter for MBT Arjun\nLabs\nVehicles Research and Development Establishment (VRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nThe weight of MBT Arjun- Mk 1A is 68t. As a tactical and strategic mobility, the MBT’s need to be transported up to the battle – field on the special transporter with tractor and full trailer combination by road. VRDE, Ahmednagar has developed full trailer for the above purpose. Full trailer realized through DRDO nominated Production Agency (PA) and DRDO Internal trials with MBT Arjun MK-1 A completed."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/22168/18589", "content": "Back to Listing\n180 Hp Diesel Engine for UAV\nLabs\nVehicles Research and Development Establishment (VRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nVRDE has developed the high specific power diesel engine for Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV). The Indigenous engine produces take-off power of 180 hp constant up to 11,000 ft. The engine has been successfully tested for power, Thrust and fuel consumption on the Dynamometer and Thrust cradle. The Fully Authority Digital Engine Control (FADEC) system is indigenously developed and extensively tested with engine. The engine is tested and validated for high-altitude performance for altitude up-to 17, 664 at Leh and Changla. Also, the engine has been extensively proven for 1100+ hours on stringent test profiles. The taxi trials of the indigenous engines were completed successfully with UAV."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2332/201", "content": "Back to Listing\nAlGaN/GaN HEMT\nLabs\nSolid State Physics Laboratory (SSPL)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2333/201", "content": "Back to Listing\nAlGaN/GaN HEMT Processed Wafer\nLabs\nSolid State Physics Laboratory (SSPL)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2470/140", "content": "Back to Listing\nPilot Mental Workload Assessment Simulator\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nThis   state-of-the-art   Simulator based on Real Time Simulator (RTS) and three channel visual projection display system along with cylindrical screen integrated with other psycho physiological measurement systems are especially established to assess the mental workload of fighter pilots. This facility is used to get a real time data capture for mental workload studies. The data collection is mission &task based and as such would help in building statistical models to arrive at the pilot’s work load for a given task and estimate the spare capacity of the pilot for better utilization.\nImages\nPilot Mental Workload Assessment Simulator"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2473/140", "content": "Back to Listing\nNirbhay\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nNirbhay is a Long Range Sub-Sonic Cruise Missile capable of deep penetration into adversary territory to strike high value targets with precision.  Aeronautical Development Establishment (ADE) as the system designer and integrator led a consortium of DRDO laboratories for the indigenous design and development of Nirbhay. Presently, Nirbhay is launched from a mobile articulated launcher. This Missile is being adopted for launch from sea and air platforms.  India is in the list of select few countries having capability to design and develop this class of cruise missiles. 6th flight of Nirbhay was successfully completed on 15 April 2019."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2474/140", "content": "Back to Listing\nPanchi\nLabs\nAeronautical Development Establishment (ADE)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nPanchi is a variant of Nishant (launcher based tactical UAV) with capability of conventional take-off and landing. Panchi is integrated with  an  all  composite  landing  gear  and  has  improved  flight envelope and endurance. Panchi carries a stabilized payload platform. It carries payloads like daylight camera, infrared camera and laser designator. It is powered with an indigenously developed rotary Wankel engine. It has state of art systems, capable of surveillance, reconnaissance, target location detection and artillery fire correction.\nFive flights of Panchi have been successfully completed proving the concept of conventional takeoff and landing. Data for aerodynamic, structure integrity and Flight control studies have been generated and analyzed."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2489/480", "content": "Back to Listing\nINMAS Products\nLabs\nInstitute of Nuclear Medicine & Allied Sciences (INMAS)\nProducts developed / under development\nNBC Medical Emergency Kit\nShudhika (Skin decontamination Kit)\nCiprofloxacin Cold Kit for Infection Scintigraphy: 'Diagnobact'\nLight Weight Foldable Stretcher\nLight weight back pack type Army field Cot\nRemcon for decontamination Wipes\nRadioprotective and radiomitigative drugs\nHigh throughput assays for quick estimation of absorbed radiation dose\nEstablishment of accredited bio-dosimetry lab.\nSingle Vial Cold Kit (Diagnomamo)\nVasodilator ointments for cold injury\nITAD therapy in cases of High Altitude Pulmonary edema and acute mountain sickness (8 products)\nGastric Pro kinetic drugs for instant action\nHerbal radioprotectors against ionizing and non-ionizing radiation\nUMBRIEL-the UV Herbal Screen for high Altitude\nNBC antidote formulations\nNano-iron with lecithin\nNano-calcium with lecithin\nAnti-epilepsy nasal drops\nClove oil-neem oil chewing gum (SR)\nDoxycycline local acting chewing gum (with chitosan)\nFluticasone local acting chewing gum (with chitosan)\nHoCl products\nEno heavy\nHandbook of Radiation Protection Manual\nTitanium Bone Implants, Surgical Kit & other devices\nImaging Agents (99mTc, 2DG)\nAdjuvent Cancer Therapy with 2-Deoxyglucose\nTechnology Transfer\nTitanium Bone Implants, Surgical Kit & other devices\nShudhika (Skin decontamination Kit)\nCiprofloxacin Cold Kit for Infection Scintigraphy: 'Diagnobact'\nLight Weight Foldable Stretcher\nLight weight back pack type Army field Cot.\nAdjuvent Cancer Therapy with 2-Deoxyglucose\nUMBRIEL-the UV Herbal Screen for high Alltitude\nRemcon for decontamination Wipes."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2507/179", "content": "Back to Listing\nAircraft-arrester barrier system\nLabs\nResearch & Development Establishment (Engrs.)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nThis system offers safe and reliable arresting solutions for combat aircrafts in case of emergencies during landing overrun or aborted take-off. Arrester Barrier Systems are available in two variants: -\nFor 6 to 20 ton class aircraft\nFor 9 to 40 ton class aircraft"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2509/179", "content": "Back to Listing\nAir-storage and delivery system for ‘Aditya'\nLabs\nResearch & Development Establishment (Engrs.)\nA trailer based system for generating; storing and delivering high-pressure compressed air has been realized for project ‘Aditya’. The system is under integration and testing."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2629/174", "content": "Back to Listing\n120 mm Armaments for ARJUN MBT\nLabs\nArmament Research & Development Establishment (ARDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nArmament & Combat Engineering Systems (ACE)\nA super velocity 120mm Main Armament and family of ammunition with FSAPDS as the primary kinetic energy kill mechanism has been developed. The armament and ammunition system are under production at OFB."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2631/174", "content": "Back to Listing\n125mm FSAPDSMk-II Ammunition\nLabs\nArmament Research & Development Establishment (ARDE)\n125mm FSAPDS Mk-II, ammunition has resulted in quantum jump in firepower performance of our T-72/T-90 tank. The project has successfully undergone User trial."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2633/174", "content": "Back to Listing\n120 mm Penetration Cum Blast (PCB) AND Thermobaric (TB) Ammunition For MBT Arjun\nLabs\nArmament Research & Development Establishment (ARDE)\nARDE has developed Penetration-Cum-Blast (PCB) and Thermobaric (TB) ammunition in order to increase the capacity of Arjun Main Battle Tank to neutralize a wide range of targets. Design commonality with existing ammunition has been achieved and hence the PCB/TB ammunition can be accommodated in the existing configuration of Arjun MBT. PCB ammunition is capable of defeating hard concrete targets and TB ammunition is effective against soft skinned targets. PCB/TB ammunition provides possibility of application in urban warfare scenario."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2653/201", "content": "Back to Listing\nAdvanced Semiconductor Products & Technology\nLabs\nSolid State Physics Laboratory (SSPL)\nAdvanced Semiconductor Products & Technology\nAlGaN/GaN HEMTprocessed wafer\nAlGaN/GaN Multifinger HEMT\nLaser Diode Module\nSingle Stage Thermoelectric Cooler\nStirling Cryocooler\nCW Laser Diode 4W\nSAW based e-Nasika\nAcoustic Emission Sensor for Snow Avalanche Prediction\nCNT based NOx sensor (n-Nasika)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2697/198", "content": "Back to Listing\nAutoject Injectors MK-II\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nSalient Features:\n• The auto injectors are handy devices for immediate administration of atropine sulphate and PAM chloride which are injectables and have to be & administered immediately by the individuals exposed to nerve agents.\n• The auto injectors contain drug filled cartridges with needle inside for intramuscular administration by pressing a trigger.\n• Technology transferred to industries for commercialization.\n• Product inducted into services."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2704/193#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nSurvival Ration\nLabs\nMRE & Rations\nVegetable pulav\nPlain Rice\nVegetable noodle\nCurry\nPotato peas curry\nRajam curry\nDal fry\nPaneer peas curry\nEgg curry\nChicken curry\nChicken pulav\nOther Ready to eat (RTE) products\nChapthies\nNo preservative chapaties\nPreserved and flavouredchapathies\nShort term preserved chapathies\nStuffed parothas\nFlavoured Chapattis\nPuff & serve chapathies\nEnergy Foods\nAppetizers\nChicken biscuits\nFlax cookies\nFlax munch\nCoco cocoa delight bar\nComposite tasty bar\nErgogenic bar\nFlax oat tasty bar\nHigh energy bar\nOmega-3-rich bar\nProtein rich mutton bar\nNutri food bar\nSweet & sour tasty bar\nInstant & Mix Foods\nReady to reconstitute / ready to cook products\nInstant coconut chutney mix\nInstant cooking pulses and dal flakes\nInstant cooking rice\nInstant dal curries\nInstant idly sambar mix\nInstant sojihalwa mix\nInstant upma mix\nInstant whole pulse and their curries\nVariety of freeze dried fruit juice powders\nSea buckthorn based herbal tea\nSea buckthorn based spiced squash\nFlax chapathi mix\nFlax sweet mix\nMillet kheer mix\nMillet chapathi mix\nMillet roti mix\nMillet dosa mix\nMillet pakoda mix\nMillet halwa mix\nMillet dokla mix\nRagi cookie mix\nBeverages\nAppetizer mix\nMillet beverage mix\nReady to drink juices and Beverages\nTender coconut water\nAloe passion drink\nBrahmi drink\nAsh gourd juices\nAlovera juice\nVegetable juices\nSea buckthorn based spiced squash\nSea buckthorn based herbal tea\nVariety of freeze dried fruit juice powders\nOther Food Products\nEthylene absorbing formulation\nMinimally processed vegetables\nPreservative coating for fruits & vegetables\nHurdle technology based preserved fruits & vegetables"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2705/193#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nFood Test kits\nLabs\nTest Kits\nMeat Test kit\nMilk adulteration kit\nFrozen/Chilled Chicken/Meat Quality Evaluation Field kit\nTest kit for E. coli detection\nPesticide detection kit\nPresumptive test kit for coliform detection\nAcidity testing paper strips\nTest kits for food borne pathogens / toxin"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2709/198#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nPersonal Decontamination Kit\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nIntroduction:\nPDK was designed to decontaminate small arms and ammunition by physical removal. PDK houses PDK-1, PDK-2 and RDP.\nPDK-1 is fuller earth based cotton pouches which can remove small droplets from the contaminated surfaces while PDK-2 is used to remove large volume of contaminants from contaminated surfaces.\nRDP is designed to remove nuclear/radiological dust.\nDescription:\nThis kit consists of three components:\n(a)\nPDK-I\n(b)\nPDK-II\n(c)\nRDP\nApplications:\nIt is used for the decontamination of CW agents by physical adsorption from human body, small areas on clothing, gloves, shoes, personal weapons etc.\nShelf Life & Storage Conditions:\n5 Years under factory packed conditions\nThe product can be stored normally at damp free location at 25c with maximum relative humidity of 50%\nPresent Status:\nBulk produced and inducted into the services."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2710/198#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nPortable Chemical Agent Detector (PCAD)\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nSalient Features:\nBased on Ion Mobility Spectrometry (IMS) Technology.\nHand held CWA Detector for Point detection.\nResponse Time:- < 60 Second, Recovery Time:- < 3 Minutes\nCan detect all chemical warfare agents and selected Toxic industrial chemicals.\nAudible and visual alarms."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2711/198#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nPortable Decontamination Apparatus (PDA)\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nSalient Features:\nPortable decontamination apparatus (DAP) is used for decontamination of vehicles, ships, area and buildings at a safe distance.\nDAP is made up of stainless steel with provision for pressurizing manually as well as from a vehicle compressor.\nDAP is designed for working at a safe distance from the contaminated surface.\nThe DAP is meant for decontamination purposes on a small scale.\nShelf Life of DAP is 5 Years for all non metallic components and 10 years for metallic components."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2712/198#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nPortable Gas Chromatograph\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nIntroduction\n:\nPortable Gas chromatograph is an area monitoring system working on chromate-graphic principle.\nUsed for the detection of chemical warfare vapors present in the environment.\nIt can detect nerve and blister agents.\nSalient Features:\nDetection and monitoring of G&H agents\nWeight 18Kg\nPresent Status:\nHanded over to services and Fitted in NBC Recce vechicle."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2713/198#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nResidual Vapour Detection Kit (RVD)\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nIntroduction:\nThe RVD kit is designed to detect CW agents in field.\nThe kit comprises of six different types specially made tubes with reagents to give color change upon reaction with CW agents.\nThis kit meets the requirement of the detection of CW agent up to 10 ppm.\nSalient Features:\nThe kit is used to detect CW agents by sucking the contaminated air from atmosphere with the help of sampling pump provided with the kit.\nThe detection of contaminants is based on appearance of color change.\nThis kit can detect CW agents: Ammonia, COCI, CNCl, HCN, Nerve agents and HD.\nShelf Life & Storage Conditions:\n2 Years. The product can be stored normally at damp free locations at 25c with maximum relative humidity of 50%.\nPresent Status:\nBulk produced and inducted into the services."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2714/198#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nThree Color Detector Paper (TCD)\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nIntroduction:\nThree color detector paper is a what man 501 based detector paper which is coated with mixture of dyes to detect H,G and V agents in aerosol/liquids form. It performs qualitative detection of CW agents.\nApplications:\nThree color detector papers are to detect minute’s droplets of H, V and G agents, when they fall upon it.\nThis paper is having sticking capability and can be fixed static and movable object.\nShelf Life & Storage Conditions:\n2 Years under factory packed conditions. The product can be stored normally at damp free location with maximum relative humidity of 75%\nPresent Status:\nBulk produced and inducted into the services."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2715/198", "content": "Back to Listing\nAnthrax Detection Kit\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nAnthrax Detection Kit\nBacillus anthracis, the causative agent of anthrax, is a large, gram-positive, non-motile, spore-forming rod shaped bacterium. Besides being one of the most important biological warfare agents, it causes public health problems in both, animals and humans. Human anthrax has three major clinical forms: cutaneous, inhalational and gastrointestinal. Early treatment of cutaneous, anthrax is usually curative and early treatment of all forms is important for recovery.\nIntended Use:\nThe assay is intended for serodiagnosis of Anthrax infection in human/animal serum samples.\nSalient Features:\nSpecific recombinant protein based Immuno flow through assay kit for serodiagnosis of anthrax\nThe kit are based broadly on principles of indirect ELISA\nThe kit can be used at point of care centers\nThe kits have been evaluated on human and animals serum samples"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2721/198#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nJapanese Encephalitis (JE) IgM ELISA Kit\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nSalient Features:\nKit is based on indirect ELISA principle.\nUtilizes recombinant envelope protein.\nTime required: 2 hrs.\nSuitable for both laboratory and field settings.\nToT to M/S Qualpro Diagnostics, Goa"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2723/198", "content": "Back to Listing\nBiodigester\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nSalient features:\nEco-friendly & cost-effective\nMinimal maintenance\nNo need for sludge removal\nNo need for water seal (P-trap) in toilet\nMore than 90% organic matter reduction\nMore than 99% pathogens reduction\nGeneration of odorless & inflammable biogas\nBiodigester can tolerate toilet cleaning agents to certain extent\nTechnology transferred to industries for commercialization"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2725/198", "content": "Back to Listing\nBiodigester for Indian Railways\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nSalient features:\nEco-friendly & cost-effective\nMinimal maintenance\nNo need for sludge removal\nMore than 90% organic matter reduction\nMore than 99% pathogens reduction\nGeneration of odorless & inflammable biogas\nBiodigester can tolerate toilet cleaning agents to certain extent\nTechnology transferred to industries for commercialization"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2729/198#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nSlow Release Insecticidal Paint (SRIP)\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nIntroduction:\nCrawling insects like cockroaches, bedbugs, flies are nuiscence as well as carrier of pathogens. Although various insecticides are recommended for management of these insects, repeated use of insecticides is harmful to human health. Keeping this in mind, DRDE Gwalior has developed a Slow Release Insecticidal Paint (SRIP) that can be applied on various surfaces to kill any crawling insects that comes in contact for a period of minimum one year.\n \nSuccessful field trials of SRIP have been conducted in DRDE, Indian Naval ships, in Indian railways and also in Indian Tourism Development Corporation (ITDC).\nSalient Features:\nSRIP is a ready to use formulation. Ideally suited for use in kitchen, restaurants, warehouses, hospitals, ships, ports, railways etc.\nPainted surface dries rapidly within an hour.\nPainted surface retains insecticidal activity for more than year.\nSafe and effective against variety of crawling insects.\nIndian patent for this paint has been awarded.\nBenefits:\nSingle application of SRIP can kill crawling insects for more than year where repeated application of insecticides can be avoided.\nHow to Use:\nApply SRIP uniformly on any surface like wall, wood, metal et. using paint brush. After drying, apply another coat.\nCurrent Status:\nTechnology has been transferred to two firms."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2730/198#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nWater Poison Detection Kit\nLabs\nDefence Research Development Establishment (DRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nIntroduction:\nWPDK has been developed to detect inorganic poisons, sulphur mustard, nerve agents and microbial contamination in water.\nKit can detect cyanide, lead, copper, arsenic, manganese and mercury. WPDK meets the requirement of WHO.\nApplications:\nThe kit can be used for testing the water sources (for metallic contaminants such as Hg, Mn, Cu, Pb, As and BW agents such as fecal bacteria microbes, cyanides, HD and Nerve agents) in areas like reservoirs, tanks, wells etc. in field during the hostile environment and also for routine under normal conditions.\nShelf Life & Storage Conditions:\n2 Years under factory packed conditions. The product can be stored normally at damp free location at 25c with maximum relative humidity of 50%.\nPresent Status:\nBulk produced and inducted into the services."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2789/196", "content": "Back to Listing\nERGONOMICALLY DESIGNED LIGHT WEIGHT BOOTS\nLabs\nDefence Institute of Physiology & Allied Sciences (DIPAS)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nFeatures:\nLight weight 1.5 kg with shock absorbing insole.\nSalient Features\nImproves balance and stability during standing and walking with and without external load.\nReduces risk of ligament injuries during walking.\nReduce transfer of force to lower extremity during running/walking\nDelayed onset of fatigue\nEnhance comfort /safety specially during heavy load carriage task.\nAnti-skid, anti-static, composite toe cap, anti-penetration, speed wearing facility.\nToT Holders:\n1) M/s\nProsafe\nInt Pvt Ltd. Plot E345, RIIC Ind Area, Bhiwadi – 301019, Contact: 9602525928\n2) M/s S\nuperHouse\nLtd, B-6 Site, UPSIDC Ind Area, Unnao – 209801, Contact: 9839808363\n3) M/s\nModel Exims\n, Plot No. A 32, Leather Technology Park, UPSIDC Banthar, Unnao, Contact: 0515 2824052\n4)M/s\nHomera Tanning Industries\n1-D (17-A-1) 150 Road Jajmau, Kanpur – 208010 Contact: 0512 2460701"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2790/196", "content": "Back to Listing\nActive Ear Defender\nLabs\nDefence Institute of Physiology & Allied Sciences (DIPAS)\nTechnology Cluster\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nNoise induced hearing loss in military and industrial environment is considered one of the most common occupational health hazards. Incidences of noise induced hearing loss are very high in different military and industrial environments.\nDesigned to:\nProtect from Noise Induced Hearing Loss\nReduce noise over complete audible range\nProvide low and high frequency noise reduction\nEnable intelligibility of speech in noisy environment/workplace\nUtility :\nSafeguard Hearing\nIntact speech intelligibility\nApplication :\nDefence: Army workshops, Airforce Station Crew, Ships Engine Room Civil: Industrial Workshop\nToT Holder:\n1. M/s Ajit Technoplast Pvt.Ltd.,104/430,P Road, Kanpur-208012, Uttar Pradesh, India Contact No. : 9335036523/991839697\n2.\nM/s Bajaj Engineers & Consultant\n491-492 Modern Industrial Estates Bahadurgarh Contact: 9811154599\n3.\nM/s Netplast Pvt. Ltd\n. 2& 4 Uptron Estate, Panki, Kanpur-208022 Contact No.: 9336836886\n4.\nM/s Argus Technologies\nPlot No 38, Phase II, 2nd Kamlapuri Colony Hyderabad. Contact No. 7093535378"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2859/144", "content": "Back to Listing\nIdentification Friend or Foe (IFF) MK XII (S) with Mode 4 Capability\nLabs\nCentre For Air Borne System (CABS)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nIFF system has been developed for both airborne, ground and ship applications. IFF is available in three flavors namely Interrogator, Transponder OR Combined interrogator and Transponder units. The IFF system can be integrated with any Mode 4 Crypto Unit with a standard STANAG interface. The IFF is under production and available with several private vendors in India."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2861/144", "content": "Back to Listing\nGround Exploitation System (GES)\nLabs\nCentre For Air Borne System (CABS)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nThe Ground Exploitation Station is a transportable field deployable system, which can receive the information from AEW&C system both through a LOS and Satellite Data Links. The GES can be located in remote locations, thereby enabling the availability of the air situation picture around them in real time."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/2873/184", "content": "Back to Listing\nImaging Infra-Red (IIR) Seeker systems\nLabs\nResearch Centre Imarat (RCI)\nTechnology Cluster\nMissiles and Strategic Systems (MSS)\nImaging Infra-Red (IIR) Seeker systems have been successfully flight tested in Anti-Tank Guided Missiles Nag, HELINA and MPATGM. IIR Seekers have also been successfully demonstrated in the Exo-Atmospheric Interceptor PDV and Anti Satellite Test (ASAT), Mission Shakti.\nImages\nImaging Infra-Red (IIR) Seeker system"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/5215/175", "content": "Back to Listing\n5 kW brushless DC Generating system for LCA Tejas\nLabs\nCombat Vehicles Research & Development Establishment (CVRDE)\nState-of-the-art 5 kW Brushless DC Generator (BLDC) is developed for LCA-Tejas to support critical electrical loads for flight safety during emergency when main AC generator fails. Generator comprises of Permanent Magnet stage, Main Exciter and Main Generator facilitating autonomous mode. FPGA/DSP based embedded controller featuring precise voltage regulation with BITE facility to meet stringent MIL standards of voltage regulation. This BLDC generator has successfully completed 1250 hours of Endurance test."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/795/191", "content": "Back to Listing\n3D Surveillance Radar for Indian Navy -Revathi\nLabs\nElectronics & Radar Development Establishment (LRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\n3D Surveillance Radar for Indian Navy is a ship borne Radar. The radar has digital receiver, programmable signal processor providing high resolution, accuracy, response and information availability. The radar can auto track upto 150 targets including tracking with IFF (Mk XI) association. There are three Antenna Rotation Rates (ARR) of 6, 12, 24 RPMs. The radar has ECCM features."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/796/192", "content": "Back to Listing\nCombat Free Fall System (CFF)\nLabs\nAerial Delivery Research and Development Establishment (ADRDE)\nDefence Bio-Engineering & Electro Medical Laboratory (DEBEL)\nTechnology Cluster\nAeronautical Systems (Aero)\nSoldier Support System (SSS)\nCFF parachute system provides total solutions to Paratrooper for jumping from height as high as 30,000 ft., can glide up to 30 km range and can land at the desired target. System can be used in High Altitude High Opening (HAHO) as well as in High Altitude Low Opening (HALO) modes. CFF parachute system has been inducted into Services."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/803/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nTorpedo Advanced Light (TAL)\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nTorpedo Advanced Light  (TAL) is an electrically propelled self-homing torpedo and can be launched from ship and rotary wing aircraft. It has both active and passive modes of operations, and all digital control and guidance systems. TAL is an anti submarine weapon, which can attack submarines in shallow waters & deep waters.\nSalient Features\nHigh power seawater activated battery\nOperating Depth 450 m\nWeight (War head version) 220 kg"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/905/168", "content": "Back to Listing\nVarunastra\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nVarunastra is ship launched, heavy weight, electrically-propelled anti-submarine torpedo capable of targeting quiet submarines, both in deep and shallow waters in an intense countermeasures environment. Varunastra can be fired from all ASW ships capable of firing heavy weight torpedoes. VARUNASTRA has been inducted by Indian Navy in 2016.\nImages\nVARUNASTRA\nVARUNASTRA\nVarunastra"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/927/167#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nABHAY\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nABHAY is Compact Hull Mounted Sonar System for Ships. It is an active cum passive sonar system, specifically targeted for installation on small to medium platforms such as Anti-Submarine Warfare (ASW) Corvettes and patrol vessels."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/929/167#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nAIDSS\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nAdvanced Indigenous Distress Sonar System (AIDSS) is the crisis management system for submarines, to indicate that a submarine is in distress."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/technology-cluster-links/labs-products-detail/940/168#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nHelicoptor Fire Control System\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nA helicopter fire control system (HFCS) has been developed by DRDO for the naval ALH. The HFCS interfaces to dunking SONAR and helicopter motion sensors, for subsurface and surface target tracking. lt performs contact motion analysis (CMA) and generates fire control solutions.\nThe system pre-sets and releases TAL and A244S torpedoes, and depth charge Mk ll. The HFCS meets MIL STD 810E and 462C EMI/EMC for airborne applications. Three systems have been delivered to Hindustan Aeronautics Limited.\nSalient Features\nInterface to Dunking Sonar and Tactical Mission System.\nGeneration of FCS by Contact Motion Analysis (CMA).\nWeapon preset and interface modules.\nContra Rotating Propellers\nConduction cooled chassis.\nWeapon preset and interface modules for TAL & A244S torpedoes.\nRecord & replay facility\nCapable to release depth- charges"},
