{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/tempest#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nTEMPEST\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nThis is an airborne self-protection jammer system developed for fighter aircrafts. This system has both ECM and ESM resources. The ECM system consists of deception jammers, pulse Doppler jammers and pulse repeater jammers. Low Band system consists of a mini pod Jammer which is external to the aircraft. Two systems were produced for IAF."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/terahertz#top", "content": "Technology Category\nTechnology Development Task\nLab\nCommunication\nWireless Terahertz Communication System for the identified use cases for Defence applications\nDEAL\nImaging\nCompact Terahertz (THz) source with sufficiently high power to illuminate the object and THz beam collimating/ scanning optics (THz collimating optics/off-axis parabolic mirrors)\nIRDE\nHigh Impact Terahertz Source Based Imaging\nIRDE\nMicro-Electromechanical System (MEMS) based TeraHertz Imaging Sensor\nSSPL\nPlasmonics enhanced 2D Photoconductive Antenna (PCA) based Terahertz (THz) Imaging\nSSPL\nCommunication\nTera Hz beam forming front end for small unit network operations\nDEAL"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/terms-conditions#top", "content": "This website is designed, developed and maintained by Defence R&D Organisation (DRDO), Ministry of Defence, Government of India. DESIDOC, a constituent of DRDO, is the nodal agency for this activity.\nThese terms and conditions shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the Indian Laws. Any dispute arising under these terms and conditions shall be subject to the jurisdiction of the courts of India, New Delhi.\nThe information posted on this website could include hypertext links or pointers to information created and maintained by non-Government/private organisations. DRDO is providing these links and pointers solely for your information and convenience. When you select a link to an outside website, you are leaving the 'Guidelines for Indian Government Websites' site and are subject to the privacy and security policies of the owners/sponsors of the outside website."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/test-facilities#top", "content": "Access of DRDO Test Facilities to Industries\nDownload (26.6 KB Docx)\nList of Test Facilities\nDRDO Test Facilities for Industries Download (288 KB Pdf)\nContact Details\nDirector\nDirectorate of Industry Interface and Technology Management (DIITM)\nDRDO Headquarter, Room No 447,\nDRDO Bhawan, Rajaji Marg\nNew Delhi – 110011\nPhone :\n011- 23007445, 011-23013209 & 011-23015291\nFax :\n011-23793008\nEmail :\ndiitm[dot]hqr[at]gov[dot]in"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/thermally-conducting-light-weight-nanocomposite-based-structures#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nThermally Conducting Light Weight Nanocomposite-Based Structures\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nElectrically insulating and thermally conducting nanocomposites have lower weight, higher viscoelasticity and better dimension stability in comparison to contemporary metal alloys being used for propulsion motor applications."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/thermally-conductive-nanofluid#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nThermally conductive nanofluid\nLabs\nDefence Materials and Stores Research and Development Establishment (DMSRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nThermally conductive nanofluid mitigates the excess heating concern of specific parts of automobiles, mechanical instruments, electronic & electrical device and also engineering process like grinding, material cutting, milling etc."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/through-wall-imaging-radar#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nThrough Wall Imaging Radar\nLabs\nElectronics & Radar Development Establishment (LRDE)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nThrough Wall Imaging Radar (TWIR) is a sensor used for detection and location of static and moving targets, especially human beings behind walls."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/time-division-multiplex-exchange-tidex#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nTime Division Multiplex Exchange (TIDEX)\nLabs\nCentre for Artificial Intelligence & Robotics (CAIR)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nTime Division Multiplex Exchange is an all digital exchange and serves as a mobile automatic telephone exchange, specially designed to work over Army Radio Engineered Network (AREN). It provides automatic switching for Subscriber, Grid Trunks and Universal Junction."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/torpedo-advanced-light-tal#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nTorpedo Advanced Light (TAL)\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nTorpedo Advanced Light  (TAL) is an electrically propelled self-homing torpedo and can be launched from ship and rotary wing aircraft. It has both active and passive modes of operations, and all digital control and guidance systems. TAL is an anti submarine weapon, which can attack submarines in shallow waters & deep waters.\nSalient Features\nHigh power seawater activated battery\nOperating Depth 450 m\nWeight (War head version) 220 kg"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/transfer-technologies#top", "content": "Transfer of Technology (ToT)\nDRDO Policy for Transfer of Technology 2025\nDownload PDF 4.6 MB\nCounter Covid 19 Technologies\nCategory A Technologies (Military Technologies)\nThese are the technologies for which Indian Armed Forces/ MHA/ other Govt. agencies (both central & state) are the only end users. Category ‘A’ technologies are military technologies and are referred to as “MILTECH”. Export of Cat ‘A’ technologies is subjected to approval process of DRDO and MoD, Govt of India. ToT to the industry is done directly by DRDO for all Category ‘A’ technologies.\nCategory A Technologies ready for ToT\nCategory-A Technologies ready for ToT to Indian Industies\n(*) Additional / Balance Licenses\nDRDO\nTechnology\nLAB\nNo of License Available\nDate of Publishing\nAir Retainable type Inflatable Aircraft Decoy technology (InfADec)\n86 KB\nDLJ\n03\n22/05/2025\nREMOCON\n177 KB\nINMAS\n04\n22/05/2025\nCartridge Electric Operating Fire Extinguisher (EOFE)\n250 KB\nARDE\n03\n09/05/2025\nManufacturing of shaped miniature Detonating Cord\n184 KB\nHEMRL\n03\n06/05/2025\nImprovised Explosive Device (IED) Containment Vessel\n169 KB\nR&DE (E)\n03*\n17/04/2025\nMounting and Support Equipment for Multi Spectral Camouflage Net (MSCN)\n3.5 MB\nDMSRDE\n06*\n08/04/2025\nG-Band Coupled Cavity Traveling-Wave Tube (G-Band CCTWT)\n210 KB\nMTRDC\n02\n26/03/2025\nCBRN Resuscitator (Manual)\n115 KB\nDEBEL\n06\n25/03/2025\nModular Bridging System\n82 KB\nR&DE(E)\n01\n25/03/2025\nPinaka Mark-I Rocket System\n75 KB\nARDE\n01\n20/03/2025\nPinaka Mark-II Rocket System\n75 KB\nARDE\n01\n20/03/2025\nFuel Cell based Hybrid Power Supply (FC-HPSS)\n156 KB\nR&DE (E)\n06\n12/03/2025\nClosed Vessel Test System\n86 KB\nHEMRL\n10\n12/03/2025\nPinaka Multi Barrel Launcher and Battery Command Post (BCP)\n74 KB\nARDE\n02\n21/02/2025\nManufacturing of 500kg Pre-fragmented (PF) Bomb\n95 KB\nARDE\n03\n21/02/2025\nMilitary Combat Parachute