{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/uav-payload#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nUAV Payload\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nThis system is a light weight, small size modular ELINT & COMINT System payloads for UAV platform. The system operates over wide range of frequencies with complete 360 degree of azimuth spatial coverage and it acts as force multiplier to build Electronic order of Battle (EOB) by providing accurate information about the hostile radar and communication systems. It can also carry out location fix using associated parameter information."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/uav#top", "content": "Technology Category\nTechnology Development Task\nLab\nDesign Configuration\nFixed wing Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV) for surveillance  and combat operations\nDYSL-AT\nWeaponisation of Drones\nDYSL-AT\nVTOL\nSpecialized Vertical Take Off & Landing (VTOL) Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs)\nDYSL-AT"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/ugv#top", "content": "Technology Category\nTechnology Development Task\nLab\nAI/ML Technology\nAI based Controls for Autonomous Driving\nVRDE\nAI based Navigation for Autonomous Driving\nVRDE\nAI Based Perception for Autonomous Driving\nVRDE\nData Set Generation for UGV application\nVRDE\nSimulation software for AI algorithms validation\nVRDE\nDeep Reinforcement Learning based Autonomous Driving\nVRDE\nAI based Simultaneous localization & Mapping (SLAM) for field/outdoor conditions\nVRDE\nDrive-by-Wire\nSmart Drive-by-Wire technology for Armoured Fighting Vehicles (AFVs)\nCVRDE\nSmart Drive-by-Wire Technology for Futuristic Unmanned Ground Vehicles (UGVs)\nCVRDE\nMSDF\nSimultaneous Localization and Mapping (SLAM) using multiple Sensors For UGVs\nCAIR\nNetwork Enabled\nCollaborative Unmanned Ground Vehicles (UGVs) and Smart UGVs\nCVRDE\nOff Road Mobility\nAssessment of remotely operated vehicle and Decision support system (DSS)\nDGRE\nSwarm Technology\nTroop level Swarm Unmanned Ground Vehicles (UGVs)\nCVRDE\nUnmanned Combat Vehicle\nPrototype Demonstration of Unmanned  Ground Combat Vehicle without Autoloader\nCVRDE\nUnmanned Ground Combat Vehicle (UGCV) Technologies\nCVRDE"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/ultra-high-strength-high-fracture-toughness-low-alloy-steel-dmr-1700#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nUltra High Strength, High Fracture Toughness Low-Alloy Steel DMR-1700\nLabs\nDefence Metallurgical Research Laboratory (DMRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nA new NiSiCrCoMo low alloy steel, called DMR-1700, with a total alloy content of about 7 wt. %is developed. Strength-toughness combination of DMR-1700 steel is better than reported values for low alloy steels 300 M and D6 AC and falls in the upper bound range for 18Ni (250) maraging steel that has a total alloying content in excess of 30 wt. %. With base steel as filler, near 100 per cent weld efficiency can be achieved in welded and heat treated conditions. The reproducibility of attractive strength and fracture toughness properties has been established in tonnage scale melts at MIDHANI. The applications include Booster Motor Casings and armour. The steel is under production at MIDHANI, Hyderabad.\nImages\n2 m Diameter Booster Motor Casing"},
