ed towards passive detection of ship/submarine\nNSTL\nSimulation Framework for Life Estimation for Mechanical Consumables & Electronic Components\nNSTL\nSimulator for analysis of CONOPs via performance metrics & Scheme for estimation of Kill-Probabilities for Underwater Weapons (delivered aerially or underwater / single shot & salvo)\nNSTL\nUnderwater Noise Simulation for use in target detection algorithm development\nNSTL\nTorpedo\nUnderwater docking system for retrieval of AUV to midget submarine/torpedo to submarine tube/ man-portable AUV to midget submarine or Combat XLAUV\nNSTL\nAll weather Precision Glide Add on kit for range enhancement of air launched lightweight torpedoes.\nNSTL\nBiomimitic structures for drag reduction & power optimization.\nNSTL\nMaterials\nSmart-Material based Surface Coating for AUV for avoidance of detection by traditional sonar\nNSTL\nSoC\nVery Low Power Open Architecture based SoC for AI/ML applications\nNSTL\nUnderwater Hybrid Vehicles\nConfiguration of a solar powered autonomous surface & underwater vehicle for covert ISR operations\nNSTL\nConfiguration of Long Life Modular Submarine Docking Station on Sea-Bed as Control Centre for AUV swarms\nNSTL\nUnderwater Mines\nConfiguration of Super-Cavitating Bullets for destroying mines deployed in shallow waters\nNSTL"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/upcoming-events#top", "content": "View Archive\nSearch for Event\nNo active record(s) available currently for this section."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/ushus#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nUSHUS\nLabs\nNaval Physical & Oceanographic Laboratory (NPOL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nUSHUS is a Submarine Sonar Suite designed for the EKM class of submarines. This is a compendium of multiple sensors for passive detection which collates different characteristics of the same target and provides target data through information fusion. The constituent sonars in the suite include passive sonar, active sonar, intercept sonar, obstacle avoidance sonar and underwater telephony."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/varuna#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nVARUNA\nLabs\nDefence Electronics Research Laboratory (DLRL)\nTechnology Cluster\nElectronics and Communication Systems (ECS)\nIt is a high performance, ship-borne Modern ESM system for interception, detection, classification and identification of conventional and modern complex radars. The system includes strategic & tactical ES requirements with 100% probability of interception. Eighteen VARUNA Systems have been delivered and are being exploited by Indian Navy since 2013."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/varunastra#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nVarunastra\nLabs\nNaval Science & Technological Laboratory (NSTL)\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nVarunastra is ship launched, heavy weight, electrically-propelled anti-submarine torpedo capable of targeting quiet submarines, both in deep and shallow waters in an intense countermeasures environment. Varunastra can be fired from all ASW ships capable of firing heavy weight torpedoes. VARUNASTRA has been inducted by Indian Navy in 2016.\nImages\nVARUNASTRA\nVARUNASTRA\nVarunastra"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/drdo/vibro-acoustic-rubber-tile#top", "content": "Back to Listing\nVibro-acoustic rubber tile\nTechnology Cluster\nNaval Systems and Materials (NS & M)\nSalient Features\nVibro-acoustic Rubber Tile has been developed which is used in submarines for sound and vibration damping on SONAR compartments."},
