{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/our-luminaries#top", "content": "DR DS Kothari\nSA to RM and DG DRDO\n(12.07.1948 – 18.03.1961)\nProf. S Bhagavantham\nSA to RM and DG DRDO\n(01.07.1961 – 13.10.1969)\nDr BD Nagchaudhuri\nSA to RM & DG DRDO\n(01.07.1970 – 01.07.1974)\nProf. MGK Menon\nSA to RM & DG DRDO\n[17.08.1974 – 10.07.1978]\nDr Raja Ramanna\nSA to RM & DG DRDO\n[10.07.1978 – 15.02.1982]\nDr VS Arunachalam\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[15.02.1982 – 10.07.1992]\nDr APJ Abdul Kalam\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[10.07.1992 – 29.12.1999]\nDr VK Aatre\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[29.12.1999 – 31.08.2004]\nShri M Natarajan\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[01.09.2004 – 31.08.2009]\nDr VK Saraswat\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[01.09.2009 – 31.05.2013]\nDr Avinash Chander\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[01.06.2013 – 31.01.2015]\nDr S Christopher\nChairman, DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[29.05.2015 – 28.05.2018]"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/prof-mgk-menon", "content": "Prof. MGK Menon\nSA to RM & DG DRDO\n[17.08.1974 – 10.07.1978]\nProf. M Govind Kumar Menon, an internationally known physicist, was Chairman, Electronics Commission and Director, Tata Institute of Fundamental Research (TIFR), Mumbai, before assuming the Office of SA to RM on 17 August 1974. He studied Advanced Physics at the University of Bristol and obtained the PhD degree in 1953. At Bristol, he worked with Nobel Laureate Professor CF Powell. Prof. Menon’s main contributions to the Organisation were two-fold. He gave thrust to projects where DRDO could contribute effectively and make a significant impact and actively encouraged and supported the strategic perspective on the new technology of missile warfare. Secondly, he made significant changes in the personnel policy of the DRDO and eliminated rigidity and inflexibility by which they were earlier characterised."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/prof-s-bhagavantham", "content": "Prof. S Bhagavantham\nSA to RM and DG DRDO\n(01.07.1961 – 13.10.1969)\nProf. Suri Bhagavantam was Director of the Indian Institute of Science, Bengaluru when he took over the stewardship of the Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO). He obtained his MSc degree under the direction of Prof. CV Raman. The DRDO at that time was a fledgling one with modest facilities and infrastructure. He soon realised that to provide tactical advantage, it was necessary to be technologically up-to-date and went about setting up laboratories. Prof. Bhagavantam steered the DRDO skilfully in the firm direction of applied research and development for meeting defence needs. He was the Head of the DRDO for about eight years. In this period, the organisation went through a process of growth and consolidation. By the time he retired from his post in October 1969, the organisation had made significant progress on many fronts."},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/running-contest-students#top", "content": "Dare to Dream 3.0"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/shri-m-natarajan", "content": "Shri M Natarajan\nSA to RM, DG DRDO & Secretary,\nDepartment of Defence R&D\n[01.09.2004 – 31.08.2009]\nShri M Natarajan worked over the years on several important programmes/assignments relating to the design and development of combat vehicles. He was associated with Arjun Main Battle Tank (MBT) programme since its inception and was appointed its Programme Director in 1987. The continued hard work and innovative design approach under his leadership resulted in India’s first indigenous state-of-the-art MBT. He also conceptualised the Self-Propelled Gun System (SPGS)-Bhima, Bridge Layer Tank (BLT)-Arjun, Combat Improved Ajeya and Tank-Ex."},
