{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area1#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n1\nDIA-CoE, IIT Delhi\n1. Advanced Ballistics and Protection Technologies (ABSSP)\n1. Light Weight Armour for Soldier.\n2. Armour for Vehicle Protection\n3. Advanced Modelling and Simulation Techniques\n4. Explosives Resistance Structure – Design and Simulation\n5. Modelling and Simulation for Long Range Artillery Guided Projectile for High ‘g’ Application.\n6. Light Weight Advanced Material for Ballistic Protection.\n7. Nanotechnology for Armour Material.\n2. Advanced Electromagnetic for Terahertz and Millimeter Wave Technologies (ETMWT)\n1. Source, Detector & Devices for THz Application.\n2. High Speed THz Communication.\n3. Spectroscopy.\n4. Imaging.\n5. Terrestrial Beam Forming Network\n6. MMW Devices\n7. RF MEMS and Subsystems\n8. MMW Communication\n9. Time Difference of Arrival (TDOA) based Geolocation\n10. Modulation Change Detection\n3. Brain Computer Interface and Brain Machine Intelligence (BCIAMI)\n1. Robotics Control\n2. Augmented Reality for Enhanced Human Communication\n3. Ambience Awareness\n4. Enhancing Inputs via Visual Mode\n5. Enhancing Inputs by Touch\n6.Brain to Brain Communication.\n4. Bio Mechanical Devices (BMD)\n1. Enhancement of Bipedal Capabilities\n2. Enhancement of Upper Body Strength\n5. Photonics Technologies and Specialty Optics for Laser Applications (PTSOLA)\n1. Sources and Detectors\n2. Custom Designed Fibres for QKD\n3. Nonlinear Photonic Devices\n4. Pump Laser Diodes\n5. Fiber Laser\n5. Spectral Beam Combining\n6. Precision Optics\n7. Speciality Coating for High Power Laser\n8. Test & Measurement\n6.Quantum Communication (QCOMM)\n1. Free Space Communication.\n2. Fibre based Communication\n3. Entanglement based QKD\n4. Hybrid QKD\n5. QKD Protocols & Electronic Implementation\n6. Robustness against Environmental Noise and Adversaries Action.\n7.High Speed Imaging and Devices (HSID)\n1. Thermal Imaging\n2. Shock Imaging\n3. Instrumentation for Critical tests\n8.Smart and Intelligent Textile Technologies (SITT)\n1. Coated and Laminated Textiles for Aerial Inflatables\n2. Electronics and Photonics Textile\n3. Protective Textiles\n4. Light Weight Textile for Thermal & Mechanical Protection\n5. Textile for Camouflage and Invisibility\n6. Variable Signature Textile using Metamaterials\n7. Sensing and Adaptation to the Environment\n8. Temperature Responsive Smart Insulation Textile for All Weather Protective Clothing\n9. Miniaturized System for Cooling Suits"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area10#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n10\nDIA-COE, IIT Hyderabad\n1.  Ultra- High Temperature Materials for Hypersonic Applications (UHTM)\n1. UHTCMC (Carbon Fibre - Ceramic Matrix Composites)\n2. SiC Fiber Indigenization\n3. Alumina Zirconia & SiC Fibre Composite for Structural Applications\n4. High Temperature Adhesive Materials\n5. High Temperature Coatings\n6. Liquid Precursor for Boron Nitride Matrix\n7. Stealth Material for High Temperature Applications\n8. EM window for Temperature from 16000C upto 25000C\n2. Artificial Intelligence for Missile and Missile Defence (AIMMD)\n1. AI for Performance Analysis, Verify Design and Operations of Missiles\n2. AI For Data Validation of Phase Check Data of Missile and Missile Defence Systems\n3. AI for Long Term Storage Health Monitoring\n4. AI for Automatic Design of Missiles\n5. Expert System for Inflight Mode Selection and Mission Management\n6. Expert System for Threat Assessment and Weapon Assignment (TAWA)\n7. High Entropy Expert Systems based TAWA (Maximising Unpredictability for Adversaries and Presenting Maximum Options Post Defence Action)\n3.  Space Systems for Defence (SSD)\n1. Self-Deploying and Unfolding Structures\n2. Power and Thermal Management Systems.\n3. Space Robotics Platform.\n4. Adoption of Technologies for Space Applications- Sensors, Radar, Optical, Communication, Electronic Warfare, Energy Storage, Mata-materials, Tracking Systems etc.\n5. Defence Mechanism for Satellites.\n6. Space Debris Modelling and its management\n4.  Adaptive Imaging and Image Processing (AIIP)\n1. AI/ML based Image Processing.\n2. Processing of Hyperspectral, Multispectral, SAR and Optical, Images for Complex Target Monitoring.\n3. On Board Generation of High Value and Small Volume Summery.\n5.  Nano-Ornithopter Technologies (NOTT)\n1. Material for Nano-Ornithopter Flapping Wing Configurations.\n2. Flight Control and Related Technologies for Nano-Ornithopter.\n3. Testing Methodologies\n4. Sensors and Payloads for Nano-Ornithopters.\n5. Swarm Applications for Nano-Ornithopters.\n6. System Integration and Mission Profile & System Definition Validation\n6.  Seeker and Homing Technologies (SHT)\n1. Novel Design and Fabrication of Active and Passive Seekers.\n2. Advanced Homing Technologies.\n3. AI/ML based Processing Devices & Algorithms Technologies for Seeker.\n4. Compressive Sensing based Wide Open Sub-Nyquist Frequency Estimation\n7.  Additive Manufacturing (AM)\n1. AM Process Optimization for Defence Components.\n2. Directed Energy Deposition and Powder Bed Fusion Equipment Design.\n3. Modelling & Simulation for Additive Manufacturing Processes.\n4. Structural Components Manufacturing by AM.\n5. AM for Single Use Components\n6. AM for Prolonged Use Components.\n7. Defence Standard for Additive Manufacturing Processes, Materials and Products.\n8. Wire Arc Additive Manufacturing for Large-Scale Parts\n9. Cold Spray Additive manufacturing\n10. Micro/Nano AM with smart materials\n11. Hybrid additive/subtractive machines\n12. Superscalable volumetric AM technologies\n13. Real Time Defect Monitoring and Process Control\n8.  Laser Beam Combining based Communication, Power Transmission and Manufacturing (LBC)\n1. Manufacturing Technologies using Lasers\n2. Spatial and Temporal Wave Front Control\n3. Laser based Wireless Charging\n4. Free Space Laser Communication\n5. Laser Beam Profile Optimization for AM\n6. Optical Phased Arrays\n7. Photonic Lanterns\n9. Extraction, Recycling and Sustainability of Materials (ERSM)\n1. Extraction of Metals from Ores\n2. Recovery of Materials from Process Scrap and End of Life Parts"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area11#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n11\nDIA-COE, IIT BHU\n1.  Powder Metallurgy (PM)\n1. Indigenous Design and Development of IGA/PREP or Other Powder Production Equipment\n2. Additive Manufacturing (AM) Grade Powders\n3. Computational Modelling & Simulation for AM materials\n4. Numerical Studies / Investigation of Material Properties of Metals & Alloys Developed through AM\n2. Ceramics (CER)\n1. Functionally Graded Material / Composites, Ceramics, Glass Ceramic Composites and Synthesis of Ceramic Powders\n2. Process, Fabrication and Characterization of Ceramics\n3. Functional Materials (FMAT)\n1. High Thermal Conductivity Lossy Materials\n2. RF Filters / Phase Shifters For MW\n3. High Purity SiC Material\n4. Polymer based High Temperature Adhesives\n5. Lower Corrosive, Lower Weight & Higher Damping Materials for Electronics/ Structural Applications\n6. Endothermic Fuels\n7. Organic-Inorganic Hybrid Functional Polymers\n8. High Performance Fibers (Aramid. Carbon and High Mol. Wt. PE)\n9. Hollow Fiber Member for Inert Gas Generation\n4. High Power Micro Wave Sources and Devices (HPMW)\n1. Components for High Power Microwaves\n2. THz Gyrotron, Gyro-Klystron Amplifier, EIK, and Folded Waveguided TWT Amplifiers\n3. Single Frequency PRF Device, High Voltage Compact Pulse Power Supply"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area12#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n12\nDIA-COE, IIT Jodhpur\n1.  Applications of Advanced Technologies for Desert Warfare (ATDW)\n1. Polymer and Prefab based Rapid Construction Technology for Desert Terrain\n2. Desert Solider: Thermal and Hydration Management\n3. Imagery Intelligence for Desert Terrain.\n4. Exploitation of Flexible Solar Cells and Electronics for Desert Terrain\n5. Unconventional Energy Harvesting in Desert\n6. Real Time Environment Change Monitoring for Combat Effectiveness\n7. PCM based Cooling Technology\n8. Terrain Simulation and Terrain Modelling for Navigation, Concealing and Traversal\n2. Futuristic Omni Mobility Drones (OMD)\n1. Air-Land, Land-Water Amphibious Drones\n2. Difficult Terrain Mobility (Hard Ground, Soft Sand and Rocky)\n3. Drones for High Altitude Mountain Areas\n3.  AI For Information Warfare and War Gaming Technologies (AIWG)\n1. Design and Assessment of Collaborative Agents\n2. Wargaming With UAV Swarm\n3. Decision Support Techniques for War Games\n4. Automatic Iterative Adversarial Model Improvement in War Gaming\n5. Modelling of Non-Contact Warfare and its Impact on Contact Warfare\n6. Non-Text Man-Machine Interface for War Gaming\n7. Post-Game Data Analysis for Doctrine and Player Assessment"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area13#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n13\nDIA-COE, IIT Kanpur\n1.  Flexible Electronics and Substrates (FES)\nMulti Element Sensors\nUltra-Thin Flexible Electronics and Substrates\nConductive Transparent Coating\nPackaging of Flexible Electronics\nApplications of Flexible Electronics\nStealth and Camouflage\nFlexible Antenna\nEnergy Harvesting\nSensors for Health Monitoring of Materials and Structures\n2.  Sensing, Stealth and Surface Protection Using Nano Materials and Meta Materials (SSSP)\nSensors / Diagnostic Using Nano Materials\nMulti-Spectral Stealth and Cloaking\nCoating for Marine Applications\nHigh Entropy Materials, Meta-materials, & Nano-composites for Enhanced Damage Tolerance\nCoating for Frigid / Extreme Environment\nProduction, Process Optimization for Nano & Meta Materials for Scalability\nSurface Finish Techniques including use of Additive Manufacturing.\n3.  Accelerated Material Design and Development (AMDD)\nICME based Accelerated Materials & Products Development\nAdvanced Metal & Super-alloys\nNG Naval Steel\nHigh Performance Structural Materials\nDesign & Synthesis of Property Specific Material Exploiting Computational Chemistry, Material Modelling and Fluid Thermodynamics\nAI/ ML for Material Design\n4.  High Energy Systems (HES)\nProduction and Scalability of Additives\nLife Prediction of Energetic and related Materials\nModelling and Simulation for Material and Geometry\nModels and Validation of the Chemical Structure of Warheads\nDevelopment and Characterization of Reactive Material for warheads and Theoretical Performance Prediction.\nGreen Synthesis of Energetic Materials\nBio-synthesis and Disposal of Energetic Materials\nInternal Ballistics\n5.  Bio- Engineering and CBRNE Applications (CBRNE)\nTissue Regeneration for Defence Related Injuries\nAssistive Devices for War-fighting\nWearable Sensors, Diagnostic & Analytics for CBRNE\nMultichannel Sensor Instrumentation for Detection of CBRNE Threats\nCBRNE Sensor Technology\nCBRNE Shelter Technology\nTechnology For Triage CBRNE Affected Casualties\nArtificial Oxygen Transport\nUniversal Decontamination Formulation\nAI based Actuated Prosthesis\n6.  Software Defined Radio and Military Communication Technologies (SDRMC)\nWaveform Design\nWireless Systems and Networks\nSpread Spectrum Analysis\nWaveforms for Cognitive Radios\nAntennas for Military Applications\nMW Passive and Active Circuits\nEfficient Hardware Architecture for SDR\nInteroperability related Standards\nRobust and high intercapacity waveform design"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area14#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n14\nDIA-COE, IIT Roorkee\n1.   Smart Infrastructure and Hardened Structures for Defence Applications (SIHS)\n1. Structures for Extreme Terrain, High Altitude, Hilly Regions and Arid Regions\n2. Materials for Extreme Environment\n3. Shock Proof Structures\n4. Thermal Management of Civil Infrastructure\n5. Semi Buried, Light Weight, Modular, Transportable, Storage Facility for Explosives.\n6. Centrifuge Facility for High Energy Explosive Blast.\n7. Bio Inspired Panels for Projectile and Blast Wave Protection.\n8. Material for Replicating Behavior of Auxetic Structures for Stopping Shrapnels Generated by Blast Wave.\n2.  Energy Storage Device (ESD)\n1. Li-Ion Batteries and BMS\n2. Novel Battery Technologies\n3. Hydrogen based Energy Systems\n4. Fuel Cells\n5. New Electrode and Electrolytes Materials for Super Capacitors, Na+, Al, Mg Ion Batteries.\n6. Nuclear Batteries for Robotics Application.\n7. Chip Ultra Capacitors for Wearable Applications.\n8. Anion Exchange Membrane Electrolyser for Hydrogen Generation.\n9. Flow Batteries for Air Independent Propulsion.\n10. Thermal, Mechanical and Electrical Energy Storage\n3.  Landslide, Snow and Avalanche Studies (LSAS)\n1. Advanced Avalanche Prediction & Mitigation Strategies\n2. Strategies for Mitigation of Landslides\n3. Tornado, Flood and Draught Management Using Microwave & Ultrasonic Technology\n4. Landslide Early Warning\n5. Strengthening of Foundation and Pavements in Perma Frost Region.\n6. Anti-Icing Solutions\n7. Equation of State Determination for Concrete and Soil\n4.  Laser Technology for Ranging and Detection (LTRD)\n1. Laser Range Finder, LIDAR\n2. SoC Development\n3. Laser Communication\n5.  Shock and Detonics (SD)\n1. Microstructure Informed Chemo-Mechano-Thermal Modelling based Predictive Assessment of Shock-Sensitivity\n2. Materials Design for Blast Mitigation\n3. Experimental and Computational Study of Chemical Kinetics and Combustion Phenomenon of Metal/Metal Oxide in Air Blasts\n4. Sensor Platform and Data Acquisition Systems for Landmine and Explosive Detection.\n6.  Thermal Management (TM)\n1 . Evaluate Film Cooling Performance\n2. Cooling Mechanisms for Cylindrical and Hole Geometries, Surface of Blades and Other Fast-Moving Structures.\n3. Cooling Solutions for High Power Electronics Chips Through Mounting and Packaging\n7.  Emerging RF Technologies for Application in Defence Communications (RFT)\n1. RF Power Amplifiers and Their Combining Techniques\n2. Signal Processing & Baseband Techniques for Radio Frequency Front-End Design and Performance Enhancement.\n3. Multi-Functional Radio-Frequency Front-End Components and Subsystem Design.\n4. New Generation Radio Frequency Integrated Circuits.\n5. Advanced RF Antenna System\n8. Advanced Electro Optic Technologies (EOT)\n1. EO Technologies For Ground based Space Situational Awareness\n2. Optronic Sensor Shield Next Generation EO Sensors\n3. Artificial Intelligence (AI) Technologies for EO Systems\n4. Camera for Wide-Area Day and Night Surveillance System\n5. Next Generation Laser Designation POD 3D Laser Imaging System\n6. High Resolution Imaging Payloads\n7. Technologies with Identification Capability"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area15#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n15\nDIA-COE, IIT Kharagpur\n1. Advanced Extractive Metallurgy and Metal Recycling Technologies (AEMMRT)\n1. Processes For Extracting/ Recovering Strategic Metals like Tungsten, Germanium, Gallium, Rare Earth Elements, Lithium, Nickel and Cobalt from Primary Ores and Secondary Waste Streams.\n2. Sustainable and Green Extractive Metallurgy\n3. Advanced Metal Refining and Purification\n4. Nanomaterials for Extractive Metallurgy\n2. Advanced Surface Engineering Technologies (ASST)\n1. Surface Coatings and Surface Modification Technologies.\n2. Testing and Performance Evaluation of Surface Coatings.\n3. Tribology and Surface Interaction\n4. Green Coatings and Surface Treatments\n5. Smart Surfaces and Intelligent Coatings\n6. Nano Coatings for Defence Platforms used in Harsh Environment\n3.  Unmanned Underwater Robotic Sensors and Actuators (UURSA)\n1. Autonomous and Unmanned Underwater Vehicles (AUVs and UUVs)\n2. Underwater Navigation and Localization\n3. Underwater Communication Systems\n4. Energy Storage and Power Systems for Long-Duration Missions\n5. Swarm Robotics and Collaborative Behaviour\n6. Underwater Sensing and Perception Technologies\n7. Hybrid and Biomimetic Underwater Robots\n8. Underwater Robotics for Anti-Submarine Warfare (ASW)\n4.  Cognitive Technologies and Cyber Physical Defence Systems (CTCPDS)\n1. Cognitive Computing using Neuromorphic Engineering\n2. Autonomous Systems and Cognitive Agents\n3. Cognitive Security and Cyber Defence\n4. Cognitive Robotics\n5. Secure Embedded Systems and IoT Security\n6. Resilient Cyber-Physical Systems (CPS) Architecture\n7. AI and Machine Learning (ML) for Cyber-Physical Security\n8. Quantum-Resistant Asymmetric Cryptography\n5.  Quality, Reliability and Safety Studies (QRSS)\n1. Quality Control and Assurance in Defence Manufacturing\n2. Safety Engineering and Hazard Analysis\n3. Environmental and Stress Testing\n4. Lifecycle Quality and Reliability Management\n5. Software Reliability\n6. Cyber System Robustness\n7. System Safety Certification and Standards Compliance\n8. Integrated Safety and Reliability Assessment\n9. Reliability-Centred Maintenance (RCM)\n6. Cryptography & Information Security (CIS)\n1. Symmetric Key Analysis\n2. Side Channel Analysis\n3. Blockchain Security\n4. Cryptology and Fault Attacks\n5. Hardware Security\n6. Post Quantum Cryptography"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area2#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n2.\nDIA-CoE, IIT Bombay\n1. Aero Engines: Small Turbo Fan Engine & Large Aero Engine (AE)\n1. Combustor Design and Combustor Component Technologies\n2. Rotor Design and Optimization\n3. Simulation and Design using Large Data\n4. Liners & Insulators Interaction\n5. Air Breathing Engine for Sub Mach 3\n6. Advanced Technologies for Fan and Compressor\n7. AI/ML based Engine Health Monitoring Technologies\n8. Digital Twin\n2. Solid Propulsion Technologies (SPT)\n1. Combustion Modelling - Simulation with Experimental Validation.\n2. Burn Rate Augmentation and Control\n3. Novel Solid Propellant Formulation.\n4. Next Generation Propulsion System for Novel Propellants.\n5. Niche Technologies for Advanced Turbo Machinery\n3. Advanced Aircraft Structures (AAS)\n1. Advanced Aerofoil Design & Experimental Validation\n2. Wing Integrated Intake Design and Flow Control\n3. Mini Actuators for Morphing\n4. Novel Controller Design for Morphing\n5. Variable Configuration Design\n6. Reconfigurable Aero Structures\n7. Aircraft engine and subsystems technologies\n4. Hypersonic Propulsion (HYP)\n1. SCRAMJET Engine Modelling, Simulation and Experimental Validation\n2. Long Duration Hypersonic Propulsion Technology\n3. Shock Boundaries Layer Interaction\n4. Supersonic Combustion and Stability\n5. Endothermic Fuels\n6. Creation and Measurement of Hypersonic Flow Field\n5. Advanced Conventional Manufacturing Technology for Aero Engine Applications (ACMT)\n1. Abrasive Flow Machining of Ti-64 Aerofoil Blades\n2. Inductive High Frequency Pressure Welding (IHFPW) Machine to Repair Blisks\n3. Diffusion Bonding of Titanium Airfoil Struts\n4. Hydro Forming of Gas Turbine Parts\n5. Rotary Friction Welding\n6. Electron Beam Melting Additive Manufacturing\n7. Laser Drilling of Shaped Holes\n6.  Advanced Propulsion Technologies for Defence Applications (APT)\n1. Optimizing Energy and Entropy\n2. Hybrid Propulsion\n3. Electrical Propulsion\n4. Hydrogen Propulsion\n5. Nuclear Propulsion\n7.  Compound Semiconductor Technologies (CSCT)\n1. High Frequency Electronics, Opto-electronics, Emitters and Detectors, Quantum Applications.\n2. Material Design, Deposition and Characterization\n3. Device design, fabrication, characterization, modelling, packaging, qualification and reliability testing.\n4. ROIC Design"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area3#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n3\nDIA-RCoE, IIT Madras\n1.  Power Electronics and its Thermal Management (PETM)\n1. Material and Devices for High Power Applications\n2. Thermal Management of Power Electronic Components\n3. Robust Electronics Implementation for Mission Critical Applications\n2. Hydro-Dynamics, Control and Acoustics (HDCA)\n1. Low Noise Propulsion System\n2. Super Cavitating Torpedo\n3. Application Specific Unconventional Hull Structure\n4. Adaption of Advanced Technologies for Naval System Integration\n5. Structural Health Monitoring for Naval Systems\n6. Design of Lightweight Auxiliary Launching Craft (Air, Surface and Underwater)\n7. Fire Control System for Naval Platforms\n8. Underwater ISR and Communication\n9. Sonar Technologies\n10. Technologies for Naval Weapons and Countermeasures\n11. AL/ML based Technologies for Underwater Systems\n12. Naval Stealth Technologies.\n13. Non Acoustic Method of U/W Detection and Communication Technologies.\n14. Ship without Wakes\n15. Stable Naval Platform for Precision Firing\n16. Acoustically Silent Vessels\n3. Advanced Combat Vehicle Technologies (ACVT)\n1. Subsystem Level Research and Design of Combat Vehicles\n2. Simulation, Modelling and Digital Twin Technologies for Combat Vehicles\n3. Heavy Engine Technologies (>500 HP)\n4. Novel Integration Components & Technologies in Combat Vehicles\n5. Battle field situational awareness technology.\n6. Passive and Active based IFF (identification of friend or foe)\n4. High Power CW Laser Technology (> 10kW) (HPLT)\n1. Coherent Beam Combining\n2. Narrow Line Width Fiber Laser Sources\n3. Low Divergence Beam Formation and Maintenance\n4. Packaging of Laser Components & Integration\n5. Laser Matter Interaction\n5. Advanced Rare Earth Materials (AREM)\n1. Rare Earth Extraction from Indian Mineral Resources\n2. Magnetic Material for Defence Application\n3. Materials for Advanced Naval Sensors\n4. Materials for High Energy Densities Batteries\n5. Rare Earth Material based Fuel Cell Technology\n6. Materials for IR & MW Signature Control\n7. Recovery of Rare Earth Elements"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area4#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n4\nDIA-CoE, University of Hyderabad\n1. High Energy Materials (HEM)\n1 Computation Modelling of High Energy Molecules\n2 Novel Material Synthesis and Characterization\n3 Insensitive Munitions.\n4 High Explosive Pyro Techniques\n5 Performance Enhancement Additive Materials\n6 Energetic Polymers/Binders & Nano Materials for High Energy Applications.\n7 Nanothermites\n2. Technologies for Handling Explosives (THEX)\n1 Low Power, Low Frequency THz Applications.\n2 Near Field THz based Explosive Detection Technologies.\n3 Laser based Explosive Detection\n4 Spectroscopic Database of HEMs.\n5 Laser based Detonation\n6 HE Reaction Kinetics\n7 Pulsed Laser based Shock Waves and Detonation: Measurement Systems via Imaging\n3.  High Power Pulsed Laser Technology: Nano Second, Pico Second and Femto Second (HPPLT)\n1 High Power Pulsed Laser Prototypes (kW to TW range)\n2 Pulsed Laser Matter Interaction Studies (ns, ps & fs)"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area5#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n5\nDIA-SVPCOE,\n1.  Application Vulnerability Analysis (AVA)\n1 Application & Firmware Vulnerability and Testing and Management.\nGujrat University\n2 System/IOC/TTP Characterization and Penetration Testing Advancements\n2.  IoT Security (IoTS)\n1 Development and Security Assessment of IoT Devices & Components\n2 System Characterization and System Hardening for IOT Devices\n3.  Malware Analysis (MA)\n1 Development of Static and Dynamic Malware Analysis Techniques\n2 Analysis and Prediction of Malware Trends\n3 AI based Malware Response\n4.  Blockchain and Web Forensics (BWF)\n1 Crypto Payment Transaction Analysis\n2 Dark Web Characterization and Exploration\n3 Investigative Grade Fusion of Knowledge and Insight Extraction.\n5.  Big Data Analytics (BDA)\n1 Investigate Grade Fusion of Knowledge and Insight Extraction\n2 Disruptive AI Models including Generative AI for Big Data Analytics"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area6#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n6\nDIA-RCoE, IISc Bengaluru\n1. Aerospace Systems Design and Characterization (ASDC)\n1 Aerodynamic Design, Shape Optimization and Evaluation\n2 Wind Tunnel Model Design & Testing\n3 Mission Design and System Engineering\n4 Aero-Elastic, Aero-Thermo Elastics, Aero-Servo Elastic, Aero-Acoustic Studies\n5 Smart Structures, Vibration Controls.\n6 Integrated Vehicle Health Management\n7 Multi-Disciplinary Optimization, Digital Twin for aerospace systems.\n8 Radomes, Pods, Thermal Management, Hydraulic, and Electro-Mechanical Systems.\n2. Aerospace Structural Materials (ASM)\n1 Advanced Composite Design, Manufacturing, Testing\n2 Damage, Fracture, Ablation, Erosion and Failure modeling\n3 Thermal and Thermo-Mechanical, Electromagnetic and Environmental Performance Analysis of Composite Materials\n4 Multifunctional Structural Materials for Aerospace Vehicle Components for Applications in Radomes, Pods, Thermal Management, Hydraulic, Electro-Mechanical Systems\n3.  Advanced Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (AUAV)\n1 UAV Propulsion Technology\n2 UAV autonomous robotic tasks and configuration design\n3 Aerodynamic Test and Evaluation\n4 Path planning, control, navigation & guidance algorithm studies\n5 Mission Profile based System Engineering\n6 Scenario Simulation Design\n4.  High Temperature Materials for Aero Engines (HTM)\n1 High Temperature Alloys, Composites & Coatings and Thermo-Mechanical & Environmental Characterisation\n2 Integrated Computational Materials Modelling\n3 Thermo-Mechanical Fatigue and Creep Testing for in Service Life Assessment of Components.\n4 Predictive Capability for Processing-Structure-Property Linkage at Multiple Length Scales.\n5.  Lifing and Remaining Life Assessment of Materials (LRLAM)\n1 Establishing Lifing Methodologies and Models\n2 Materials Degradation Modeling\n3 Rejuvenation of materials, Repair and Refurbishment\n6.  Micro and Nano Systems Science and Technology (MNSST)\n1 MEMS / NEMS Sensors and Actuators for Navigation and Control\n2 Photovoltaic Devices and Sensors\n3 Silicon Photonics Systems and Related Technologies.\n4 Modelling and Simulation of Nano-Engineering\n5 Materials for Solar Cells\n6 Solar Cells for Space Applications.\n7 Heterogenous integration and advanced packaging of Sensors.\n8 Microfluidics\n9 CO2/O2 Management in Closed / Confined Environment\n7.  Artificial Intelligence and Autonomous Systems (AIAS)\n1 Sensor Processing for Autonomous Systems\n2 Active Sensing\n3 Navigation for Autonomous Systems\n4 Classical Control based Autonomous Systems\n5 Reinforcement Learning based Control\n6 Sensor Data Processing for Autonomous Systems\n7 Mission Planning for Autonomous Systems\n8 Neuromorphic Computing\n9 Extraction of Knowledge from Heterogeneous Sources like Structured, Unstructured and Contextual Data.\n10 Data Analytics and Visualization at High Velocity and Volume.\n11 Believable AI\n12 Active learning in Field\n13 Light Weight AI\n8.  Quantum Phenomena and Device Technology (QT)\n1 Quantum Sensing, Metrology and Devices\n2 Quantum Materials\n3 Quantum Simulations\n4 Quantum Radar & Imaging\n5 Quantum Computation, Simulation and Algorithm\n6 QRNG Applications\n9. Strategic Technology Studies (STS)\n1 Multilateral Regimes Impacting Technology\n2 Technology Forecasting and Roadmaps Generation\n3 Current and Future Market Assessment of Future Defence Technology\n4 Defence Technology Policies\n5 Technology Management Framework and Analysis"},
{"url": "https://www.drdo.gov.in/thrust-area7#top", "content": "S. No.\nCentre Name\nResearch Verticals\nThrust Areas\n7.\nDIA-CoE, Mizoram University\n1. Agro-Bio Resources for Soldier Survival (ABRSS)\n1. Exploration & Geo Mapping of Agro Bio Resources in Remote Areas for Survival\nMedical\nNutritional\n2. Preservation & Processing Technology for Medicinal & Nutritional Resources.\n3. Extraction of Active Ingredient for Medicinal Remedies.\n2. Defence Waste Management (DWM)\n1 Human Waste Management for Minimising Habitation Footprint\n2 Recycling / Disposal of Human Waste Materials\n3 Bio-Digesters Effluent Management\n4 Bio Remediation / Chemical Treatment of Defence Waste\n3. Harnessing Environment for Soldier Survival (HESS)\n1 Water Sourcing – Identification and Purification\n2 Energy Harvesting Techniques\n3 Power and Energy from Natural Sources\n4 Shelter from Natural Sources\n5 Camouflage for Protection\n4. Human Cognition Studies under Extreme Environmental and Combat Stress (HCS)\n1 Cultural Markers of Local Demographic Variation for Defence & Security.\n2 Technologies for Enhancing Human to Human Communication for Defence Operations.\n3 Asymmetric Technologies for Crowd Management.\n4 Soldier Training Modules for Local Soft Skills.\n5 Psychological Impacts of Isolation and Challenging Conditions."},
